dTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Inserting and removing a QSFP+ transceiver may result in the forwarding plane agent restart and a brief traffic outage to occur. A workaround is to configure a forced speed on the corresponding interface via CLI before inserting/removing a transceiver.\nChanging interface speed interface configuration via CLI may require user confirmation to continue. Upon user confirmation, the forwarding plane agent restarts and a brief traffic outage occurs.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7050TX3-48C8'}]]}, {'bugId': 388309, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'nat and baremetal profiles support at most 1024 ip|ipv6 access-group <aclName> in ACL bindings, and 1024 ip|ipv6 access-group <aclName> out ACL bindings. If a limit is exceeded, the forwarding agents continuously restart.', 'alertNote': "nat and baremetal profiles support at most 1024 'ip|ipv6 access-group <aclName> in' ACL bindings, and 1024 'ip|ipv6 access-group <aclName> out' ACL bindings.  If a limit is exceeded, the forwarding agents continuously restart. ip and ipv6 access-groups in the same direction apply against the same limit.  For example, 11 'ip access-group <aclName1> in' and 1014 'ipv6 access-group <aclName2> in' would count as 1025 bindings for the 'in' direction.  'in' and 'out' have separate limits.\nTo stop the continuous forwarding agent restarts, revert the configuration to avoid exceeding a limit.\n\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.5', '4.22.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.21.10', '4.22.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1740528000, 'releaseNote': "nat and baremetal profiles support at most 1024 'ip|ipv6 access-group <aclName> in' ACL bindings, and 1024 'ip|ipv6 access-group <aclName> out' ACL bindings.  If a limit is exceeded, the forwarding agents continuously restart. ip and ipv6 access-groups in the same direction apply against the same limit.  For example, 11 'ip access-group <aclName1> in' and 10