s the DRAM, we switch to using OCB. In OCB mode due to excessive copp queues even small amounts of traffic gets dropped. Thus disabling dramRecovery via "no platform sand enqueue performance-monitor " helps.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.20.5'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.2'], 'bites': 9, 'lastBiteTime': 1684388113, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'When the congested traffic exceeds the DRAM, we switch to using OCB. In OCB mode due to excessive copp queues even small amounts of traffic gets dropped. Thus disabling dramRecovery via "no platform sand enqueue performance-monitor " helps.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Jericho'}]]}, {'bugId': 486938, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Bridged packets that hit a mac entry pointing to the ingress interface are dropped as dropVoqInNoForwardAction instead of dropVoqInSourcePortFilter. This results in these packets getting incorrectly labeled as an Adverse drop', 'alertNote': 'Bridged packets that hit a mac entry pointing to the ingress interface are dropped as dropVoqInNoForwardAction instead of dropVoqInSourcePortFilter. This results in these packets getting incorrectly labeled as an Adverse drop.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.9', '4.23.7', '4.24.3', '4.25.0'], 'bites': 9, 'lastBiteTime': 1682376494, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Bridged packets that hit a mac entry pointing to the ingress interface are dropped as dropVoqInNoForwardAction instead of dropVoqInSourcePortFilter. This results in these packets getting incorrectly labeled as an Adverse drop.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Jericho2'}]]}, {'bugId': 487198, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "In an EVPN MPLS configuration, broadcast ARP requests may not be forwarded when the TCAM profile doesn't have the feature 'evpn mpls irb'. The workaround is to add the feature 'evpn mpls irb' to the TCAM profile.", 'alertNot