ing the speed, the spanning-tree cost of that interface will be set to 2,000 and will not be updated once the port speed is negotiated.\n\nWorkaround is to configure the interface spanning-tree cost or to bring the interface down and back up again.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'stpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 541460, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Fixed an issue where on disabling dualstack, APs were not able to form VxLAN tunnel.', 'alertNote': 'Fixed an issue where on disabling dualstack, APs were not able to form VxLAN tunnel.', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['mwm-v1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['mwm-v9.0.1-14-vv1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1761696000, 'releaseNote': 'Fixed an issue where on disabling dualstack, APs were not able to form VxLAN tunnel.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Wifi11AXAP'}]]}, {'bugId': 541643, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'CloudEOS on Azure platform can sometimes crash and take more time to boot when multiple Accelerated NICs are present', 'alertNote': 'CloudEOS  on Azure platform can sometime crash and take more time to boot\x1bwhen multiple Accelerated NICs are present', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.0.1FX'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.4', '4.25.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'CloudEOS  on Azure platform can sometime crash and take more time to boot\x1bwhen multiple Accelerated NICs are present', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CloudEOS'}]]}, {'bugId': 541667, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'SWhen multiple TACACS+ server are configured, and fallback as happened, its possible for a certain user to use different servers for authentication and authorization. Some servers  may reject authorization requests if the user is unknown to them', 'alertNote': "Syslog ROUTING-3-FEC_RESOURCE_FULL may be logged while resources are not full, if an MPLS route with an action to swap to multiple labels (some of which may be pushed by MPLS tunnels resolving the MPLS route) is to be installed to the forwarding chip. This may not occur in all occurrences of MPLS routes resolved over MPLS tunnels. The relevant MPLS route will fail to be programmed. Workarounds may vary from taking no action if transient, configuring 'fec sharing igp tunnel disabled' if applicable, to changing the MPLS route resolution.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1599723339, 'exportedTime': 1675814400, 'releaseNote': "Syslog ROUTING-3-FEC_RESOURCE_FULL may be logged while resources are not full, if an MPLS route with an action to swap to multiple labels (some of which may be pushed by MPLS tunnels resolving the MPLS route) is to be installed to the forwarding chip. This may not occur in all occurrences of MPLS routes resolved over MPLS tunnels. The relevant MPLS route will fail to be programmed. Workarounds may vary from taking no action if transient, configuring 'fec sharing igp tunnel disabled' if applicable, to changing the MPLS route resolution.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'TACACSenabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 542196, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Packets forwarded by MPLS swap routes that are optimized as forward routes may get corrupted.', 'alertNote': 'Packets forwarded by MPLS swap routes that are optimized as forward routes may get corrupted.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.9', '4.23.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Packets forwarded by MPLS swap routes that are optimized as forward routes may get corrupted.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Jericho2'}, {'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 542197, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Disabling of egress RACL sharing ("no hardware access-list resource sharing vlan ipv4 out") is not supported with MPLS swap routes that are optimized as forward routes.', 'alertNote': 'Disabling of egress RACL sharing ("no hardware access-list resource sharing\nvlan ipv4 out") is not supported with MPLS swap routes that are optimized as\nforward routes. The workaround is to re-enable egress RACL sharing, which is\nthe default option.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.23.7', '4.24.4', '4.25.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Disabling of egress RACL sharing ("no hardware access-list resource sharing\nvlan ipv4 out") is not supported with MPLS swap routes that are optimized as\nforward routes. The workaround is to re-enable egress RACL sharing, which is\nthe default option.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Jericho2'}, {'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 542757, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When disabling MPLS on an interface in the non-default VRF, it may cause software forwarding or control plane generated IP packets for routes which point to tunnels, nexthop-groups or when routing from one IP address-family to another (RFC 5549) to route ', 'alertNote': 'When disabling MPLS on an interface in the non-default VRF, it may cause software forwarding or\ncontrol plane generated IP packets for routes which point to tunnels, nexthop-groups or when\nrouting from one IP address-family to another (RFC 5549) to route the packet incorrectly.\nThis will only affect packets in the default VRF.  These packets may end up being routed in\nthe non-default VRF.\n\nConfigure an SVI with no autostate configured in the default VRF to work around this issue.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.3'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.10', '4.23.7', '4.24.4', '4.25.3', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1604636859, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'When disabling MPLS on an interface in the non-default VRF, it may cause software forwarding or\ncontrol plane generated IP packets for routes which point to tunnels, nexthop-groups or when\nrouting from one IP address-family to another (RFC 5549) to route the packet incorrectly.\nThis will only affect packets in the default VRF.  These packets may end up being routed in\nthe non-default VRF.\n\nConfigure an SVI with no autostate configured in the default VRF to work around this issue.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}, {'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 542977, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The "clear counters" CLI command incorrectly clears the L2 and L3 subinterface SNMP counters.', 'alertNote': 'The "clear counters" CLI command incorrectly clears the L2 and L3 subinterface SNMP counters.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.23.9', '4.24.7', '4.25.5', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1605778675, 'exportedTime': 1703116800, 'releaseNote': 'The "clear counters" CLI command incorrectly clears the L2 and L3 subinterface SNMP counters.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SNMPenabled'}, {'tag': 'subintEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 543010, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "The CLI command \\'neighbor <ADDR> prefix-list <NAME> <in|out>\\' fails in IPv4/IPv6 multicast address-family. The workaround is to configure a route-map with command \\'neighbor <ADDR> route-map <NAME> <in|out>\\'in IPv4/IPv6 multicast address-family config.", 'alertNote': "The CLI command 'neighbor <ADDR> prefix-list <NAME> <in|out>' fails in IPv4 and IPv6 multicast address-family.\n\nTo workaround this issue, route maps containing prefix-lists may be configured on the neighbor within the relavant address family multicast configuration.\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1650933708, 'exportedTime': 1731888000, 'releaseNote': "The CLI command 'neighbor <ADDR> prefix-list <NAME> <in|out>' fails in IPv4 and IPv6 multicast address-family.\n\nTo workaround this issue, route maps containing prefix-lists may be configured on the neighbor within the relavant address family multicast configuration.\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'BGPIpv4MulticastEnabled'}, {'tag': 'BGPIpv6MulticastEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 543453, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The SandPtp agent may restart once unexpectedly when linecard firmware is upgraded.', 'alertNote': 'The SandPtp agent may restart once unexpectedly when linecard firmware is upgraded.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.6', '4.26.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1636058611, 'exportedTime': 1701129600, 'releaseNote': 'The SandPtp agent may restart once unexpectedly when linecard firmware is upgraded.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7500R'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7800'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7800R3'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280R3'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7500R3'}]]}, {'bugId': 543494, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': 'CVE-2020-26116', 'alertSummary': 'CVE-2020-26116: EOS is not affected by this CVE, however custom agents using the python3 runtime can be vulnerable.', 'alertNote': 'EOS is not vulnerable to CVE-2020-26116. However, custom agents using the python3 runtime can be vulnerable. http.client in Python 3.x before 3.5.10, 3.6.x before 3.6.12, 3.7.x before 3.7.9, and 3.8.x before 3.8.5 allows CRLF injection if the attacker controls the HTTP request method, as demonstrated by inserting CR and LF control characters in the first argument of HTTPConnection.request. The fix for this CVE-2020-26116 prevents header injection in http methods.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.23.10', '4.24.4', '4.25.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'EOS is not vulnerable to CVE-2020-26116. However, custom agents using the python3 runtime can be vulnerable. http.client in Python 3.x before 3.5.10, 3.6.x before 3.6.12, 3.7.x before 3.7.9, and 3.8.x before 3.8.5 allows CRLF injection if the attacker controls the HTTP request method, as demonstrated by inserting CR and LF control characters in the first argument of HTTPConnection.request. The fix for this CVE-2020-26116 prevents header injection in http methods.'}, {'bugId': 543497, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': 'CVE-2019-20907', 'alertSummary': 'CVE-2019-20907: EOS is not affected by this CVE, however custom agents using the python3 runtime can be vulnerable.', 'alertNote': 'EOS is not vulnerable to CVE-2019-20907. However, custom agents using the python3 runtime can be vulnerable. \n\nIn Lib/tarfile.py in Python through 3.8.3, an attacker is able to craft a TAR archive leading to an infinite loop when opened by tarfile.open, because _proc_pax lacks header validation. The fix for CVE-2019-20907 updates the python3 tarfile module to prevent an infinite loop.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.23.10', '4.24.4', '4.25.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'EOS is not vulnerable to CVE-2019-20907. However, custom agents using the python3 runtime can be vulnerable. \n\nIn Lib/tarfile.py in Python through 3.8.3, an attacker is able to craft a TAR archive leading to an infinite loop when opened by tarfile.open, because _proc_pax lacks header validation. The fix for CVE-2019-20907 updates the python3 tarfile module to prevent an infinite loop.'}, {'bugId': 543510, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': ' The "show daemon" cli command displays the last PID if the agent has died and not yet restarted', 'alertNote': 'The "show daemon" cli command displays the last PID if the agent has died and not yet restarted', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1605668301, 'exportedTime