rfaces and end up in active-partial state while a burst of MAC learning events are being exchanged between the two MLAG peers, then it is possible for the L2 agent to skip programming some of the MAC addresses synced between the two peers.\n\nThe workaround is to flap the M-LAG members on the peer whose MAC table is out of sync. \n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'LACPPortChannel'}, {'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'MLAGinterface'}]]}, {'bugId': 543931, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Under sustained heavy load, when more than one interface is receiving traffic at linerate capacity, the SandCounters process may restart repeatedly until traffic is reduced.', 'alertNote': 'Under sustained heavy load, when more than one interface is receiving traffic at linerate capacity, the SandCounters process may restart repeatedly until traffic is reduced.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.5', '4.29.2'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1678243343, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Under sustained heavy load, when more than one interface is receiving traffic at linerate capacity, the SandCounters process may restart repeatedly until traffic is reduced.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 543981, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': '"ptp monitor threshold offset-from-master drop" must be configured after PTP has synced from its master. If configured prior, the switch will drop all PTP packets indefinitely until the command is unconfigured', 'alertNote': "'ptp monitor threshold offset-from-master drop' must be configured after PTP has synced from its master. If configured prior, the switch will drop all PTP packets indefinitely until the command is unconfigured.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.23.14', '4.25.5', '4.26.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1643185610, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': "'ptp monitor threshold offset-from-master drop' must be configured after PTP has synced from its master. If configured prior, the switch will drop all PTP packets indefinitely until the command is unconfigured.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'PTPMonitorThresholdOffsetDrop'}]]}, {'bugId': 543999, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In EVPN VXLAN IRB deployment, if a host generates ICMP traffic towards a silent host on a different VNI hosted on a remote VTEP, the host may receive ICMP unreachable response from the first hop VTEP. The ICMP request will eventually succeed.', 'alertNote': 'In EVPN VXLAN IRB deployment, if a host generates ICMP traffic towards a silent host on a different VNI hosted on a remote VTEP, the host may receive ICMP unreachable response from the first hop VTEP. \n\nThe ICMP request will eventually succeed. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.10', '4.23.7', '4.24.5', '4.25.3', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1634279859, 'exportedTime': 1703116800, 'releaseNote': 'In EVPN VXLAN IRB deployment, if a host generates ICMP traffic towards a silent host on a different VNI hosted on a remote VTEP, the host may receive ICMP unreachable response from the first hop VTEP. \n\nThe ICMP request will eventually succeed. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnVxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 544313, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Under high ambient temperature conditions, the switch may reboot due to a critical system temperature.', 'alertNote': 'Under high ambient temperature conditions, the switch may reboot due to a critical system temperature.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.21.2.9', '4.21.14', '4.22.10', '4.23.7', '4.24.5', '4.25.3', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1627511562, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Under high ambient temperature conditions, the switch may reboot due to a critical system temperature.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7280CR2'}]]}, {'bugId': 544551, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When DPS feture is configured, there is a race condition with a transit router configuration that may lead to an unexpected restart of the Sfe agent. There is no available work around.', 'alertNote': 'When DPS feture is configured, there is a race condition with a transit router configuration that may lead to an unexpected restart of the Sfe agent. There is no available work around.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.5', '4.25.3', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1659144375, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'When DPS feture is configured, there is a race condition with a transit router configuration that may lead to an unexpected restart of the Sfe agent. There is no available work around.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CloudEOS'}]]}, {'bugId': 545404, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Running "show mpls route" or "show mpls route summary" on a standby supervisor can result in a CLI session restart.', 'alertNote': "Running 'show mpls route' or 'show mpls route summary' on a standby supervisor can result in a CLI session restart", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.7', '4.26.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1736522899, 'exportedTime': 1738281600, 'releaseNote': "Running 'show mpls route' or 'show mpls route summary' on a standby supervisor can result in a CLI session restart", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 545818, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'SandTm agent restart while a system or a linecard is being initialized can cause traffic flow to and from said system or linecard to be dropped.Workaround is power cycle the system or linecard', 'alertNote': 'SandTm agent restart while a system or a linecard is being initialized can cause traffic flow to and from said system or linecard to be dropped.\nWorkaround is power cycle the system or linecard.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.36.0FX-wbb', '4.36.0FX-wbb.1', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1774585654, 'exportedTime': 1785456000, 'releaseNote': 'SandTm agent restart while a system or a linecard is being initialized can cause traffic flow to and from said system or linecard to be dropped.\nWorkaround is power cycle the system or linecard.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}], [{'tag': 'SandGen5'}]]}, {'bugId': 546134, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On a device that is an MLAG or had MLAG configured if egress sFlow is enabled, interfaces can go to blocking with syslog SPANTREE-4-INTERFACE_SELF_LOOPED. To workaround, disable egress sFlow.', 'alertNote': "On a device that's an MLAG or had MLAG configured if egress sFlow is enabled, interfaces can go to blocking with syslog SPANTREE-4-INTERFACE_SELF_LOOPED.\n\nTo workaround, disable egress sFlow.\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.17.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.10', '4.23.8', '4.24.5', '4.25.3', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1624994452, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': "On a device that's an MLAG or had MLAG configured if egress sFlow is enabled, interfaces can go to blocking with syslog SPANTREE-4-INTERFACE_SELF_LOOPED.\n\nTo workaround, disable egress sFlow.\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'SflowEnabled'}, {'tag': 'stpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 546239, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'While in Tap Aggregation mode, changing the composition of a tool group may trigger a cascade of events which could lead to the group not able to replicate and transmit packets.  To restore functionality, exit and then re-enable Tap Aggregation mode.', 'alertNote': 'While in Tap Aggregation mode, changing the composition of a tool group may trigger a cascade of events which could lead to the group not able to replicate and transmit packets.\n\nTo restore functionality, exit and then re-enable Tap Aggregation mode.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'While in Tap Aggregation mode, changing the composition of a tool group may trigger a cascade of events which could lead to the group not able to replicate and transmit packets.\n\nTo restore functionality, exit and then re-enable Tap Aggregation mode.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}, {'tag': 'tapaggEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 546255, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When a counter feature in a TCAM profile fails to be programed into hardware, enabling the corresponding hardware counter feature may cause repetitive SandFap agent restarts. The workaround is to switch to a working TCAM profile.', 'alertNote': 'When a counter feature in a TCAM profile fails to be programed into the hardware, enabling the corresponding hardware counter feature may cause repetitive SandFap agent restarts. The workaround is to switch to a working TCAM profile.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.20.5'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1635284914, 'exportedTime': 1703116800, 'releaseNote': 'When a counter feature in a TCAM profile fails to be programed into the hardware, enabling the corresponding hardware counter feature may cause repetitive SandFap agent restarts. The workaround is to switch to a working TCAM profile.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen3'}]]}, {'bugId': 546409, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Hardware port resource (logical port) exhaustion may cause one of the following: - One or more interface to discard all packets. - Forwarding agent to restart (including continuous restarts).  Hardware port resource exhaustion is identified by STRATA-4-HW', 'alertNote': 'Hardware port resource (logical port) exhaustion may cause one of the following:\n- One or more interface to discard all packets (blackhole). \n- Forwarding agent to restart (including continuous restarts).\n\nThe error state may be entered at any time after the initial hardware port resource exhaustion event and may be triggered by transceiver insertion or removal, speed change, interface shutdown.\n\nHardware port resource exhaustion is identified by STRATA-4-HW_PORT_RESOURCE_FULL syslog. The switch may run out of hardware port resources (logical ports) in following cases:\n- Several 4x10G or 4x25G breakout ports are configured.\n- 40G-only transceivers inserted with a default speed configuration (e.g., 40GBASE-SRBD).\n\nIngress discards may be observed on the affected interfaces, and can be checked using the CLI command "show interfaces counters discards | nz"\n\nThe workaround is to reduce the number of 4x10G or 4x25G breakout connections to 2 (one breakout per following interface groups Ethernet49-52 and Ethernet53-56) and to configure 40G-only transceivers with the "speed 40g" interface configuration. After the configuration is applied, the forwarding agent must be restarted using the CLI command "platform trident reset". This will cause all interfaces to flap and a brief traffic outage to occur.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.6', '4.22.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.11', '4.23.8', '4.24.6', '4.25.4', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 10, 'lastBiteTime': 1721752399, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Hardware port resource (logical port) exhaustion may cause one of the following:\n- One or more interface to discard all packets (blackhole). \n- Forwarding agent to restart (including continuous restarts).\n\nThe error state may be entered at any time after the initial hardware port resource exhaustion event and may be triggered by transceiver insertion or removal, speed change, interface shutdown.\n\nHardware port resource exhaustion is identified by STRATA-4-HW_PORT_RESOURCE_FULL syslog. The switch may run out of hardware port resources (logical ports) in following cases:\n- Several 4x10G or 4x25G breakout ports are configured.\n- 40G-only transceivers inserted with a default speed configuration (e.g., 40GBASE-SRBD).\n\nIngress discards may be observed on the affected interfaces, and can be checked using the CLI command "show interfaces counters discards | nz"\n\nThe workaround is to reduce the number of 4x10G or 4x25G breakout connections to 2 (one breakout per following interface groups Ethernet49-52 and Ethernet53-56) and to configure 40G-only transceivers with the "speed 40g" interface configuration. After the configuration is applied, the forwarding agent must be restarted using the CLI command "platform trident reset". This will cause all interfaces to flap and a brief traffic outage to occur.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident3X5'}]]}, {'bugId': 546413, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'While in Tap Aggregation mode, if a port configured as a tool becomes inactive, e.g. due to speed change, the tool groups to which this port belongs may stop forwarding traffic. Please refer release notes for more info', 'alertNote': 'While in Tap Aggregation mode, if a port configured as a tool becomes inactive, e.g. due to speed change, the tool groups to which this port belongs may stop forwarding traffic.\n\nThe workaround is to temporarily reactivate this port, remove the tool configuration, and then deactivate it again.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.18.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.6', '4.25.4', '4.26.1'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1790884072, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'While in Tap Aggregation mode, if a port configured as a tool becomes inactive, e.g. due to speed change, the tool groups to which this port belongs may stop forwarding traffic.\n\nThe workaround is to temporarily reactivate this port, remove the tool configuration, and then deactivate it again.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}, {'tag': 'tapaggEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 546478, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Link quality may be poor on interfaces Ethernet1/1-Ethernet3/4 and Ethernet31/1-Ethernet32/4 with DAC cables longer than 1m. The workaround is to only use these ports with optics or with cables 1m or less.', 'alertNote': 'Link quality may be poor on interfaces Ethernet1/1-Ethernet3/4 and Ethernet31/1-Ethernet32/4 with DAC cables longer than 1m.\n\nThe workaround is to only use these ports with optics or with cables 1m or less.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.3'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.10', '4.23.7', '4.24.5', '4.25.3', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1605850478, 'exportedTime': 1701129600, 'releaseNote': 'Link quality may be poor on interfaces Ethernet1/1-Ethernet3/4 and Ethernet31/1-Ethernet32/4 with DAC cables longer than 1m.\n\nThe workaround is to only use these ports with optics or with cables 1m or less.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7170-32CD'}]]}, {'bugId': 546649, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'LACP port-channel member interface(s) may unexpectedly leave the port-channel due to "partner not in sync" syslog reason without member interface link status change. The member interface will rejoin the port-channel immediately after.', 'alertNote': 'LACP port-channel member interface(s) may unexpectedly leave the port-channel\ndue to "partner not in sync" syslog reason without member interface link status\nchange. The member interface will rejoin the port-channel immediately after.\nHowever, the event may cause port-channel interface to flap if there is only\none member interface configured in it.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.17.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.10', '4.23.8', '4.24.5', '4.25.3', '4.26.0'], 'bites': 67, 'lastBiteTime': 1778054485, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'LACP port-channel member interface(s) may unexpectedly leave the port-channel\ndue to "partner not in sync" syslog reason without member interface link status\nchange. The member interface will rejoin the port-channel immediately after.\nHowever, the event may cause port-channel interface to flap if there is only\none member interface configured in it.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'LACPPortChannel'}]]}, {'bugId': 546864, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Control plane traffic may be affected if there are packet drops that appear in show hardware counter drop.', 'alertNote': "Control plane traffic may be affected if there are packet drops that appear in 'show hardware counter drop'.\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.26.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.4', '4.26.0FX-BD', '4.26.0.1', '4.26.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1715881648, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': "Control plane traffic may be affected if there are packet drops that appear in 'show hardware counter drop'.\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 547328, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A single event upset (SEU) in the TDM_CALENDAR* tables may lead to packet loss. A forwarding agent restart is required to forward traffic normally.', 'alertNote': 'A single event upset (SEU) in the TDM_CALENDAR* tables may lead to packet loss.\n\nA forwarding agent restart is required to forward traffic normally.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.20.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.21.2.9', '4.21.14', '4.22.9', '4.23.7', '4.24.4', '4.25.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1720656000, 'releaseNote': 'A single event upset (SEU) in the TDM_CALENDAR* tables may lead to packet loss.\n\nA forwarding agent restart is required to forward traffic normally.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Tomahawk2'}]]}, {'bugId': 547329, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL'