y.\n\nThe workaround is to enable control word.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnMplsEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Jericho'}, {'tag': 'JerichoPlus'}]]}, {'bugId': 576810, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Some IPv4 system ACLs may not be applied correctly on tunneled IPv4 traffic that is routed on its inner IP header.', 'alertNote': 'Some IPv4 system ACLs may not be applied correctly on tunneled IPv4 traffic that is routed on its inner IP header', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.3.1', '4.25.4', '4.26.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Some IPv4 system ACLs may not be applied correctly on tunneled IPv4 traffic that is routed on its inner IP header', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Jericho2'}]]}, {'bugId': 577257, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If a BGP route is leaked from one VRF to another using VrfLeak agent and and the leaked route in target VRF is again leaked to another VRF using route-target import/export configuration in BGP, the Bgp agent can restart unexpectedly.', 'alertNote': 'If a route received from a BGP peer is leaked from one VRF to another using VrfLeak agent (https://eos.arista.com/eos-4-22-1f/eos-vrfleak-agent/) and the leaked route in the target VRF is again leaked to another VRF using route-target import/export configuration in BGP (https://eos.arista.com/eos-4-21-3f/inter-vrf-local-route-leaking/), the Bgp agent can restart unexpectedly.\n\nAs a workaround, use these mechanism to leak distinct set of routes. If a route has to be leaked across multiple VRFs, use either VrfLeak agent or route-target import/export configuraiton for leaking the route to all the target VRFs.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.9', '4.25.7', '4.26.5', '4.27.1'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1691103448, 'exportedTime': 1731888000, 'releaseNote': 'If a route received from a BGP peer is leaked from one VRF to another using VrfLeak agent (https://eos.arista.com/eos-4-22-1f/eos-vrfleak-agent/) and the leaked route in the target VRF is again leaked to another VRF using route-target import/export configuration in BGP (https://eos.arista.com/eos-4-21-3f/inter-vrf-local-route-leaking/), the Bgp agent can restart unexpectedly.\n\nAs a workaround, use these mechanism to leak distinct set of routes. If a route has to be leaked across multiple VRFs, use either VrfLeak agent or route-target import/export configuraiton for leaking the route to all the target VRFs.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'BGPEnabledVrf'}]]}, {'bugId': 577462, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a MLAG setup, non routable packets destined to VARP MAC address coming in on a VXLAN VLAN (either on VXLAN edge port or encapped and entering a core port) can get looped over the peer-link.', 'alertNote': 'In a MLAG setup, non routable packets destined to VARP MAC address coming in on a VXLAN VLAN (either on VXLAN edge port or encapped and entering a core port) can get looped over the peer-link.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.12', '4.21.2.7', '4.21.6.4', '4.22.7', '4.23.1.1', '4.23.5', '4.24.2.2', '4.24.2FX-EVPN-MCAST.1', '4.24.3', '4.25.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.11', '4.23.8', '4.24.6', '4.25.4', '4.26.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1617657267, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'In a MLAG setup, non routable packets destined to VARP MAC address coming in on a VXLAN VLAN (either on VXLAN edge port or encapped and entering a core port) can get looped over the peer-link.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7250X'}, {'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}, {'tag': 'vxlanRouting'}], [{'tag': '7300X3'}, {'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}, {'tag': 'vxlanRouting'}]]}, {'bugId': 578037, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Rib agent or the multiagents (Isis/Ospf) can restart with a large prefix-list configuration.', 'alertNote': 'Rib agent or the multiagents (Isis/Ospf) can restart with a large prefix-list configuration\n\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.10', '4.25.8', '4.26.4', '4.27.2'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1644442713, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Rib agent or the multiagents (Isis/Ospf) can restart with a large prefix-list configuration\n\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ospfEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'RibModel'}], [{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'isisEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 578084, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'With "logging format timestamp traditional timezone" and dynamic daylight saving timezones such as EST5EDT, logging messages do not update timezone properly when it switches to or from daylight saving.time. Please refer release notes', 'alertNote': 'With "logging format timestamp traditional timezone" and dynamic daylight saving timezones such as EST5EDT, logging messages do not update timezone properly when it switches to or from daylight saving.time. To work around this issue, toggle any logging configuration to force an update.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.1'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1655417188, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'With "logging format timestamp traditional timezone" and dynamic daylight saving timezones such as EST5EDT, logging messages do not update timezone properly when it switches to or from daylight saving.time. To work around this issue, toggle any logging configuration to force an update.'}, {'bugId': 578132, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In the event that a LANZ streaming client sends data to the server, the server will fail to recognise the connection as closed even after it was closed, so the client is still counted as active., please refer release notes for more info and workaround', 'alertNote': "In the event that a LANZ streaming client sends data to the server, the server will fail to recognise the connection as closed even after it was closed, so the client is still counted as active. The stale connection will also show up in the `show queue-monitor streaming clients' output. If enough clients do this, the maximum number (as set by the `max-connections <number>` command in the `queue-monitor streaming' configuration) will be reached and no more clients can connect. A workaround is to restart the LANZ agent.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.23.9', '4.24.9', '4.25.7', '4.26.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1642545710, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': "In the event that a LANZ streaming client sends data to the server, the server will fail to recognise the connection as closed even after it was closed, so the client is still counted as active. The stale connection will also show up in the `show queue-monitor streaming clients' output. If enough clients do this, the maximum number (as set by the `max-connections <number>` command in the `queue-monitor streaming' configuration) will be reached and no more clients can connect. A workaround is to restart the LANZ agent.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'lanzEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 578146, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A primary policy applied via a config session may not get programmed correctly in hardware if the interface\\(s\\) where this policy is applied is/are also covered by a fallback PBR policy.', 'alertNote': 'A config-session that applies primary policy to an interface and updates ACLs/classes used by the primary policy may lead to the policy to not be programmed correctly in hardware if the interface(s) where this policy is applied is/are also covered by a fallback PBR policy.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1631343466, 'exportedTime': 1793664000, 'releaseNote': 'A config-session that applies primary policy to an interface and updates ACLs/classes used by the primary policy may lead to the policy to not be programmed correctly in hardware if the interface(s) where this policy is applied is/are also covered by a fallback PBR policy.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'PBRconfigured'}, {'tag': 'Sand'}]]}, {'bugId': 578276, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'DHCPv6 prefix received with valid lifetime of zero may persist forever inthe routing database in the presence of ipv6 dhcp relay install routes. Please check Release Notes for further details.', 'alertNote': 'A DHCPv6 prefix received with valid lifetime of zero may persist forever in the routing database in the presence of \'ipv6 dhcp relay install routes\'. A workaround might be to toggle "ipv6 dhcp relay install routes" command, which deletes all DHCPv6 routes, including the stale ones with negative lifetime.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.20.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.11', '4.23.9', '4.24.7', '4.25.4', '4.26.1'], 'bites': 7, 'lastBiteTime': 1680567912, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'A DHCPv6 prefix received with valid lifetime of zero may persist forever in the routing database in the presence of \'ipv6 dhcp relay install routes\'. A workaround might be to toggle "ipv6 dhcp relay install routes" command, which deletes all DHCPv6 routes, including the stale ones with negative lifetime.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ipv6RoutingEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 578375, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In an EVPN deployment, ARP entries learned from MAC/IP advertisement routes may remain stale after removing the associate MAC-VRF or changing the BGP AS number.  The workaround is to restart the BGP agent.', 'alertNote': 'In an EVPN deployment, ARP entries learned from MAC/IP advertisement routes may remain stale after removing the associate M