ded  as well as new members are added to the Port-channel at same time. The workaround is to reapply the ACL on the port-channel sub-interface.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.26.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1722308316, 'exportedTime': 1759968000, 'releaseNote': 'Ingress ACL applied to port-channel sub-interface, might not be installed properly, if ACL rules are added  as well as new members are added to the Port-channel at same time. The workaround is to reapply the ACL on the port-channel sub-interface.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 583831, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Continous route churn within a BGP address family can cause the Bgp agent to restart due to excessive memory usage ', 'alertNote': 'Continous route churn within a BGP address family can cause the Bgp agent to restart due to excessive memory usage.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.4', '4.26.1'], 'bites': 42, 'lastBiteTime': 1763178824, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Continous route churn within a BGP address family can cause the Bgp agent to restart due to excessive memory usage.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 584222, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a EVPN MH deployment, reloading a PE with one or more EVPN instances configured with designated-forwarder election preference rule low may result in DF election disagreement and result in packet duplication or loss', 'alertNote': 'In a EVPN MH deployment, reloading a PE with one or more EVPN instances configured with "designated-forwarder election preference rule low" may result in the election using the "high" rule. This may result in DF election disagreement causing  multiple or zero PE to be elected the designated forwarder and result in packet duplication or loss.\n\nThe workaround is to apply 