r, but the interface over which the BGP neighbor is connected is shut down, EOS will generate periodic ARP requests, which lead to output discards. The workaround is to remove the BGP neighbor or to put the interface into switchport mode.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.13.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.2'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1711418893, 'exportedTime': 1786406400, 'releaseNote': 'When BFD is enabled for a BGP neighbor, but the interface over which the BGP neighbor is connected is shut down, EOS will generate periodic ARP requests, which lead to output discards. The workaround is to remove the BGP neighbor or to put the interface into switchport mode.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'BFDenabled'}, {'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'ArBgp'}]]}, {'bugId': 623597, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Using optics at 4x10G mode on Ethernet104 port might cause the forwarding agent to restart continuously. A workaround is to use any other QSFP100 port for 4x10G operation with optics.', 'alertNote': 'Using optics at 4x10G mode on Ethernet104 port might cause the forwarding agent to restart continuously.\n\nA workaround is to use any other QSFP100 port for 4x10G operation with optics.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.6', '4.25.3', '4.26.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.9', '4.25.7', '4.26.4', '4.27.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1638284659, 'exportedTime': 1774396800, 'releaseNote': 'Using optics at 4x10G mode on Ethernet104 port might cause the forwarding agent to restart continuously.\n\nA workaround is to use any other QSFP100 port for 4x10G operation with optics.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident3'}]]}, {'bugId': 623667, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': ' If the router receives IPv4 or IPv6 multicast BGP routes with nexthop covered by the same prefix and the nexthop is resolved by a route in unicast RIB table, it may cause continous recursive nexthop resolution