ation.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'portChannelEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 638604, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A PE configured for Ipv6 EVPN MPLS IRB that is supporting multi-homed hosts, may start consuming large amounts of CPU and continuously issuing BGP EVPN updates to its peers when discovering the IPv6 ND binding of a host on the VLAN', 'alertNote': 'A PE configured for EVPN MPLS IRB that is supporting multi-homed hosts, and has IPv6 configuration on an EVPN enabled VLAN interface, may start consuming large amounts of CPU and continuousl\ny issuing BGP EVPN updates to its peers when discovering the IPv6 ND binding of a host on the VLAN.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.26.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.5', '4.27.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1634680968, 'exportedTime': 1784764800, 'releaseNote': 'A PE configured for EVPN MPLS IRB that is supporting multi-homed hosts, and has IPv6 configuration on an EVPN enabled VLAN interface, may start consuming large amounts of CPU and continuousl\ny issuing BGP EVPN updates to its peers when discovering the IPv6 ND binding of a host on the VLAN.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpn-multihoming-enabled'}, {'tag': 'evpnMplsEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Ipv6Interface'}]]}, {'bugId': 638747, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A Receive Broadcast route may be incorrectly used to resolve a next hop, causing the Rib agent to restart unexpectedly.', 'alertNote': 'A Receive Broadcast route may be incorrectly used to resolve a next hop, causing the Rib agent to restart unexpectedly.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.26.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.5', '4.27.4', '4.28.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1716050449, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'A Receive Broadcast route may be incorrectly used to resolve a next hop, causing the Rib agent to restart unexpectedly.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'RibModel'}]]}, {'bugId': 638807, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The BGP aggregate update may get delayed (potentially indefinitely) when contributors to the aggregate churn continuously', 'alertNote': 'The BGP aggregate update may get delayed (potentially indefinitely) when contributors to the aggregate churn continuously.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.16.7-L2EVPN', '4.18.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.8', '4.26.6', '4.27.5', '4.28.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1630509432, 'exportedTime': 1731888000, 'releaseNote': 'The BGP aggregate update may get delayed (potentially indefinitely) when contributors to the aggregate churn continuously.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'BGPAggregateAddress'}, {'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 638893, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'DHCPv6 requests will be dropped if there is no global unicast address on the client facing interface. Workaround is to configure a global address.', 'alertNote': 'DHCPv6 requests will be dropped if there is no global unicast address on the client facing interface.\n\nWorkaround is to configure a global address.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.8', '4.29.5', '4.30.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1713424980, 'exportedTime': 1716163200, 'releaseNote': 'DHCPv6 requests will be dropped if there is no global unicast address on the client facing interface.\n\nWorkaround is to configure a global address.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dhcpRelayConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 639415, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a VXLAN MLAG deployment, configuring "hardware forwarding id" on a Loopback interface of the primary can cause the corresponding dynamic VLAN to get re-allocated endlessly on both MLAG peers', 'alertNote': "In a VXLAN MLAG deployment, configuring 'hardware forwarding id' on a Loopback interface of the primary can cause the corresponding dynamic VLAN to get re-allocated endlessly on both MLAG peers.\n\nAs a workaround, disable 'hardware forwarding id' and configure a VLAN and then create an SVI in that VRF.  The SVI will need to have an ip address assigned and no autostate configured.\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.7', '4.26.5', '4.27.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1637620027, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': "In a VXLAN MLAG deployment, configuring 'hardware forwarding id' on a Loopback interface of the primary can cause the corresponding dynamic VLAN to get re-allocated endlessly on both MLAG peers.\n\nAs a workaround, disable 'hardware forwarding id' and configure a VLAN and then create an SVI in that VRF.  The SVI will need to have an ip address assigned and no autostate configured.\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 639721, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'EVPN VXLAN Multihomed peers may not be able to ping each other using overlay physical IPs.', 'alertNote': "In an EVPN VXLAN All-Active Multihoming (MH) deployment, pings between any overlay physical IPs configured on local SVIs on the MH peers will fail to resolve the ARP entry for the overlay physical IPs and therefore fail.\n\nThe workaround is to configure static ARP entries for the overlay  SVI physical IP addresses on  the relevant MH peers. \n\nIf the multi-homed VTEPs are acting as an any-cast centralized gateway for one or more L2-VTEPs and are configured with a VIRTUAL VTEP IP (VVTEP IP), then the ARP resolution for a host behind a L2-VTEP  initiated from one of the MH VTEPs may fail to synchronize the ARP reply on all the any-cast gateway MH VTEPs. \n\nThe workaround would be to use 'ip virtual-router' instead of 'ip address virtual'  to configure the any-cast gateway IPs on the MH VTEPs. \n\n\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.10', '4.24.8', '4.25.6', '4.26.3', '4.27.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.10', '4.25.8', '4.26.5', '4.27.4', '4.28.0'], 'bites': 8, 'lastBiteTime': 1717208824, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': "In an EVPN VXLAN All-Active Multihoming (MH) deployment, pings between any overlay physical IPs configured on local SVIs on the MH peers will fail to resolve the ARP entry for the overlay physical IPs and therefore fail.\n\nThe workaround is to configure static ARP entries for the overlay  SVI physical IP addresses on  the relevant MH peers. \n\nIf the multi-homed VTEPs are acting as an any-cast centralized gateway for one or more L2-VTEPs and are configured with a VIRTUAL VTEP IP (VVTEP IP), then the ARP resolution for a host behind a L2-VTEP  initiated from one of the MH VTEPs may fail to synchronize the ARP reply on all the any-cast gateway MH VTEPs. \n\nThe workaround would be to use 'ip virtual-router' instead of 'ip address virtual'  to configure the any-cast gateway IPs on the MH VTEPs. \n\n\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpn-multihoming-enabled'}, {'tag': 'evpnVxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 639912, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When a BGP UPDATE message is received with a 32-byte IPv6 nexthop field, then if the first 64 bits of the link-local address are something other than the RFC4291-compliant value of fe80:: followed by 54 zeros, a warning is logged to syslog.', 'alertNote': 'When a BGP UPDATE message is received with a 32-byte IPv6 nexthop field (containing a global address and a scoped, link local address) if the first 64 bits of the link-local address are something other than the RFC4291-compliant value of fe80:: followed by 54 zeros, a warning is logged to syslog.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1637746280, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'When a BGP UPDATE message is received with a 32-byte IPv6 nexthop field (containing a global address and a scoped, link local address) if th