ite delay post its successful Dot1x authentication, its MAC address can get advertised in the older (non-phone) VLAN via EVPN. The workaround is to restart Dot1x agent.', 'alertNote': "In the scenario of a phone sending LLDP packets after a finite delay post it's successful Dot1x authentication, it's MAC address can get advertised in the older (non-phone) VLAN via EVPN. The workaround is to restart Dot1x agent.\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.24.10', '4.25.8', '4.26.5', '4.27.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1638441509, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': "In the scenario of a phone sending LLDP packets after a finite delay post it's successful Dot1x authentication, it's MAC address can get advertised in the older (non-phone) VLAN via EVPN. The workaround is to restart Dot1x agent.\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}, {'tag': 'evpnVxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 645771, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In single-agent mode,changing BGP maximum-path configuration and dynamic peer group configuration in a configuration session(or via configuration replace) may cause dynamic peer received routes to have wrong local preference and administrative distance', 'alertNote': 'In single agent mode, changing the BGP maximum-path configuration and a dynamic peer group configuration together in a configuration session (or via configuration replace) may cause routes received from the dynamic peers to be assigned a local preference of 0 (instead of the default 100) and administrative distance of 255 (instead the default 200 or configured distance).\n\nAs a workaround avoid changing maximum-path config with dynamic peer group config together in a config session.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.22.8', '4.23.6', '4.24.4', '4.25.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1639727321, 'exportedTime': 1739145600, 'releaseNote': 'In single agent mode, changing the BGP maximum-path configuration and a dynamic peer group configuration together in a configuration session (or via configuration replace) may cause routes received from the dynamic peers to be assigned a local preference of 0 (instead of the default 100) and administrative distance of 255 (instead the default 200 or configured distance).\n\nAs a workaround avoid changing maximum-path config with dynamic peer group config together in a config session.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}, {'tag': 'RibModel'}]]}, {'bugId': 645945, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Latency based queue drops may be observed on VOQs configured to have dynamic rate class based features. For the list please refer release notes', 'alertNote': 'Latency based queue drops may be observed on VOQs configured to have dynamic rate class based features. The list includes:-\n1) Configurable static tail-drops/FADT per speed, per speed+traffic-class\n2) WRED\n3) ECN\n4) Interface based per traffic-class per drop precedence tail drops', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.1.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Latency based queue drops may be observed on VOQs configured to have dynamic rate class based features. The list includes:-\n1) Configurable static tail-drops/FADT per speed, per speed+traffic-class\n2) WRED\n3) ECN\n4) Interface based per traffic-class per drop precedence tail drops', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 647110, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'OpenConfig agent is unable to populate the tunnel counters at "interfaces/interface[name=Tunnel*]/state/counters".', 'alertNote': 'OpenConfig agent is unable to populate the tunnel counters at "interfaces/interface[name=Tunnel*]/state/counters". A workaround is to configure Octa agent and add the following CLI config:\nmanagement api models\n   provider