]]}, {'bugId': 676677, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When there is a churn in group membership or a unicast route to RP causes (*, g) routes to be deleted and re-added, (*, G) routes may not get programmed in hardware. This causes complete traffic loss for those groups.', 'alertNote': "When there is a churn in group membership or a unicast route to RP causes (*, g) routes to be deleted and re-added, (*, G) routes may not get programmed in hardware. This causes complete traffic loss for those groups.\n\nTriggers:\nThis is applicable when spt-threshold is configured to infinity. Otherwise, (*, G) routes are not programmed in hardware and hence this bug is not applicable.\n\nWorkaround:\nSometimes 'clear ip mroute' will resolve this issue. Otherwise, 'shut and no shut' of the IIF interface of the (*, G) route will clear this condition.\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.10', '4.26.nofixyet', '4.27.nofixyet', '4.28.1'], 'bites': 10, 'lastBiteTime': 1753490887, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': "When there is a churn in group membership or a unicast route to RP causes (*, g) routes to be deleted and re-added, (*, G) routes may not get programmed in hardware. This causes complete traffic loss for those groups.\n\nTriggers:\nThis is applicable when spt-threshold is configured to infinity. Otherwise, (*, G) routes are not programmed in hardware and hence this bug is not applicable.\n\nWorkaround:\nSometimes 'clear ip mroute' will resolve this issue. Otherwise, 'shut and no shut' of the IIF interface of the (*, G) route will clear this condition.\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'multicastEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'ipv6MulticastEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 677001, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Strata agent may report successful parity error correction before the error is corrected. If correction later fails, another syslog reports the failure for the same memory.', 'alertNote': "Strata agent can prematurely report success of parity error correction for a memory, where the parity error hasn't actually been corrected. If the parity error correction failed afterward, another syslog will be emitted to indicate parity error correction failure of the same memory.. ", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.3'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1784400538, 'exportedTime': 1793318400, 'releaseNote': "Strata agent can prematurely report success of parity error correction for a memory, where the parity error hasn't actually been corrected. If the parity error correction failed afterward, another syslog will be emitted to indicate parity error correction failure of the same memory.. ", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident4X11'}], [{'tag': '7388X5-SC'}]]}, {'bugId': 677922, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On ports with CRT50216 PHY, interfaces with misconfigured speeds may not show up in the output of #show interfaces status by default. Workaround is to run #service interface inactive expose, command to expose the interfaces and be able to configure them.', 'alertNote': 'On ports with CRT50216 PHY, interfaces with misconfigured speeds may not show up in the output of "show interfaces status" by default.\n\nWorkaround is to run "service interface inactive expose" CLI command to expose the interfaces and be able to configure them.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1646180583, 'exportedTime': 1710288000, 'releaseNote': 'On ports with CRT50216 PHY, interfaces with misconfigured speeds may not show up in the output of "show interfaces status" by default.\n\nWorkaround is to run "service interface inactive expose" CLI command to expose the interfaces and be able to configure them.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}], [{'tag': '7289'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7130LBR-48S6QD'}]]}, {'bugId': 67