s of an aggregate can cause the Bgp agent to restart unexpectedly.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.8', '4.26.6'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1670463900, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'Churn on the contributors of an aggregate can cause the Bgp agent to restart unexpectedly.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 701800, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may drop log messages sometimes, especially at startup.', 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may drop log messages sometimes, especially at startup.', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v0.1'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.28.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1654502420, 'exportedTime': 1784160000, 'releaseNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may drop log messages sometimes, especially at startup.'}, {'bugId': 701820, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When configuring MLAG before the system is fully warm, the system can restart unexpectedly due to a kernel panic', 'alertNote': 'When configuring MLAG before the system is fully warm, the system can restart unexpectedly due to a kernel panic.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.10', '4.26.9', '4.27.7', '4.28.4', '4.29.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'When configuring MLAG before the system is fully warm, the system can restart unexpectedly due to a kernel panic.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Strata'}], [{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Trident4'}]]}, {'bugId': 701912, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Under scenarios involving port speed change, transceiver hotswap while port is carrying traffic, the port queues may get stuck. ', 'alertNote': "Under scenarios involving port speed change, transceiver hotswap while port is carrying traffic, it's queues may get stuck.\nFollowing are the workarounds:-\n1) For flow stuck arising from transceiver hotswap we will need to restart SandFapNi agent\n2) For flow stuck arising from port Speed change we will need to reload to recover if (1) doesn't \n     work out.\n\nTo avoid flow stuck due to port speed change, follow the steps below\na) Shutdown the port\nb) Change the speed around 5 to 10 seconds later\nc) Unshut the port. ", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.8', '4.27.7', '4.28.3', '4.29.0'], 'bites': 14, 'lastBiteTime': 1767686527, 'exportedTime': 1700784000, 'releaseNote': "Under scenarios involving port speed change, transceiver hotswap while port is carrying traffic, it's queues may get stuck.\nFollowing are the workarounds:-\n1) For flow stuck arising from transceiver hotswap we will need to restart SandFapNi agent\n2) For flow stuck arising from port Speed change we will need to reload to recover if (1) doesn't \n     work out.\n\nTo avoid flow stuck due to port speed change, follow the steps below\na) Shutdown the port\nb) Change the speed around 5 to 10 seconds later\nc) Unshut the port. ", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 702037, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A flap on Et1-Et24 BASE-T interfaces may cause the forwarding agent to restart. This will cause multiple interfaces to briefly flap and a traffic outage to occur.', 'alertNote': 'A flap on Et1-Et24 BASE-T interfaces may cause the forwarding agent to restart. This will cause multiple interfaces to briefly flap and a traffic outage to occur.\n\nA workaround would be to use the "speed forced 1gfull" command on all BASE-T ports which are operating at 1Gbps.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.26.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.8', '4.28.2'], 'bites': 28, 'lastBiteTime': 1774053162, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'A flap on Et1-Et24 BASE-T interfaces may cause the forwarding agent to restart. This will cause multiple interfaces to briefly flap and a traffic outage to occur.\n\nA workaround would be to use the "speed forced 1gfull" command on all BASE-T ports which are operating at 1Gbps.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7010TX'}]]}, {'bugId': 702086, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Certain features may stop working after a reload on switches that meet all of the criteria listed in release notes. Please refer release notes for more in detail information', 'alertNote': 'Certain features may stop working after a reload on switches that meet all of the criteria listed below:\n- at least one group of SFP28 interfaces is present on the switch\n- at least one interface in the group does not have a transceiver\n\nThe following features may stop working:\n- L2 or L3 Subinterface\n- VLAN Mapping\n- EVPN MPLS\n- VXLAN\n- Private VLAN\n- TAP Aggregation\n- L3 interface\n\nThe workaround is to flap the packet\'s ingress interface by doing "shut" followed by "no shut".', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.11', '4.28.6', '4.29.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1711769184, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Certain features may stop working after a reload on switches that meet all of the criteria listed below:\n- at least one group of SFP28 interfaces is present on the switch\n- at least one interface in the group does not have a transceiver\n\nThe following features may stop working:\n- L2 or L3 Subinterface\n- VLAN Mapping\n- EVPN MPLS\n- VXLAN\n- Private VLAN\n- TAP Aggregation\n- L3 interface\n\nThe workaround is to flap the packet\'s ingress interface by doing "shut" followed by "no shut".', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}, {'tag': 'SandGen3'}], [{'tag': 'SandGen3'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 702131, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'With 7816R3-FM fan failure