m churn, the system can begin to run out of memory after a period of time.\n'}, {'bugId': 704768, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Some IP/IPv6 routes resolved over VXLAN may drop traffic. Affected routes will be shown with type "dropRoute" in "show ip hardware ale routes" CLI output. Please see Release Notes for more details.', 'alertNote': 'Some IP/IPv6 routes resolved over VXLAN may persistently drop traffic. Affected routes will be shown with type "dropRoute" in the "show ip hardware ale routes" CLI command, which indicates that these routes are presently dropping traffic. The issue can occur when these routes have previously been unresolved according to the device\'s static configuration or protocol state (eg. BGP).\nWorkarounds include removing and re-adding the affected route, or forcing a temporary update to the route, such as adding and removing a more preferred path to the route.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.11', '4.27.10', '4.28.7', '4.29.3', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1740524286, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Some IP/IPv6 routes resolved over VXLAN may persistently drop traffic. Affected routes will be shown with type "dropRoute" in the "show ip hardware ale routes" CLI command, which indicates that these routes are presently dropping traffic. The issue can occur when these routes have previously been unresolved according to the device\'s static configuration or protocol state (eg. BGP).\nWorkarounds include removing and re-adding the affected route, or forcing a temporary update to the route, such as adding and removing a more preferred path to the route.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Strata'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 704851, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If an OpenStack region with over 4000 VMs attempts to sync with the OpenStack service on CVX it may fail preventing dynamic VLANs and VLAN to VNI mappings from being provisioned. Please see release notes', 'alertNote': 'If an OpenStack region with over 4000 VMs attempts to sync with the OpenStack service on CVX, it may fail, preventing dynamic VLANs and VLAN to VNI mappings from being provisioned. When this issue occurs, the error message "client intended to send too large body" will appear in /var/log/nginx-error.log on CVX.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.18.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.10', '4.26.8', '4.27.6', '4.28.3', '4.29.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1656619336, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'If an OpenStack region with over 4000 VMs attempts to sync with the OpenStack service on CVX, it may fail, preventing dynamic VLANs and VLAN to VNI mappings from being provisioned. When this issue occurs, the error message "client intended to send too large body" will appear in /var/log/nginx-error.log on CVX.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CVXserverconfigured'}, {'tag': 'openstackEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 704903, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "In a CVX deployment, a switch's mount of CVX state might be stuck in the InProgress state if there is link flap between the switch and CVX.", 'alertNote': 'In a CVX deployment, a switch\'s mount of CVX state might be stuck in the "InProgress" state if there is link flap between the switch and CVX. The status of the switch mount of CVX state is available through "show management cvx mounts"\n\nIn a MLAG deployment, a workaround is to trigger a failover on the switch with a mount in the "InProgress" state. In a non-MLAG deployment a workaround is to reload the switch.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.25.10', '4.26.9', '4.27.6', '4.28.3', '4.29.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1656324706, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'In a CVX deployment, a switch\'s mount of CVX state might be stuck in the "InProgress" state if there is link flap between the 