he lease time for the IP expires.Please refer release notes', 'alertNote': 'CloudEOS routers deployed on cloud platforms (AWS,Azure,GCP) can lose the IP address on the Ethernet1 interface if the IP is assigned via DHCP and the lease time for the IP expires.\nThe workaround is to set the lifetime of the IP to be infinite using "bash sudo ip addr change 10.10.10.10/24 dev et1 valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever" command where 10.10.10.10/24 is an example IP address that is assigned on the interface via DHCP.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1706895796, 'exportedTime': 1734134400, 'releaseNote': 'CloudEOS routers deployed on cloud platforms (AWS,Azure,GCP) can lose the IP address on the Ethernet1 interface if the IP is assigned via DHCP and the lease time for the IP expires.\nThe workaround is to set the lifetime of the IP to be infinite using "bash sudo ip addr change 10.10.10.10/24 dev et1 valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever" command where 10.10.10.10/24 is an example IP address that is assigned on the interface via DHCP.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'cEOS'}]]}, {'bugId': 739571, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': '"transceiver qsfp default-mode 4x10G" does not work on QSFP100 ports', 'alertNote': '"transceiver qsfp default-mode 4x10G" does not work on QSFP100 ports', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1746660643, 'exportedTime': 1748563200, 'releaseNote': '"transceiver qsfp default-mode 4x10G" does not work on QSFP100 ports', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR3M-48YC8'}]]}, {'bugId': 739620, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In the single agent mode when an ECMP route has a mix of IPv4 and IPv6 nexthops, the underlying adjacency may be programmed incorrectly and the route may become unreachable.Please refer release notes', 'alertNote': 'In the single agent mode when an ECMP route has a mix of IPv4 and IPv6 nexthops, the underlying adjacency may be programmed incorrectly and the route may become unreachable. \n\nPossible workarounds:\n1) Switch to the multi-agent mode OR\n2) At Rib level, prevent formation of ECMP groups that have a combination of v4 and v6 nexthops using policy or other config.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.17.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.8', '4.28.5', '4.29.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1728938076, 'exportedTime': 1672531200, 'releaseNote': 'In the single agent mode when an ECMP route has a mix of IPv4 and IPv6 nexthops, the underlying adjacency may be programmed incorrectly and the route may become unreachable. \n\nPossible workarounds:\n1) Switch to the multi-agent mode OR\n2) At Rib level, prevent formation of ECMP groups that have a combination of v4 and v6 nexthops using policy or other config.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'RibModel'}]]}, {'bugId': 739931, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'QSFP-100G-CWDM4 and QSFP-100G-XCWDM4 transceivers with serials beginning with XHT may experience high pre-FEC BER and uncorrectable FEC errors on the peer or fail to link up.', 'alertNote': "QSFP-100G-CWDM4 and QSFP-100G-XCWDM4 transceivers with serials beginning with XHT may experience high pre-FEC BER and  uncorrectable FEC errors on the peer or fail to link up. \n\nA workaround is to adjust the tx input equalization of the transceiver with the command 'transceiver electrical lane 1-4 tx-input-equalization module-default' in config-if mode. The command is to be applied on the /1 of the QSFP interface. ", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.15.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.10', '4.27.9', '4.28.6', '4.29.3', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1748437019, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': "QSFP-100G-CWDM4 and QSFP-100G-XCWDM4 transceivers with serials beginning with XHT may experience high pre-FEC BER and  uncorrectable FEC errors on the peer or fail to link up. \n\nA workaround is to adjust the tx input equalization of the transceiver with the command 'transceiver electrical lane 1-4 tx-input-equalization module-default' in config-if mode. The command is to be applied on the /1 of the QSFP interface. ", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'QSFP-100G-CWDM4'}], [{'tag': 'QSFP-100G-XCWDM4'}]]}, {'bugId': 740294, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'BASE-T ports with auto-negotiation enabled with the command #speed auto, that auto-negotiate to a speed less than 10G can flap when the "speed" CLI command is run on another port or the transceiver is removed on another port.', 'alertNote': 'BASE-T ports with auto-negotiation enabled with the command \'speed auto\',  that auto-negotiate to a speed less than 10G can flap when the "speed" CLI command is run on another port or the transceiver is removed on another port.\n\nThe workaround is to not configure the speed with \'no speed\' or force the speed of the port to the auto-negotiated speed using the \'speed forced <speed>\'  CLI command.  The \'no speed\' configuration is equivalent to the \'speed auto\' configuration for the fixed BASE-T ports.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.18.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.12', '4.28.9', '4.29.5', '4.30.2'], 'bites': 7, 'lastBiteTime': 1734353106, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'BASE-T ports with auto-negotiation enabled with the command \'speed auto\',  that auto-negotiate to a speed less than 10G can flap when the "speed" CLI command is run on another port or the transceiver is removed on another port.\n\nThe workaround is to not configure the speed with \'no speed\' or force the speed of the port to the auto-negotiated speed using the \'speed forced <speed>\'  CLI command.  The \'no speed\' configuration is equivalent to the \'speed auto\' configuration for the fixed BASE-T ports.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7280TR'}