18377, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Constant link flaps on a lag member of MLAG peer links may result in STP looping with VXLAN MLAG', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Sand'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 761575, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If the combined headroom for all no-drop priority flow control priorities on all ports is large to exhaust the entire shared ingress cells, then any restart of the Strata forwarding plane agent can cause continuous restarts. Refer release notes', 'alertNote': 'If the combined headroom for all \'no-drop\' priority flow control priorities on all ports is sufficiently large to exhaust the entire shared ingress cells as shown by "show platform trident mmu buffers", then any restart of the Strata forwarding plane agent can cause successive continuous restarts.\nA workaround is to reduce the total number of \'no-drop\' priorities configured, or to reduce the headroom value using the "ingress headroom" option of the "platform trident mmu queue profile" command.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.9', '4.28.8', '4.29.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1671738863, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'If the combined headroom for all \'no-drop\' priority flow control priorities on all ports is sufficiently large to exhaust the entire shared ingress cells as shown by "show platform trident mmu buffers", then any restart of the Strata forwarding plane agent can cause successive continuous restarts.\nA workaround is to reduce the total number of \'no-drop\' priorities configured, or to reduce the headroom value using the "ingress headroom" option of the "platform trident mmu queue profile" command.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Helix4'}]]}, {'bugId': 762363, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'After linecard hotswap or slice agent restart, static or peer-learned MAC addresses may go missing in hardware, resulting in unexpected flooding, and be incorrectly displayed in the mac-address table. A workaround is to remove and re-add the MAC address.', 'alertNote': 'After linecard hotswap or slice agent restart, static or peer-learned MAC addresses may go missing in hardware, which can result in unexpected flooding.  Further, such missing macs may incorrectly be displayed in the output for "show mac-address-table". \nA workaround for this issue is to remove and readd the MAC address.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.1', '4.29.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1719360000, 'releaseNote': 'After linecard hotswap or slice agent restart, static or peer-learned MAC addresses may go missing in hardware, which can result in unexpected flooding.  Further, such missing macs may incorrectly be displayed in the output for "show mac-address-table". \nA workaround for this issue is to remove and readd the MAC address.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident3'}]]}, {'bugId': 762693, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When upgrading an MLAG switch pair between certain EOS versions, MLAG may fail to form if there are too many VLANs in the MST configuration; around 2000+ VLANs in non-zero MSTs, this issue may occur.', 'alertNote': 'When upgrading an MLAG switch pair between certain EOS versions, MLAG may fail to form if there are too many VLANs in the MST configuration. Specifically, if around 2000+ VLANs are configured in non-zero MSTs, this issue may occur.\n\nThe best workaround is to upgrade to a release which has the fix for this issue. As long as the newer version of EOS that is being upgraded to has the fix, this bug will not be hit.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.9', '4.28.6', '4.29.2'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1739316272, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'When upgrading an MLAG switch pair between certain EOS versions, MLAG may fail to form if there are too many VLANs in the MST configuration. Specifically, if around 2000+ VLANs are configured in non-zero MSTs, this issue may occur.\n\nThe best workaround is to upgrade to a release which has the fix for this issue. As long as the newer version of EOS that is being upgraded to has the fix, this bug will not be hit.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 762981, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Switch may silently drop control plane forwarded traffic after Strata-Linecard forwarding plane agent restart.', 'alertNote': 'Switch may silently drop control plane forwarded traffic after Strata-Linecard forwarding plane agent restart', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.8', '4.29.4', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1700784000, 'releaseNote': 'Switch may silently drop control plane forwarded traffic after Strata-Linecard forwarding plane agent restart', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident3X4'}]]}, {'bugId': 763570, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'ConfigAgent may not be able to accept new CLI connections if an exception happens very early when a CLI connection is initialized. All new CLI connections will enter standalone mode. Please check Release Notes for further details.', 'alertNote': 'ConfigAgent may not be able to accept new CLI connections if an exception happens very early when a CLI connection is initialized. All new CLI connections will enter standalone mode. When this happens, run the "agent ConfigAgent terminate" command to restart the ConfigAgent.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.11', '4.27.10', '4.28.7', '4.29.5', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 23, 'lastBiteTime': 1784601406, 'exportedTime': 1704844800, 'releaseNote': 'ConfigAgent may not be able to accept new CLI connections if an exception happens very early when a CLI connection is initialized. All new CLI connections will enter standalone mode. When this happens, run the "agent ConfigAgent terminate" command to restart the ConfigAgent.'}, {'bugId': 763856, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'BGP IPv4 routes received in IP-VRF are not advertised to remote domain EVPN peers as EVPN IP-Prefix routes. The workaround is to configure a static route in the VRF and configure `redistribute static` under the VRF.', 'alertNote': 'BGP IPv4 routes received in IP-VRF are not advertised to remote domain EVPN peers as EVPN IP-Prefix routes.\n\nThe workaround is to configure a static route in the VRF and configure `redistribute static` under the VRF.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.26.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.9', '4.28.6', '4.29.3', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1729921291, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'BGP IPv4 routes received in IP-VRF are not advertised to remote domain EVPN peers as EVPN IP-Prefix routes.\n\nThe workaround is to configure a static route in the VRF and configure `redistribute static` under the VRF.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 764777, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': 'https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/17240-security-advisory-0085', 'cve': 'CVE-2023-24513', 'hotfixIds': [34, 37, 38, 39], 'alertSummary': 'On affected Arista CloudEOS a size check bypass issue in the Software Forwarding Engine (Sfe) may allow buffer over reads in later code.', 'alertNote': 'Security Advisory 85 for CVE-2023-24513. \nSee https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/17240-security-advisory-0085 for more details.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.10', '4.27.9', '4.28.6', '4.29.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Security Advisory 85 for CVE-2023-24513. \nSee https://www.arista.com/e