duced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.9', '4.31.6', '4.32.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1668707435, 'exportedTime': 1731888000, 'releaseNote': 'Unknown multicast traffic that is software forwarded via the CPU bypasses the VLAN membership check in the hardware causing these packets to be sent with wrong VLAN tags on the interfaces that are not a member of the VLAN. This condition will recover once the multicast forwarding tables are populated by the software. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'multicastEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Trident3'}, {'tag': 'TrunkEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 765840, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'SandFap/SandFapNi agents may restart with syslog FAP_ISOLATED if a line card gets inserted with power disabled and power is enabled more than10 later', 'alertNote': 'SandFap/SandFapNi agents may restart with syslog FAP_ISOLATED if a line card gets inserted with power disabled and power is enabled more than10 later.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.9', '4.30.1'], 'bites': 7, 'lastBiteTime': 1711096425, 'exportedTime': 1703116800, 'releaseNote': 'SandFap/SandFapNi agents may restart with syslog FAP_ISOLATED if a line card gets inserted with power disabled and power is enabled more than10 later.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}]]}, {'bugId': 765936, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'KernelFib process can constantly consume high CPU even when rest of the system is idle and there is no route churn. Restarting the process will recover the setup.', 'alertNote': 'KernelFib process can constantly consume high CPU even when rest of the system is idle and there is no route churn. Restarting the process will recover the setup.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.10', '4.28.7', '4.29.4', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1755357934, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'KernelFib process can constantly consume high CPU even when rest of the system is idle and there is no route churn. Restarting the process will recover the setup.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}], [{'tag': 'RibModel'}]]}, {'bugId': 765974, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a scaled environment under BGP route churn, it may be possible that stale state is retained improperly in the BgpCliHelper agent, resulting in leaked memory. ', 'alertNote': 'In a scaled environment under BGP route churn, it may be possible that stale state is retained improperly in the BgpCliHelper agent, resulting in leaked memory. \n\nTo workaround this issue, the offending optimization can be disabled by configuring "neighbor default index routes peer disabled" under "router bgp".', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.11', '4.28.8', '4.29.4', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1765528094, 'exportedTime': 1703116800, 'releaseNote': 'In a scaled environment under BGP route churn, it may be possible that stale state is retained improperly in the BgpCliHelper agent, resulting in leaked memory. \n\nTo workaround this issue, the offending optimization can be disabled by configuring "neighbor default index routes peer disabled" under "router bgp".', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 766687, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Front and rear sensors have been removed from "show system environment temperature"', 'alertNote': 'Front and rear sensors have been removed from "show system environment temperature"', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.10', '4.29.6', '4.30.5', '4.31.2'], 'bites': 14, 'lastBiteTime': 1790759407, 'exportedTime': 1728000000, 'releaseNote': 'Front and rear sensors have been removed from "show system environment temperature"', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7300X'}]]}, {'bugId': 767011, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The MCS agent might restart after multiple addSenders POST requests for the same senders that exist in the setup.', 'alertNote': 'The MCS agent might restart when sending notifications after processing multiple POST delSenders and delReceivers requests.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.9', '4.31.6', '4.32.4', '4.33.1'], 'bites': 7, 'lastBiteTime': 1770193640, 'exportedTime': 1763596800, 'releaseNote': 'The MCS agent might restart when sending notifications after processing multiple POST delSenders and delReceivers requests.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'MCSServiceEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 767089, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may restart unexpectedly shortly after connecting to CloudVision or receiving a gNMI Subscribe request with the following text in its log file: 'fatal error: concurrent map read and map write'", 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may restart unexpectedly shortly after connecting to CloudVision or receiving a gNMI Subscribe request with the following text in its log file: "fatal error: concurrent map read and map write".', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.25.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.25.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1784160000, 'releaseNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may restart unexpectedly shortly after connecting to CloudVision or receiving a gNMI Subscribe request with the following text in its log file: "fatal error: concurrent map read and map write".'}, {'bugId': 767275, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'LOC and RDI might be in unexpected state.', 'alertNote': 'LOC and RDI might be in unexpected state.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.7', '4.29.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'LOC and RDI might be in unexpected state.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Jericho2CPlus'}]]}, {'bugId': 767306, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Issuing a NETCONF <lock> RPC on the running datastore will cause subsequent NETCONF <commit> RPC to run into the error "Unable to run this command (configuration is locked by another session)".', 'alertNote': 'Issuing a NETCONF <lock> RPC on the running datastore will cause subsequent NETCONF <commit> RPC to run into the error "Unable to run this command (configuration is locked by another session)".\n\nThere are two possible workarounds:\n1) If the priority is locking out other config changes, then customers can issue NETCONF <lock> RPC on the running datastore and apply the NETCONF <edit-config> RPC to the running datastore directly. The feature lost in this workaround is that the customer can no longer stage config changes in the candidate datastore and then issue a NETCONF <commit> RPC to commit them at a later time.\n2) If the priority is to stage changes in the candidate datastore, then customers can issue NETCONF <lock> RPC on the candidate datastore and apply the NETCONF <edit-config> RPC to the candidate datastore to stage config changes. Then at a later time, they can issue a NETCONF <commit> RPC to apply all of their staged changes to the running datastore at once. The feature lost in this workaround is that the customer can no longer lock out any config change to the running datastore.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.26.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.10', '4.28.7', '4.29.3', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1673478210, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Issuing a NETCONF <lock> RPC on the running datastore will cause subsequent NETCONF <commit> RPC to run into the error "Unable to run this command (configuration is locked by another session)".\n\nThere are two possible workarounds:\n1) If the priority is locking out other config changes, then customers can issue NETCONF <lock> RPC on the running datastore and apply the NETCONF <edit-config> RPC to the running datastore directly. The feature lost in this workaround is that the customer can no longer stage config changes in the candidate datastore and then issue a NETCONF <commit> RPC to commit them at a later time.\n2) If the priority is to stage changes in the candidate datastore, then customers can issue NETCONF <lock> RPC on the candidate datastore and apply the NETCONF <edit-config> RPC to the candidate datastore to stage config changes. Then at a later time, they can issue a NETCONF <commit> RPC to apply all of their staged changes to the running datastore at once. The feature lost in this workaround is that the customer can no longer lock out any config change to the running datastore.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'netconfenabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 767559, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'NVGRE packets that match a GRE tunnel will lead to DchUnreachable drops', 'alertNote': 'NVGRE packets that match a GRE tunnel will lead to DchUnreachable drops', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.10.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.9', '4.28.7', '4.29.3', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1705237388, 'exportedTime': 1783036800, 'releaseNote': 'NVGRE packets that match a GRE tunnel will lead to DchUnreachable drops', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'GreEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Jericho'}]]}, {'bugId': 768372, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A short AC input power outage of 10ms may cause the links to go down permanently with the Strata-FixedSystem agent crashing repeatedly. Reloading the system is required to recover from this failure.', 'alertNote': 'A short AC input power outage of 10ms may cause the links to go down permanently with the Strata-FixedSystem agent crashing repeatedly. Reloading the system is required to recover from this failure.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.1']