 redistributed BGP routes undergo IAR amid churn.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'OspfDefOriginal'}], [{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'OspfRedistBGP'}]]}, {'bugId': 790428, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The "session limit" command under "management accounts" mode does not take effect if its loaded from startup-config', 'alertNote': 'The "session limit" command under "management accounts" mode does not take effect if it\'s loaded from startup-config.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.20.5'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.4', '4.30.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1679360291, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'The "session limit" command under "management accounts" mode does not take effect if it\'s loaded from startup-config.'}, {'bugId': 790579, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': 'CVE-2023-28450', 'alertSummary': 'The dnsmasq version EOS ships with is susceptible to CVE-2023-28450. The workaround is to not use the external proxying feature to prevent the processing of untrusted DNS queries', 'alertNote': 'The dnsmasq version EOS ships with is susceptible to CVE-2023-28450.\n\nThe workaround is to not use the external proxying feature to prevent the processing of untrusted DNS queries.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.11', '4.27.11', '4.28.8', '4.29.4', '4.30.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'The dnsmasq version EOS ships with is susceptible to CVE-2023-28450.\n\nThe workaround is to not use the external proxying feature to prevent the processing of untrusted DNS queries.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dnsProxyEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 791285, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'VRRP acts as master on both sides when we remove the VRF from the interface on the configure session', 'alertNote': 'When changing a VRF on an interface with VRRP configured through a configure session and no virtual or physical IP addresses were modified, the VRRP instances might end up in a master/master scenario. The workaround is to flap the interface or VRRP groups after configure session has applied the new VRF.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.8', '4.29.4', '4.30.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1678518164, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'When changing a VRF on an interface with VRRP configured through a configure session and no virtual or physical IP addresses were modified, the VRRP instances might end up in a master/master scenario. The workaround is to flap the interface or VRRP groups after configure session has applied the new VRF.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}, {'tag': 'VRRPEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 791371, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'After a CCT run on the AP, AP is unable to redirect wireless clients to the portal URL.', 'alertNote': 'After a CCT run on the AP, AP is unable to redirect wireless clients to the portal URL.\n', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['wm.v13.0.0-67-vv10'], 'versionFixed': ['wm-v16.0.0-214-vv1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1687467535, 'exportedTime': 1736467200, 'releaseNote': 'After a CCT run on the AP, AP is unable to redirect wireless clients to the portal URL.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'WifiAPs'}]]}, {'bugId': 791543, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'VXLAN encapsulated IPv6 Neighbor Discovery protocol packets are replicated to the fabric kernel interface. This makes VXLAN IPv6 ND suppression feature not work properly', 'alertNote': 'VXLAN encapsulated IPv6 Neighbor Discovery protocol packets are replicated to the fabric kernel interface. This makes VXLAN IPv6 ND suppression feature not work properly. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.4', '4.30.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1722501599, 'exportedTime': 1739404800, 'releaseNote': 'VXLAN encapsulated IPv6 Neighbor Discovery protocol packets are replicated to the fabric kernel interface. This makes VXLAN IPv6 ND suppression feature not work properly. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}, {'tag': 'VxlanControllerClientndproxy'}]]}, {'bugId': 792302, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'heThe SandAcl agent may restart unexpectedly when applying a Tap Aggregation service policy to an interface while there are 31 or more other Tap Aggregation policies programmed on interfaces on the same forwarding chip.', 'alertNote': 'The SandAcl agent may restart unexpectedly when applying a Tap Aggregation service policy to an interface while there are 31 or more other Tap Aggregation policies programmed on interfaces on the same forwarding chip.\n\nThe work around is to add "port qualifier size 6 bits" to each of the Tap Aggregation steering feature which are in use in a custom TCAM profile, e.g. "feature tapagg ip", "feature tapagg ipv6", and "feature tapagg mac". This will allow up to 63 ports to be used.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1718910073, 'exportedTime': 1728604800, 'releaseNote': 'The SandAcl agent may restart unexpectedly when applying a Tap Aggregation service policy to an interface while there are 31 or more other Tap Aggregation policies programmed on interfaces on the same forwarding chip.\n\nThe work around is to add "port qualifier size 6 bits" to each of the Tap Aggregation steering feature which are in use in a custom TCAM profile, e.g. "feature tapagg ip", "feature tapagg ipv6", and "feature tapagg mac". This will allow up to 63 ports to be used.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}, {'tag': 'tapaggEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 792500, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Groups of four adjacent BASE-T ports in the range Et1-Et24 share a common hardware resource; for eg, Et1-Et4 and Et5-Et8 etc. Due to an issue with the shared hardware resource, all 4 ports may fail to link up, even if the link partners report a linkup.', 'alertNote': 'Groups of four adjacent BASE-T ports in the range Et1-Et24 share a common hardware resource; for example, Et1-Et4 and Et5-Et8 and so on. Due to an issue with the shared hardware resource, all 4 ports may fail to link up, even if the link partners report a linkup.\n\nOn fixed systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident reset`. On modular systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident <linecard> reset` on the affected linecard.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1735890139, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Groups of four adjacent BASE-T ports in the range Et1-Et24 share a common hardware resource; for example, Et1-Et4 and Et5-Et8 and so on. Due to an issue with the shared hardware resource, all 4 ports may fail to link up, even if the link partners report a linkup.\n\nOn fixed systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident reset`. On modular systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident <linecard> reset` on the affected linecard.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7010TX-48'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-722XPM-48Y4'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7010TX-48-DC'}]]}, {'bugId': 792506, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "Groups of four adjacent BASE-T ports share a common hardware resource, if there's an issue with the hardware resource, all 4 ports may fail to link up, even if the link partners report a linkup", 'alertNote': 'Groups of four adjacent BASE-T ports in the range Et1-Et24 share a common hardware resource; for example, Et1-Et4 and Et5-Et8 and so on. Due to an issue with the shared hardware resource, all 4 ports may fail to link up, even if the link partners report a linkup.\n\nOn EOS versions prior to 4.29.0F, on fixed systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident reset`; on modular systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident <linecard> reset` on the affected linecard. On EOS versions 4.29.0F and onwards, the workaround is to run `reset platform trident phy interface INTF pcs` on one of the affected interfaces.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.10', '4.30.8', '4.31.4', '4.32.2'], 'bites': 12, 'lastBiteTime': 1792037743, 'exportedTime': 1721952000, 'releaseNote': 'Groups of four adjacent BASE-T ports in the range Et1-Et24 share a common hardware resource; for example, Et1-Et4 and Et5-Et8 and so on. Due to an issue with the shared hardware resource, all 4 ports may fail to link up, even if the link partners report a linkup.\n\nOn EOS versions prior to 4.29.0F, on fixed systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident reset`; on modular systems, the workaround is to run `platform trident <linecard> reset` on the affected linecard. On EOS versions 4.29.0F and onwards, the workaround is to run `reset platform trident phy interface INTF pcs` on one of the affected interfaces.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Strata'}]]}, {'bugId': 792656, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In an EVPN VXLAN IRB deployment, a remote ARP (or IPv6 neighbor) entry learned over EVPN might not be installed', 'alertNote': 'After a disruptive SandL3Unicast agent restart, "show platform fap vxlan vtep\nencapsulation" command may show invalid tunnel entries with 0.0.0.0 as\ndestination IP.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.30.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.5', '4.31.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1703116800, 'releaseNote': 'After a disruptive SandL3Unicast agent restart, "show platform fap vxlan vtep\nencapsulation" command may show invalid tunnel entries with 0.0.0.0 as\ndestination IP.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnVxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 792987, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'VRF names with `.` result in repeated restart of the Launcher agent while starting a process with a name like `Rib-vrf-foo.bar`.', 'alertNote': 'VRF names with "." result in repeated restart of the Launcher agent while starting a process with a name like "Rib-vrf-foo.bar". \n\nTo restore the system, first remove the VRF with "." in its name with "no vrf instance <vrf.name>". Then, delete any file in /etc/ProcMgr.d/run/ownedByLauncher/ of the form "<agent>-vrf.<vrf.name>". For an example VRF named "foo.bar", the file to delete might be "Rib-vrf.foo.bar" or, when using the multi-agent routing protocol model, a file for a protocol-specific agent such as "Ospf-vrf.foo.bar" or "Isis-vrf.foo.bar".', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.2'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1763410957, 'exportedTime': 1754092800, 'releaseNote': 'VRF names with "." result in repeated restart of the Launcher agent while starting a process with a name like "Rib-vrf-foo.bar". \n\nTo restore the system, first remove the VRF with "." in its name with "no vrf instance <vrf.name>". Then, delete any file in /etc/ProcMgr.d/run/ownedByLauncher/ of the form "<agent>-vrf.<vrf.name>". For an example VRF named "foo.bar", the file to delete might be "Rib-vrf.foo.bar" or, when using the multi-agent routing protocol model, a file for a protocol-specific agent such as "Ospf-vrf.foo.bar" or "Isis-vrf.foo.bar".', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'RibModel'}, {'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 793377, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In the SandAcl agent, there is a memory leak when TCAM entries are deleted. A workaround would be to restart the agent.', 'alertNote': 'In the SandAcl agent, there is a memory leak when TCAM entries  are deleted.\n\nA workaround would be to restart the agent.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1688194221, 'exportedTime': 1700784000, 'releaseNote': 'In the SandAcl agent, there is a memory leak when TCAM entries  are deleted.\n\nA workaround would be to restart the agent.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}]]}, {'bugId': 793494, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'LedPolicy agent memory use grows over time. This may lead to an out-of-memory condition and other agents being restarted. The workaround is to configure the switch with "agent LedPolicy shutdown". ', 'alertNote': "LedPolicy agent's memory use grows over time. This may lead to an out-of-memory condition and other agents being restarted.\nThe workaround is to configure the switch with `agent LedPolicy shutdown`. This will prevent the LedPolicy agent from running and will prevent the increasing memory usage, but system LEDs will stop updating as a result.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2', '4.29.2FX-CB'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.3', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1787339971, 'exportedTime': 1727136000, 'releaseNote': "LedPolicy agent's memory use grows over time. This may lead to an out-of-memory condition and other agents being restarted.\nThe workaround is to configure the switch with `agent LedPolicy shutdown`. This will prevent the LedPolicy agent from running and will prevent the increasing memory usage, but system LEDs will stop updating as a result.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CCS-720DP'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720DT'}], [{'tag': 'AWE-5000'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-710P'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720DF'}]]}, {'bugId': 793936, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'DHCP unicast packets over MLAG peer link may be dropped with "mlag peer-link requests disabled" configured restricting DHCP OFFER/ACK packets from DHCP server to reach intended DHCP relay agent', 'alertNote': "DHCP unicast packets over MLAG peer link may be dropped with 'mlag peer-link requests disabled' configured restricting DHCP OFFER/ACK packets from DHCP server to reach intended DHCP relay agent", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.7', '4.29.4', '4.30.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1675713359, 'exportedTime': 1731888000, 'releaseNote': "DHCP unicast packets over MLAG peer link may be dropped with 'mlag peer-link requests disabled' configured restricting DHCP OFFER/ACK packets from DHCP server to reach intended DHCP relay agent", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dhcpRelayConfigured'}, {'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Mlagpeerlinkreqdisabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 794205, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Under high loads, EVPN Type 2 MAC-only routes may not be advertised to peers despite being locally learned. Learning a new MAC entry in the VLAN or terminating the BGP agent fixes this and triggers the missing routes to be advertised over EVPN.', 'alertNote': 'EVPN Type 2 MAC only routes may not be advertised to EVPN peers despite these MAC addresses being locally learnt.  This may happen if the system is under high loads during route redistribution.\nLearning a new MAC entry in the VLAN fixes the problem and triggers the missing routes to be advertised over EVPN. Alternatively, BGP agent could be terminated to fix this issue.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.10', '4.29.6', '4.30.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1711646542, 'exportedTime': 1719360000, 'releaseNote': 'EVPN Type 2 MAC only routes may not be advertised to EVPN peers despite these MAC addresses being locally learnt.  This may happen if the system is under high loads during route redistribution.\nLearning a new MAC entry in the VLAN fixes the problem and triggers the missing routes to be advertised over EVPN. Alternatively, BGP agent could be terminated to fix this issue.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 794347, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Routes redistributed into BGP using `network` command do not redistribute the tag. To workaround this issue, instead of using `network` command, use `redistribute` command.', 'alertNote': "Routes redistributed into BGP using 'network' command do not redistribute the tag.\nTo workaround this issue, instead of using 'network' command, use 'redistribute' command.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1718661037, 'exportedTime': 1761177600, 'releaseNote': "Routes redistributed into BGP using 'network' command do not redistribute the tag.\nTo workaround this issue, instead of using 'network' command, use 'redistribute' command.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 794372, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The BessMgr agent might crash while performing software-forwarding of multicast data packets. The likelihood of encountering this problem increases as the number of outgoing interfaces in the multicast route grows.', 'alertNote': 'The BessMgr agent might crash while performing software-forwarding of multicast data packets. The likelihood of encountering this problem increases as the number of outgoing interfaces in the multicast route grows.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.30.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.6', '4.31.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1729223522, 'exportedTime': 1742947200, 'releaseNote': 'The BessMgr agent might crash while performing software-forwarding of multicast data packets. The likelihood of encountering this problem increases as the number of outgoing interfaces in the multicast route grows.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'multicastEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 795104, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': 'CVE-2023-0464', 'alertSummary': 'AP is vulnerable to CVE-2023-0464.', 'alertNote': 'AP is vulnerable to CVE-2023-0464.', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['mwm-v1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['wm-v16.0.0-214-vv1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1704844800, 'releaseNote':