 prefix lists, communtiy lists, as path lists, sub route-maps etc) until the route map config is changed. Route maps will also ignore any updates to the sub route-map names associated with any of its clauses.\n\nWorkaround: After any change to the SR label range is made, make a direct change to the route map. e.g. Add and removing a deny all route map statement with a very large sequence number.\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.12', '4.28.10', '4.29.6', '4.30.4', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1739302621, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': "If the SR label range is changed, route maps without any 'set segment-index' rules will ignore updates to referenced policy constructs (such as prefix lists, communtiy lists, as path lists, sub route-maps etc) until the route map config is changed. Route maps will also ignore any updates to the sub route-map names associated with any of its clauses.\n\nWorkaround: After any change to the SR label range is made, make a direct change to the route map. e.g. Add and removing a deny all route map statement with a very large sequence number.\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 824297, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On multichip systems, reload may cause VLAN traffic-policy rules tonot be reprogrammed across all chips.', 'alertNote': 'On multichip systems, reload may cause VLAN traffic-policy rules to not be reprogrammed across all chips. Workaround would be to reconfigure the VLAN traffic-policy rule.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'On multichip systems, reload may cause VLAN traffic-policy rules to not be reprogrammed across all chips. Workaround would be to reconfigure the VLAN traffic-policy rule.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'modular'}, {'tag': 'Trident3'}]]}, {'bugId': 824839, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Changing VXLAN source-interface under "interface vxlan" may not take effect resulting in sending the VXLAN encapsulated packets with an incorrect source IP address. Workaround is to flap the VXLAN interface.', 'alertNote': 'Changing VXLAN source-interface under "interface vxlan" may not take effect resulting in sending the VXLAN encapsulated packets with incorrect source IP address. Workaround is to flap the VXLAN interface.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.7', '4.30.5', '4.31.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1707291619, 'exportedTime': 1738108800, 'releaseNote': 'Changing VXLAN source-interface under "interface vxlan" may not take effect resulting in sending the VXLAN encapsulated packets with incorrect source IP address. Workaround is to flap the VXLAN interface.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Tomahawk4'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 825596, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Continuously restarting agents many times can rarely cause continuous restarts. Workaround: reload the device.', 'alertNote': 'Continuously restarting agents many times can rarely cause continuous restarts.\nWorkaround: reload the device.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.12', '4.28.9', '4.29.6', '4.30.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Continuously restarting agents many times can rarely cause continuous restarts.\nWorkaround: reload the device.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Strata'}]]}, {'bugId': 826013, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a EVPN VXLAN deployment, using configuration replace migrate a MLAG pair into an EVPN All-Active Multihoming model can result in multicast and broadcast traffic from edge to be duplicated towards the core. The workaround is to reload the devices.', 'alertNote': 'In a EVPN VXLAN 