Note': 'AP gets rebooted multiple times because the packet reception is stuck on its radio.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'WifiAPs'}]]}, {'bugId': 834453, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If linerate traffic is sent too soon after SandFapNi agent warm up it may cause packet loss if the fabric side has not fully warmed up.', 'alertNote': 'If linerate traffic is sent too soon after SandFapNi agent warm up it may cause packet loss if the fabric side has not fully warmed up.\n\nPlease confirm "show platform sand fabric monitor capacity" displays that monitored fabric capacity threshold over fap capacity is at or over 100%.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1743113833, 'exportedTime': 1725840000, 'releaseNote': 'If linerate traffic is sent too soon after SandFapNi agent warm up it may cause packet loss if the fabric side has not fully warmed up.\n\nPlease confirm "show platform sand fabric monitor capacity" displays that monitored fabric capacity threshold over fap capacity is at or over 100%.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Jericho2CPlus'}]]}, {'bugId': 834496, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Configuration changes with MLAG port-channels may lead to no MAC addresses being learnt. Workaround is to flap the port-channel interface.', 'alertNote': 'Configuration changes with MLAG port-channels may lead to no MAC addresses being learnt.\n\nWorkaround is to flap add and remove the port-channel from the VLAN.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.12', '4.28.10', '4.29.6', '4.30.4', '4.31.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1701754635, 'exportedTime': 1700784000, 'releaseNote': 'Configuration changes with MLAG port-channels may lead to no MAC addresses being learnt.\n\nWorkaround is to flap add and remove the port-channel from the VLAN.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Strata