Summary': 'MLAG peer will not forward traffic over the peer link if the MLAG-portchannel is shut down after the switch is started or reloaded.', 'alertNote': 'MLAG peer will not forward traffic over the peer link if the MLAG-port channel is shut down after the switch is started or reloaded.\n\nWorkaround:\nBring up the affected MLAG-port channel, can be shut down again afterwards.\n\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.9', '4.29.5', '4.30.1.1', '4.30.4', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1736269961, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'MLAG peer will not forward traffic over the peer link if the MLAG-port channel is shut down after the switch is started or reloaded.\n\nWorkaround:\nBring up the affected MLAG-port channel, can be shut down again afterwards.\n\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Trident4'}]]}, {'bugId': 836192, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': ' When OSPF is configured with multiple unnumbered interfaces connected to the same neighbor, packet drops may occur.', 'alertNote': 'When OSPF is configured with multiple unnumbered interfaces connected to the same neighbor, packet drops may occur.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.9', '4.29.5', '4.30.4', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1689276675, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'When OSPF is configured with multiple unnumbered interfaces connected to the same neighbor, packet drops may occur.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ospfEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'ospfV3Enabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 836252, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If the loma400Cpld is reprogrammed at boot time, the system may not fully initialize Workaround: Reload the switch', 'alertNote': 'If the loma400Cpld is reprogrammed at boot time, the system may not fully initialize\nWorkaround: Reload the switch', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.30.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.5', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'If the loma400Cpld is reprogrammed at boot time, the system may not fully initialize\nWorkaround: Reload the switch', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7050CX4-24D8'}]]}, {'bugId': 836750, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If internal loopback is being used for TX mirroring to CPU, the packets are sometimes unexpectedly re-sent to the loopback causing a packet storm on the lo interface. It consumes a lot of the processing time affecting normal forwarding.', 'alertNote': "When the internal loopback is being used for TX mirroring to CPU, the packets are sometimes unexpectedly re-sent back into the loopback causing a packet storm on the loopback interface. This storm consumes a large amount of the forwarding chip's processing power which can interfere with normal forwarding.\n\nOther symptoms include (but not limited to): MACs learning happening on unexpected ports (which may manifest as frequent MAC relearns), traffic loops, and traffic drops.\n\nWorkaround: Configure a dedicated recirculation channel for CPU mirroring on an unused interface before configuring mirror to CPU.  Note: The interface must NOT be shutdown, and the recirculation interface must be configured before configuring the mirroring session.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.6', '4.30.4', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 26, 'lastBiteTime': 1792993649, 'exportedTime': 1714435200, 'releaseNote': "When the internal loopback is being used for TX mirroring to CPU, the packets are sometimes unexpectedly re-sent back into the loopback causing a packet storm on the loopback interface. This storm consumes a large amount of the forwarding chip's processing power which can interfere with normal forwarding.\n\nOther symptoms include (but not limited to): MACs learning happening on unexpected ports (which may manifest as frequent MAC relearns), traffic loops, and traffic drops.\n\nWorkaround: Configure a dedicated recirculation channel for CPU mirroring on an unused interface before configuring mirror to CPU.  Note: The interface must NOT be shutdown, and the recirculation interface must be configured before configuring the mirroring session.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident3'}]]}, {'bugId': 836920, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'MACsec enabled interface at 400G may occasionally transmit corrupted packets with FCS-Error. A temporary workaround is to decrease the MAC TX FIFO through the following command:hardware phy cms et<lc>/<port>/1 diag mac line write 8 9.', 'alertNote': 'MACsec enabled interface at 400G may occasionally transmit corrupted packets with FCS-Error.  A temporary workaround is to decrease the MAC TX FIFO through the following command: "hardware phy cms et<lc>/<port>/1 diag mac line write 8 9".  However, this workaround doesn\'t survive agent restart or changes in the interface speed.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.26.12', '4.27.12', '4.28.9', '4.29.5', '4.30.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1688722403, 'exportedTime': 1704844800, 'releaseNote': 'MACsec enabled interface at 400G may occasionally transmit corrupted packets with FCS-Error.  A temporary workaround is to decrease the MAC TX FIFO through the following command: "hardware phy cms et<lc>/<port>/1 diag mac line write 8 9".  However, this workaround doesn\'t survive agent restart or changes in the interface speed.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7388'}, {'tag': 'MacsecEnabled'}], [{'tag': '7800R3K-36DM-LC'}, {'tag': 'MacsecEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 837177, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The ambient temperature reported by the system may be higher than the actual ambient temperature at low fan speeds', 'alertNote': 'The ambient temperature reported by the system may be higher than the actual ambient temperature at low fan speeds', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.30.5', '4.31.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1752953730, 'exportedTime': 1761264000, 'releaseNote': 'The ambient temperature reported by the system may be higher than the actual ambient temperature at low fan speeds', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7010TX-48C-DC'}]]}, {'bugId': 839987, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If Port Security and 802.1X are configured on an interface with supplicants authenticated on the interface, post SSU, it is seen that the supplicants are logged off and are made to re-authenticate post SSU.', 'alertNote': 'If Port Security and 802.1X are configured on an interface with supplicants authenticated on the interface, post SSU, it is seen that the supplicants are logged off and are made to re-authenticate resulting in traffic loss for such supplicants. A workaround to avoid this traffic loss would be to disable portsec on the interface.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.11', '4.29.7', '4.30.5', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1740528000, 'releaseNote': 'If Port Security and 802.1X are configured on an interface with supplicants authenticated on the interface, post SSU, it is seen that the supplicants are logged off and are made to re-authenticate resulting in traffic loss for such supplicants. A workaround to avoid this traffic loss would be to disable portsec on the interface.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dot1xMacBasedAuthAlways'}]]}, {'bugId': 840024, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': '2.5GBASE-T ports configured with `speed auto 100full`/`no speed` and linked up at 100M speed may fail to pass traffic after an SSU reload if they link down while the SSU reload is in progress, and come back up after the SSU reload is complete. ', 'alertNote': '2.5GBASE-T ports configured with `speed auto 100full`/`no speed` configurations and linked up at 100M speed may fail to pass traffic after an SSU reload (i.e. reload fast-boot) if they link down while the SSU reload is in progress, and come back up after the SSU reload is complete.\n\nWorkaround is to run `shutdown` followed by a `no shutdown` on the affected interfaces. The issue can also be avoided by configuring the susceptible interfaces with `speed forced 100full` configuration prior to the SSU reload. Please note that the configuration change will flap the interfaces.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1780099200, 'releaseNote': '2.5GBASE-T ports configured with `speed auto 100full`/`no speed` configurations and linked up at 100M speed may fail to pass traffic after an SSU reload (i.e. reload fast-boot) if they link down while the SSU reload is in progress, and come back up after the SSU reload is complete.\n\nWorkaround is to run `shutdown` followed by a `no shutdown` on the affected interfaces. The issue can also be avoided by configuring the susceptible interfaces with `speed forced 100full` configuration prior to the SSU reload. Please note that the configuration change will flap the interfaces.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CCS-720XP-48ZC2'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720XP-24ZY4'}]]}, {'bugId': 840624, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'With the scale of VXLAN VLANs and flood VTEPs, churn in flood VTEP list may result in exhaustion of replication group used for flooding. Workaround is to flap the VXLAN interface.', 'alertNote': 'With the scale of VXLAN VLANs and flood VTEPs, churn in flood VTEP list may result in exhaustion of replication group used for flooding. Workaround is to flap the VXLAN interface.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.7', '4.32.4', '4.33.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1747896228, 'exportedTime': 1753660800, 'releaseNote': 'With the scale of VXLAN VLANs and flood VTEPs, churn in flood VTEP list may result in exhaustion of replication group used for flooding. Workaround is to flap the VXLAN interface.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Tomahawk4'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 840871, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Multiple restarts of platform forwarding agents, e.g. Strata-FixedSystem, Strata-Linecard, SandFap-FixedSystem, SandFapNi-Linecard, etc., can result in an out of memory condition. To recover from this situation, power cycle the switch.', 'alertNote': 'Multiple restarts of platform forwarding agents, e.g. Strata-FixedSystem, Strata-Linecard, SandFap-FixedSystem, SandFapNi-Linecard, etc., can result in an out of memory condition.\n\nTo recover from this situation, power cycle the switch.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.4', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1759150741, 'exportedTime': 1698105600, 'releaseNote': 'Multiple restarts of platform forwarding agents, e.g. Strata-FixedSystem, Strata-Linecard, SandFap-FixedSystem, SandFapNi-Linecard, etc., can result in an out of memory condition.\n\nTo recover from this situation, power cycle the switch.'}, {'bugId': 840967, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If multiple VRFs are active route counts for Static, Route input, BGP, Connected, VRF leak and GRIBI in "show rib route summary brief" and "show rib route summary vrf <VRF-name>" commands may be inaccurate.', 'alertNote': 'If multiple VRFs are active route counts for Static, Route input, BGP, Connected, VRF leak and GRIBI in "show rib route summary brief" and "show rib route summary vrf <VRF-name>" commands may be inaccurate.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.7', '4.30.6', '4.31.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1690312259, 'exportedTime': 1712620800, 'releaseNote': 'If multiple VRFs are active