aseNote': 'AP would slowly leak memory while handling proc filesystem read and writes.'}, {'bugId': 848542, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On devices running EVPN multicast OISM, when a PIM External Gateway ( PEG) device is configured as RP, receivers in the external network that join the EVPN network via the PEG-nonDR RP may experience traffic loss.', 'alertNote': 'On devices running EVPN multicast OISM, when a PIM External Gateway ( PEG) device is configured as RP,  receivers in the external network that join the EVPN network via the PEG-nonDR RP may experience traffic loss. \n\n`clear  pim ipvX vrf <VRF> sparse-mode route <S> <G> ` on the PEG-non-DR will recover the flow. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1783468800, 'releaseNote': 'On devices running EVPN multicast OISM, when a PIM External Gateway ( PEG) device is configured as RP,  receivers in the external network that join the EVPN network via the PEG-nonDR RP may experience traffic loss. \n\n`clear  pim ipvX vrf <VRF> sparse-mode route <S> <G> ` on the PEG-non-DR will recover the flow. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnMulticast'}]]}, {'bugId': 848837, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may stop streaming to CloudVision upon reading unexpected data for a Smash path.', 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may stop streaming to CloudVision upon reading unexpected data for a Smash path.', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v0.1'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.28.1', 'TerminAttr-v1.29.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1696468855, 'exportedTime': 1784160000, 'releaseNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may stop streaming to CloudVision upon reading unexpected data for a Smash path.'}, {'bugId': 849796, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The EpniAlignerError counter may be incremented in non-adverse scenarios. As a workaround, to determine whether there is an adverse condition, run the command `show platform fap counters | grep AlignerCrcError`.', 'alertNote': 'The EpniAlignerError counter may be incremented in non-adverse scenarios, including but not limited to the following:\n\nSplit horizon drops\nMTU violating packets\nThe `show forwarding destination` command\nMPLS ping/traceroute\nEgress VLAN membership check\n\nAs a workaround, to determine whether there is an adverse condition, run the command `show platform fap counters | grep AlignerCrcError`. Any AlignerCrcError entries with a non-zero count indicate an adverse condition.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.7', '4.32.5', '4.33.3', '4.34.0'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1753593224, 'exportedTime': 1743897600, 'releaseNote': 'The EpniAlignerError counter may be incremented in non-adverse scenarios, including but not limited to the following:\n\nSplit horizon drops\nMTU violating packets\nThe `show forwarding destination` command\nMPLS ping/traceroute\nEgress VLAN membership check\n\nAs a workaround, to determine whether there is an adverse condition, run the command `show platform fap counters | grep AlignerCrcError`. Any AlignerCrcError entries with a non-zero count indicate an adverse condition.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}, {'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 850193, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Configuring "traffic-loopback source system device mac" causes the interface to become ineligible for channel-group membership. The workaround is to configure "speed forced 1000full" on the affected interfaces.', 'alertNote': 'Configuring "traffic-loopback source system device mac" causes the interface to become ineligible for channel-group membership. The workaround is to configure "speed forced 1000full" on the affected interfaces.\n\nAffected ports:\n - CCS-722XPM-48Y4: 25-48\n - CCS-720DP-48S: 25-48\n - CCS-710P: 1-12\n - CCS-720DP-24S: 1-24\n - DCS-7010TX-48: 25-48', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1781747821, 'exportedTime': 1728604800, 'releaseNote': 'Configuring "traffic-loopback source system device mac" causes the interface to become ineligible for channel-group membership. The workaround is to configure "speed forced 1000full" on the affected interfaces.\n\nAffected ports:\n - CCS-722XPM-48Y4: 25-48\n - CCS-720DP-48S: 25-48\n - CCS-710P: 1-12\n - CCS-720DP-24S: 1-24\n - DCS-7010TX-48: 25-48', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CCS-720DP'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-722XPM'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7010TX'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-710P'}]]}, {'bugId': 850320, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Commands run from the config CLI are not logged to syslog.', 'alertNote': 'Commands run from the config CLI are not logged to syslog.', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['mwm-v12.0.0-162'], 'versionFixed': ['wm-v16.0.0-214-vv1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1691097025, 'exportedTime': 1736467200, 'releaseNote': 'Commands run from the config CLI are not logged to syslog.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'WifiAPs'}]]}, {'bugId': 850326, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Logs for device access via ssh are not logged to syslog.', 'alertNote': 'Logs for device access via ssh are not logged to syslog.', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['mwm-v8.9.0-63-vv1'], 'versionFixed': ['wm-v16.0.0-214-vv1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1691097025, 'exportedTime': 1712620800, 'releaseNote': 'Logs for device access via ssh are not logged to syslog.'}, {'bugId': 851194, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If a device is trying to auth with 802.1X when simultaneous MBA and EAPOL auth is configured to use dot1x mac-based authentication always,and the RADIUS server is unreachable at this point, disabling MBA auth always cause agent to restart.Please refer RN.', 'alertNote': "If a device is trying to authenticate with 802.1X when simultaneous MBA and EAPOL authentication is configured ('dot1x mac based authentication always') and if the RADIUS server is unreachable at this point, disabling MBA authentication always and flapping the port might cause the Dot1x agent to continuously restart unexpectedly. \nA workaround in case agent restarts are observed, would be to disable 802.1X MBA on the interface and re-enable it.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1706952751, 'exportedTime': 1761696000, 'releaseNote': "If a device is trying to authenticate with 802.1X when simultaneous MBA and EAPOL authentication is configured ('dot1x mac based authentication always') and if the RADIUS server is unreachable at this point, disabling MBA authentication always and flapping the port might cause the Dot1x agent to continuously restart unexpectedly. \nA workaround in case agent restarts are observed, would be to disable 802.1X MBA on the interface and re-enable it.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dot1xMacBasedAuthAlways'}], [{'tag': 'dot1xMBA'}, {'tag': 'Radius'}]]}, {'bugId': 851399, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If a VXLAN inner destination MAC points to a remote VTEP in the MAC table, then receiving VTEP will encapsulate the packet again to the remote VTEP, instead of dropping the packet. This may lead to an L2 packet loop and MAC moves in the network.', 'alertNote': 'After VXLAN tunnel termination, if an inner destination MAC address points to a remote VTEP in MAC table then the receiving VTEP will encapsulate the packet again to the remote VXLAN VTEP, instead of dropping the packet. This may lead to L2 packet loop and MAC moves in the network. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.10', '4.29.6', '4.30.4', '4.31.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1692937382, 'exportedTime': 1738108800, 'releaseNote': 'After VXLAN tunnel termination, if an inner destination MAC address points to a remote VTEP in MAC table then the receiving VTEP will encapsulate the packet again to the remote VXLAN VTEP, instead of dropping the packet. This may lead to L2 packet loop and MAC moves in the network. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Tomahawk4'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 851456, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'After linecard removal and insertion, traffic coming from the peer link may be incorrectly forwarded on MLAG port-channel members instead of filtered out. To recover, restart the Strata agent associated with the linecard', 'alertNote': 'After linecard removal and insertion, traffic coming from the peer link may be incorrectly forwarded on MLAG port-channel members instead of filtered out.\n\nTo recover, restart the Strata agent associated with the linecard.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.11', '4.29.6', '4.30.4', '4.31.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1736397914, 'exportedTime': 1740960000, 'releaseNote': 'After linecard removal and insertion, traffic coming from the peer link may be incorrectly forwarded on MLAG port-channel members instead of filtered out.\n\nTo recover, restart the Strata agent associated with the linecard.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7050X4'}, {'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7358'}, {'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 852119, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'An EAPOL supplicant may fail authentication when the switch sends Access-Requests with a stale value for the State attribute. This may happen when there is a delay in receiving responses from the RADIUS server or from the EAPOL supplicant. ', 'alertNote': 'An EAPOL supplicant may fail authentication when the switch sends Access-Requests with a stale value for the State attribute. This may happen when there is a delay in receiving responses from the RADIUS server or from the EAPOL supplicant.\nThe switch would recover from this state after the authentication failure. If the responses are received quickly then, the supplicant may authenticate successfully. \nIf the delay in responses are expected, a potential workaround for this issue is to increase one of the following timeouts:\n1. "dot1x timeout tx-period <>" to increase the time the switch waits for a supplicant to respond.\nOR\n2. "radius-server timeout <>" to increase the time the switch waits for a server to respond.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1772083733, 'exportedTime': 1779494400, 'releaseNote': 'An EAPOL supplicant may fail authentication when the switch sends Access-Requests with a stale value for the State attribute. This may happen when there is a delay in receiving responses from the RADIUS server or from the EAPOL supplicant.\nThe switch would recover from this state after the authentication failure. If the responses are received quickly then, the supplicant may authenticate successfully. \nIf the delay in responses are expected, a potential workaround for this issue is to increase one of the following timeouts:\n1. "dot1x timeout tx-period <>" to increase the time the switch waits for a supplicant to respond.\nOR\n2. "radius-server timeout <>" to increase the time the switch waits for a server to respond.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 852761, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Fans may spin faster than necessary and Fe sensors may report overheating due to incorrect sensor limits', 'alertNote': 'Fans may spin faster than necessary and Fe sensors may report overheating due to incorrect sensor limits', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.10',