he virtual mac', 'alertNote': 'In a VXLAN IPv6 routing setup using data plane learning, when the SVI is configured using "ipv6 address virtual", an invalid multicast NS packets may get duplicated (sent twice) over VXLAN when the target is the link local address for the virtual mac. There is no such duplication for the valid multicast NS packets. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1713470389, 'exportedTime': 1733097600, 'releaseNote': 'In a VXLAN IPv6 routing setup using data plane learning, when the SVI is configured using "ipv6 address virtual", an invalid multicast NS packets may get duplicated (sent twice) over VXLAN when the target is the link local address for the virtual mac. There is no such duplication for the valid multicast NS packets. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Ipv6Interface'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 857846, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a VXLAN routing setup when either EVPN IPv6 IRB or "vxlan controller-client nd proxy" config is enabled and a SVI is configured with ipv6 address virtual", there may be duplicate proxy Neighbor Advertisement replies.', 'alertNote': 'In a VXLAN routing setup when either EVPN IPv6 IRB or "vxlan controller-client nd proxy" config is enabled and a SVI is configured with  ipv6 address virtual", there may be duplicate proxy Neighbor Advertisement replies to a front panel multicast Neighbor Solicitation for target that is the SVI link local address corresponding to the virtual mac. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.1'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1774974891, 'exportedTime': 1733097600, 'releaseNote': 'In a VXLAN routing setup when either EVPN IPv6 IRB or "vxlan controller-client nd proxy" config is enabled and a SVI is configured with  ipv6 address virtual", there may be duplicate proxy Neighbor Advertisement replies to a front panel multicast Neighbor Solicitation for target that is the SVI link local address corresponding to the virtual mac. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Ipv6Interface'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 858716, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When the egress port mirror-to-cpu feature is enabled on a VXLAN core port, sending packets of certain sizes may result in the some types of CPU-bound traffic getting corrupted, resulting in protocols not converging.', 'alertNote': 'When the egress port mirror-to-cpu feature is enabled on a VXLAN core port, sending packets of certain sizes may result in the some types of CPU-bound traffic getting corrupted, resulting in protocols not converging.\n\nThese VXLAN traffic may also cause parity errors in the egress data buffer of the switch.\n\nAs a workaround, disable all CPU monitoring sessions.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.10', '4.30.9', '4.31.6', '4.32.4', '4.33.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1692937382, 'exportedTime': 1737590400, 'releaseNote': 'When the egress port mirror-to-cpu feature is enabled on a VXLAN core port, sending packets of certain sizes may result in the some types of CPU-bound traffic getting corrupted, resulting in protocols not converging.\n\nThese VXLAN traffic may also cause parity errors in the egress data buffer of the switch.\n\nAs a workaround, disable all CPU monitoring sessions.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7388'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7060X5'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 858900, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'BFD session may flap immediately after corrected DRAM ECC error.', 'alertNote': 'BFD session may flap immediately after corrected DRAM ECC error.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.1'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1745616327, 'exportedTime': 1786406400, 'releaseNote': 'BFD session may flap immediately after corrected DRAM ECC error.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'BFDenabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 859536, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Deleted alerts are seen in alert reports', 'alertNote': 'Deleted alerts are seen in alert reports', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['mwm-v1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['wm-v16.0.0-214-vv1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1694433129, 'exportedTime': 1719360000, 'releaseNote': 'Deleted alerts are seen in alert reports'}, {'bugId': 860272, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a VMTracer deployment that is connecting to a VMware vCenter deployment with tens of ESX servers, the VMTracer agent may enter a restart loop as the data returned from vCenter can be paged.', 'alertNote': 'In a VMTracer deployment that is connecting to a VMware vCenter deployment with tens of ESX servers, the VMTracer agent may enter a restart loop as the data returned from vCenter can be paged. \n\nA workaround is to disable a feature toggle that forces VMTracer to make use of a newer vCenter API which is the root of the issue. A feature toggle can be disabled by:\n\nswitch#bash\n$ sudo vi /etc/toggle.d/VmwareVI.json\n\n-      "enabled": true\n+      "enabled": false\n\nOnce the file is saved VMTracer will make use of the older API used in previous releases when it starts up. If the agent is in a reboot loop then this should be automatic.\n\nNote that changes to  the toggle file will not be persisted across reboots and that a patch or an upgrade to newer release with the fix is needed.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.12', '4.28.10', '4.29.6', '4.30.5', '4.31.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1699320152, 'exportedTime': 1703116800, 'releaseNote': 'In a VMTracer deployment that is connecting to a VMware vCenter deployment with tens of ESX servers, the VMTracer agent may enter a restart loop as the data returned from vCenter can be paged. \n\nA workaround is to disable a feature toggle that forces VMTracer to make use of a newer vCenter API which is the root of the issue. A feature toggle can be disabled by:\n\nswitch#bash\n$ sudo vi /etc/toggle.d/VmwareVI.json\n\n-      "enabled": true\n+      "enabled": false\n\nOnce the file is saved VMTracer will make use of the older API used in previous releases when it starts up. If the agent is in a reboot loop then this should be automatic.\n\nNote that changes to  the toggle file will not be persisted across reboots and that a patch or an upgrade to newer release with the fix is needed.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'vmtracerEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 860742, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Under heavy CPU load, the Strata agent may unexpectedly restart because of a timeout.', 'alertNote': 'Under heavy CPU load, the Strata agent may unexpectedly restart because of a timeout.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.27.2'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1784122383, 'exportedTime': 1699315200, 'releaseNote': 'Under heavy CPU load, the Strata agent may unexpectedly restart because of a timeout.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Strata'}]]}, {'bugId': 860836, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Multi threaded EosSdk application may crash due to non-thread safe access to data structures', 'alertNote': 'Multi threaded EosSdk application may crash due to non-thread safe access to data structures', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.21.3'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.11', '4.29.8', '4.30.2FX-400G-MACSEC', '4.30.4', '4.31.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1710283625, 'exportedTime': 1716768000, 'releaseNote': 'Multi threaded EosSdk application may crash due to non-thread safe access to data structures'}, {'bugId': 862051, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When editing traffic-policy match rules, if one tries to edit a rule for a different match type it is possible to configure an unsupported address family source/destination prefix. The result is a continuous SandAegis crash.', 'alertNote': "When editing traffic-policy match rules, if one tries to edit a rule for a different match type it is possible to configure an unsupported address family source/destination prefix. For example, if you have 'match myRule ipv4' and try to create 'match myRule ipv6' a warning is thrown, but you are able to add v6 prefixes to the rule which incorrectly lead to the v6 prefixes being added to the 'match myRule ipv4'. The result is a continuous SandAegis crash. To stop the crashes, either delete the rule or remove the v6 prefixes from the v4 match rule.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.11', '4.29.7', '4.30.6', '4.31.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1739843414, 'exportedTime': 1748563200, 'releaseNote': "When editing traffic-policy match rules, if one tries to edit a rule for a different match type it is possible to configure an unsupported address family source/destination prefix. For example, if you have 'match myRule ipv4' and try to create 'match myRule ipv6' a warning is thrown, but you are able to add v6 prefixes to the rule which incorrectly lead to the v6 prefixes being added to the 'match myRule ipv4'. The result is a continuous SandAegis crash. To stop the crashes, either delete the rule or remove the v6 prefixes from the v4 match rule."}, {'bugId': 862089, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Increase in the number of "auto" keywords in "set as-path match all replacement" statement of a route map inside a config session may not result in expected BGP advertisement after policy application. See Release Notes for more details.', 'alertNote': 'Increase in the number of "auto" keywords in "set as-path match all replacement" statement of a route map inside a config session may not result in expected BGP advertisement after policy application\nAs a workaround, make an additional change to the route map sequence with "set as-path ..." to force the re-evaluation of the route map. For example, the additional change can be a change in tag value in "set tag".\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.28.10', '4.29.6', '4.30.5', '4.31.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1695094349, 'exportedTime': 1712620800, 'releaseNote': 'Increase in the number of "auto" keywords in "set as-path match all replacement" statement of a route map inside a config session may not result in expected BGP advertisement after policy application\nAs a workaround, make an additional change to the route map sequence with "set as-path ..." to force the re-evaluation of the route map. For example, the additional change can be a change in tag value in "set tag".\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 862185, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On image integrity failure, AP tries upgrade the corrupted partition using the http protocol.', 'alertNote': 'On image integrity failure, AP tries upgrade the corrupted partition using the http protocol.', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['mwm-v1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['wm-v16.1.0-51'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1696305430, 'exportedTime': 1736467200, 'releaseNote': 'On image integrity failure, AP tries upgrade the corrupted partition using the http protocol.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'WifiAPs'}]]}, {'bugId': 862203, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a EVPN VXLAN multicast setup, IPv6 ND packets received on an interface that is attached to a multicast routing enabled SVI might be incorrectly forwarded back to the ingress interface. See Release Notes for more details', 'alertNote': 'In EVPN VXLAN multicast setup, IPv6 ND packets received on an interface that is attached to a multicast routing enabled SVI might be incorrectly forwarded back to the ingress 