rkaround is to avoid configuring more than the maximum logical ports in a pool.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1742932004, 'exportedTime': 1746576000, 'releaseNote': 'Forwarding agent may restart unexpectedly when logical port resources are exhausted. Forwarding agent restart will not impact traffic as long as there are no other forwarding agent restarts within a two-hour window.\n\nWorkaround is to avoid configuring more than the maximum logical ports in a pool.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7260CX3-64'}]]}, {'bugId': 905493, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'While processing traffic classified as kerberos5 or h225, an assert may be triggered by an unexpected return value from the DPI engine and cause the SFE agent to restart. Please see Release Notes for more details.', 'alertNote': 'While processing traffic classified as kerberos5 or h225, an assert may be triggered by an unexpected return value from the DPI engine and cause the SFE agent to restart.  This affects any customer sending these protocols through a DPS tunnel or using a Virtual Topology. \n\nThe workaround is to disable DPI. Please work with the customer support team if you are impacted by this issue to apply the workaround to your configuration.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2FX-CB'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.6', '4.31.1.1FX-AWE', '4.31.2'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1746771814, 'exportedTime': 1734134400, 'releaseNote': 'While processing traffic classified as kerberos5 or h225, an assert may be triggered by an unexpected return value from the DPI engine and cause the SFE agent to restart.  This affects any customer sending these protocols through a DPS tunnel or using a Virtual Topology. \n\nThe workaround is to disable DPI. Please work with the customer support team if you are impacted by this issue to apply the workaround to your configuration.', 'conjunctio