hurn (like interface flaps, peer reload, deletion or addition of remote vteps or changing a route path to remote vteps etc), multicast replication (for features like VXLAN HER, multicast routing, IGMP snooping etc) may be programmed incorrectly in the HW resulting in traffic loss (like BUM/Known mutlicast etc). The workaround is to restart the StrataL3Unicast agent.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident4'}], [{'tag': 'Tomahawk5'}]]}, {'bugId': 906652, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Resolving DNS names for flow streaming may cause excessive CPU usage and send extra notifications to CloudVision.', 'alertNote': "Resolving DNS names for flow streaming may cause excessive CPU usage and send extra notifications to CloudVision.\nThe workaround for this is to disable the DNS resolver with the flag '-flowdns=false'.", 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.27.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.28.4', 'TerminAttr-v1.31.2', 'TerminAttr-v1.32.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1786492800, 'releaseNote': "Resolving DNS names for flow streaming may cause excessive CPU usage and send extra notifications to CloudVision.\nThe workaround for this is to disable the DNS resolver with the flag '-flowdns=false'."}, {'bugId': 907310, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'After disabling IPv4 route compression and restarting SandL3Unicast,”show hardware capacity” may continue to report usage of EcmpLevel1 and FecLevel1 resources under feature FlexRoute, despite the fact that these resources are not actually being used.', 'alertNote': "After disabling IPv4 route compression and restarting SandL3Unicast, 'show hardware capacity' may continue to report usage of EcmpLevel1 and FecLevel1 resources under feature FlexRoute, despite the fact that these resources are not actually being used.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1706147349, 'exportedTime': 1712620800, 'releaseNote': "After disabling IPv4 route compression and restarting SandL3Unicast, 'show hardware capacity' may continue to report usage of EcmpLevel1 and FecLevel1 resources under feature FlexRoute, despite the fact that these resources are not actually being used.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 907407, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Dynamic authorization (CoA) message authentication may fail for Dot1x sometimes, but may pass on retry', 'alertNote': 'Dynamic authorization (CoA) message authentication may fail for Dot1x sometimes, but may pass on retry', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.8', '4.30.6', '4.31.3', '4.32.1'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1762516163, 'exportedTime': 1720656000, 'releaseNote': 'Dynamic authorization (CoA) message authentication may fail for Dot1x sometimes, but may pass on retry', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CCS-710P'}, {'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720DF'}, {'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720DP'}, {'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720DT'}, {'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720XP'}, {'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-722XPM'}, {'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-750'}, {'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 907512, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'BfnNat agent can restart on a 7170 platform when configured with the profile nat-vxlan and access list that divide the NAT translations between full-cone and dynamic with destination port ranges. Please see Release Notes for more details.', 'alertNote': 'BfnNat agent can restart on a 7170 platform configured with the profile nat-vxlan.  The following NAT configuration could lead to the problem:\nip access list nat_fullcone\n   // perform full-cone NAT for udp traffic with destination port in the range [ minValue, maxValue ]\n  10 permit udp <network> any range <minValue> <maxValue>\nip access list nat_dynamic\n  // perform dynamic NAT  for udp traffic with destination port in the range [ 0, minValue ]\n  10 permit udp <network> any range 0 <minValue>\nip nat profile <profileName>\n   ip nat source dynamic access-list nat_fullcone pool poolNat full-cone priority 3\n   ip nat source dynamic access-list nat_dynamic pool poolNat priority 2\n\nThis config is allowing the same sourceIp/sourcePort to translate via full-cone or non-fullCone depending on the destination port.  This can cause "incorrect" full-cone NAT translations in kernel mode.  The same sourceIp/sourceIp might map to 2 different Nat addresses in full-cone mode which will not cause issues on the majority of the platforms but is not ideal.  It will cause issues on the 7170 running in nat-vxlan mode. \n\nThe recommendation is to not create access-lists that divide the NAT translations between full-cone and dynamic with destination port ranges until the fix is in place. \n\n\n\n\n  ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2FX-SIE', '4.31.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1789405402, 'exportedTime': 1714435200, 'releaseNote': 'BfnNat agent can restart on a 7170 platform configured with the profile nat-vxlan.  The following NAT configuration could lead to the problem:\nip access list nat_fullcone\n   // perform full-cone NAT for udp traffic with destination port in the range [ minValue, maxValue ]\n  10 permit udp <network> any range <minValue> <maxValue>\nip access list nat_dynamic\n  // perform dynamic NAT  for udp traffic with destination port in the range [ 0, minValue ]\n  10 permit udp <network> any range 0 <minValue>\nip nat profile <profileName>\n   ip nat source dynamic access-list nat_fullcone pool poolNat full-cone priority 3\n   ip nat source dynamic access-list nat_dynamic pool poolNat priority 2\n\nThis config is allowing the same sourceIp/sourcePort to translate via full-cone or non-fullCone depending on the destination port.  This can cause "incorrect" full-cone NAT translations in kernel mode.  The same sourceIp/sourceIp might map to 2 different Nat addresses in full-cone mode which will not cause issues on the majority of the platforms but is not ideal.  It will cause issues on the 7170 running in nat-vxlan mode. \n\nThe recommendation is to not create access-lists that divide the NAT translations between full-cone and dynamic with destination port ranges until the fix is in place. \n\n\n\n\n  ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7170'}, {'tag': 'natEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 907709, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'For SSO-enabled systems, on the standby supervisor with the link flap damping feature enabled, link flaps can cause the forwarding agent to restart.', 'alertNote': 'For SSO-enabled systems, on the standby supervisor with the link flap damping feature enabled, link flaps can cause the forwarding agent to restart.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1720818367, 'exportedTime': 1786665600, 'releaseNote': 'For SSO-enabled systems, on the standby supervisor with the link flap damping feature enabled, link flaps can cause the forwarding agent to restart.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}, {'tag': 'ssoEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 909128, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'LDAP base-dn strings with space are saved as unquoted strings in running-config which causes syntax error.', 'alertNote': 'LDAP base-dn strings with space are saved as unquoted strings in running-config which causes syntax error.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.8', '4.30.6', '4.31.3', '4.32.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1721110080, 'exportedTime': 1731888000, 'releaseNote': 'LDAP base-dn strings with space are saved as unquoted strings in running-config which causes syntax error.', 'conj