h point to\ntunnels, nexthop-groups, or when routing from one IP address-family to another (RFC 5549) may not work.\n\nConfigure 'hardware forwarding id' under a loopback interface as a workaround if\nmac-address router or mac address virtual is enabled on any interface.\nhttps://www.arista.com/en/support/toi/eos-4-25-0f/14709-support-for-in-band-traffic-in-a-management-vrf-without-routed-svi-or-physical-interfaces\n", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.9', '4.31.6', '4.32.5', '4.33.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1714015275, 'exportedTime': 1788912000, 'releaseNote': "Under certain circumstances if there is an L3 interface with uRPF strict mode enabled,\nsoftware forwarding or control plane generated IP packets for routes which point to\ntunnels, nexthop-groups, or when routing from one IP address-family to another (RFC 5549) may not work.\n\nConfigure 'hardware forwarding id' under a loopback interface as a workaround if\nmac-address router or mac address virtual is enabled on any interface.\nhttps://www.arista.com/en/support/toi/eos-4-25-0f/14709-support-for-in-band-traffic-in-a-management-vrf-without-routed-svi-or-physical-interfaces\n", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'uRPFenabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 951199, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When a TCP SYN/SYN+ACK without an MSS option is received on a DPS tunnel or Ethernet interface with tcp mss ceiling ipv4 configured, the router miscalculates IP length and IP/TCP checksums after adding MSS, causing packet drops locally or downstream.', 'alertNote': 'When a TCP SYN/SYN+ACK packet without any MSS options is received on a DPS tunnel or an Ethernet interface, and "tcp mss ceiling ipv4 [ MSS value ] ... " configuration is present under "router path-selection" or under the Ethernet interface respectively, then the router fails to calculate the IP length and IP/TCP checksum correctly after adding the MSS option. This results in the TCP packet getting dropped on the router or further downstream.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.4', '4.32.2'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1739828208, 'exportedTime': 1767657600, 'releaseNote': 'When a TCP SYN/SYN+ACK packet without any MSS options is received on a DPS tunnel or an Ethernet interface, and "tcp mss ceiling ipv4 [ MSS value ] ... " configuration is present under "router path-selection" or under the Ethernet interface respectively, then the router fails to calculate the IP length and IP/TCP checksum correctly after adding the MSS option. This results in the TCP packet getting dropped on the router or further downstream.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CloudEOS'}]]}, {'bugId': 951223, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When ARP Suppression is enabled, ARP requests from edge interfaces go to `Others` CPU queue rather than `ARP` queue which may result in some ARP requests getting dropped.', 'alertNote': 'When ARP Suppression is enabled, ARP requests from edge interfaces go to "Others" CPU queue rather than "ARP" queue which may result in some ARP requests getting dropped.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1779840000, 'releaseNote': 'When ARP Suppression is enabled, ARP requests from edge interfaces go to "Others" CPU queue rather than "ARP" queue which may result in some ARP requests getting dropped.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnEnabled'}, {'tag': 'IPAddVirtCheck'}, {'tag': 'Strata'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 952421, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If AP receives CoA request without session-timeout, Hostapd may get stuck in a loop and flood logs', 'alertNote': 'If AP receives CoA request without session-timeout, Hostapd may get stuck in a loop and flood logs', 'product': 'mwm', 'versionIntroduced': ['wm-v16.1.0-51'], 'versionFixed': ['wm-v17.0.0-236-vv4'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1736467200, 'releaseNote': 'If AP receives CoA request without session-timeout, Hostapd may get stuck in a loop and flood logs', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'WifiAPs'}]]}, {'bugId': 952501, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When BGP neighbors include long descriptions, the `show ip(v6) bgp summary` commands can get aborted if descriptions include unicode character at the column width boundary of the display. Please see Release Notes for more details.', 'alertNote': 'When BGP neighbors include long descriptions, the `show ip(v6) bgp summary` commands truncate the descriptions to fit them in within the provided column.  If a long description includes a unicode character at the boundary of the column width, the display code may truncate the string in the middle of the unicode character producing an incorrect UTF-8 string which causes the command to be aborted.\nA workaround is to run the command via eAPI.  Similar output may also be retained using `show ip bgp summary | json`.  Alternatively, the `show bgp summary` command may be used to obtain similar information, without the neighbor description.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.7', '4.31.4', '4.32.2'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1736779415, 'exportedTime': 1720656000, 'releaseNote': 'When BGP neighbors include long descriptions, the `show ip(v6) bgp summary` commands truncate the descriptions to fit them in within the provided column.  If a long description includes a unicode character at the boundary of the column width, the display code may truncate the string in the middle of the unicode character producing an incorrect UTF-8 string which causes the command to be aborted.\nA workaround is to run the command via eAPI.  Similar output may also be retained using `show ip bgp summary | json`.  Alternatively, the `show bgp summary` command may be used to obtain similar information, without the neighbor description.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}]]}, {'bugId': 954550, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In the multi-agent mode, BGP default-originate policy may affect non-default routes which leads to those non-default routes being advertised with unexpected attributes or being advertised while the routes should be denied by the neighbor outbound policy.', 'alertNote': 'In the multi-agent mode, the BGP default-originate policy may affect non-default routes which leads to those non-default routes being advertised with unexpected attributes or being advertised while the routes should be denied by the neighbor outbound policy.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.8', '4.32.5', '4.33.3', '4.34.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1782320177, 'exportedTime': 1791331200, 'releaseNote': 'In the multi-agent mode, the BGP default-originate policy may affect non-default routes which leads to those non-default routes being advertised with unexpected attributes or being advertised while the routes should be denied by the neighbor outbound policy.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}]]}, {'bugId': 955097, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "Streaming Agent (TerminAttr)'s version string included a commit hash, which has been removed. No technical impact.", 'alertNote': "Streaming Agent (TerminAttr)'s version string included a commit hash, which has been removed. No technical impact. ", 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.31.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.31.4', 'TerminAttr-v1.32.1', 'TerminAttr-v1.33.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1784160000, 'releaseNote': "Streaming Agent (TerminAttr)'s version string included a commit hash, which has been removed. No technical impact. "}, {'bugId': 955244, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When ARP requests o