d member interface(s) are also configured to be part of private VLAN, traffic ingressing on the member interface(s) may not be correctly forwarded after deleting the port channel.\nA workaround is to change the switchport mode of the member interface(s) and revert it back to initial switchport mode after deleting the port channel.\n\nSimilarly, traffic ingressing on the member interface(s) may not be correctly forwarded after creating a port channel having member interface(s) configured to be part of private VLAN and configured with switchport mode different from the port channel or after adding such a port channel to a private VLAN.\nA workaround is to change the switchport mode of the port channel and revert it back to initial switchport mode.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.31.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1726790400, 'releaseNote': 'If a port channel is configured with switchport mode different from its member interface(s) and is part of a private VLAN and member interface(s) are also configured to be part of private VLAN, traffic ingressing on the member interface(s) may not be correctly forwarded after deleting the port channel.\nA workaround is to change the switchport mode of the member interface(s) and revert it back to initial switchport mode after deleting the port channel.\n\nSimilarly, traffic ingressing on the member interface(s) may not be correctly forwarded after creating a port channel having member interface(s) configured to be part of private VLAN and configured with switchport mode different from the port channel or after adding such a port channel to a private VLAN.\nA workaround is to change the switchport mode of the port channel and revert it back to initial switchport mode.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 964466, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'AAA sessions may be leaked if a connection to OpenConfig or Octa is closed immediately after opening.', 'alertNote': 'AAA sessions may be leaked if a connection to OpenConfig or Octa is closed immediately after opening.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.8', '4.31.5', '4.32.1FX-400G-MACSEC', '4.32.2'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1760042312, 'exportedTime': 1737936000, 'releaseNote': 'AAA sessions may be leaked if a connection to OpenConfig or Octa is closed immediately after opening.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'gNMIEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 965192, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Source MAC addresses of IPv4 and IPv6 packets with TTL=0/HopLimit=0 are unexpectedly learned.', 'alertNote': 'Source MAC addresses of IPv4 and IPv6 packets with TTL=0/HopLimit=0 are unexpectedly learned.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.7', '4.32.5', '4.33.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1726001554, 'exportedTime': 1728604800, 'releaseNote': 'Source MAC addresses of IPv4 and IPv6 packets with TTL=0/HopLimit=0 are unexpectedly learned.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7808-CH'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7816-CH'}], [{'tag': 'SandGen4'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7804-CH'}], [{'tag': '7289'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7812-CH'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7130LBR-48S6QD'}], [{'tag': '7289R3A-SC'}], [{'tag': '7289R3AK-SC'}], [{'tag': '7289R3AM-SC'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7816L-CH'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280TR3-40C6'}], [{'tag': 'EaglePeak'}]]}, {'bugId': 965239, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Disabling IPv4/IPv6 multicast via "no router multicast" or "no ipv4/ipv6" or issuing "software-forwarding sfe" even within a "configure session" might end up preventing the programming of new multicast routes', 'alertNote': 'Disabling IPv4/IPv6 multicast via "no router multicast" or "no ipv4/ipv6" or issuing "software-forwarding sfe" even within a "configure session" might end up preventing the programming of new multicast routes.\n\nTo resolve this issue, reconfig