ag': 'CCS-722XPM-48Y4'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7010TX-48-DC'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7050SX3-48C8'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-722XPM-48ZY8'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280TR3-40C6'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR3-48YC8'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720XP-48TXH-2C-S'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR3M-48YC8'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR3K-48YC8'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-720XP-24ZY4'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7050CX3-32S'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7150SC-64-CLD'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7150SC-24-CLD'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280CR3-96'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR-48C6'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR3-40YC6'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR3E-40YC6'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7060CX-32C'}]]}, {'bugId': 1019688, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The switch will be operating in store-and-forward mode even while the config is in cut-through mode. The status command "show switch forwarding mode" also says that the switch is in cut-through mode.', 'alertNote': 'The switch will be operating in store-and-forward mode even while the config is in cut-through mode. The status command "show switch forwarding mode" also says that the switch is in cut-through mode.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1734393600, 'releaseNote': 'The switch will be operating in store-and-forward mode even while the config is in cut-through mode. The status command "show switch forwarding mode" also says that the switch is in cut-through mode.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7368'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7388'}]]}, {'bugId': 1019978, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If a community list is deleted in a config session, or if the system is under load when the list is deleted, it is possible for the community list deletion to end up in an incomplete state.', 'alertNote': 'If a community list is deleted in a config session, or if the system is under load when the list is deleted, it is possible for the community list deletion to end up in an incomplete state. The knock on effect of this is that any route map which referenes this incomplete community list will not react to configuration changes. The route map configuration changes will not be reflected in running policy.\n\nWorkaround is to remove any references to the deleted community list from any running route map.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.29.10', '4.30.9', '4.31.6', '4.32.4', '4.33.1'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1751601282, 'exportedTime': 1733097600, 'releaseNote': 'If a community list is deleted in a config session, or if the system is under load when the list is deleted, it is possible for the community list deletion to end up in an incomplete state. The knock on effect of this is that any route map which referenes this incomplete community list will not react to configuration changes. The route map configuration changes will not be reflected in running policy.\n\nWorkaround is to remove any references to the deleted community list from any running route map.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}]]}, {'bugId': 1020318, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'With 802.1X "dot1x mac based authentication always" and "monitor server radius" configured, if AAA is unreachable, the switch may continue sending unicast identity requests to an EAPOL supplicant even after authentication fails. See bug description.', 'alertNote': 'With "dot1x mac based authentication always" and "monitor server radius" feature for 802.1X configured, when AAA is unreachable, the switch may continue to send unicast identity request to an EAPOL supplicant even after if fails authentication due to unreachable AAA servers. This may happen if deadtime is configured for RADIUS servers instead of "monitor server radius" feature.\nThe switch recovers from this state when the AAA servers are reachable. Another potential workaround is to disable "dot1x mac based authentication always" configuration.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.7', '4.32.5', '4.33.2'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1734592109, 'exportedTime': 1785888000, 'releaseNote': 'With "dot1x mac based authentication always" and "monitor server radius" feature for 802.1X configured, when AAA is unreachable, the switch may continue to send unicast identity request to an EAPOL supplicant even after if fails authentication due to unreachable AAA servers. This may happen if deadtime is configured for RADIUS servers instead of "monitor server radius" feature.\nThe switch recovers from this state when the AAA servers are reachable. Another potential workaround is to disable "dot1x mac based authentication always" configuration.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dot1xMBA'}]]}, {'bugId': 1020540, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If admin enabled state of an interface is Unknown, the telemetry of the YANG path /interfaces/interface/state/admin-status will have the value "TESTING". The telemetry client should interpret it as value UP like the CLI command', 'alertNote': 'If admin enabled state of an interface is Unknown, the telemetry of the YANG path /interfaces/interface/state/admin-status will have the value "TESTING". The telemetry client should interpret it as value UP, just like how the corresponding CLI show command does.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.7', '4.32.5', '4.33.2'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1773974596, 'exportedTime': 1740096000, 'releaseNote': 'If admin enabled state of an interface is Unknown, the telemetry of the YANG path /interfaces/interface/state/admin-status will have the value "TESTING". The telemetry client should interpret it as value UP, just like how the corresponding CLI show command does.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'gNMIEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1020833, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Fast roaming failures are reported as association failures on the 