rying to program the new nextHop. The route action, with which the route was programmed with, can be stashed and used instead of using the current state of the nextHop to help avoid this issue.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'NexthopGroupConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1022516, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'DOM values may not be updated while an interface is in use. Use "shut" followed by "no shut" on an interface to refresh the DOM values.', 'alertNote': 'DOM values may not be updated while an interface is in use.\n\nUse "shut" followed by "no shut" on an interface to refresh the DOM values. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.6', '4.34.0'], 'bites': 6, 'lastBiteTime': 1790290203, 'exportedTime': 1759795200, 'releaseNote': 'DOM values may not be updated while an interface is in use.\n\nUse "shut" followed by "no shut" on an interface to refresh the DOM values. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7130'}]]}, {'bugId': 1022550, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In VXLAN routing setups, the counter value of "Number of Pkts dropped by DMA socket" from the CLI "show vxlan counter software" output may incorrectly show large values which may result in a syslog "VXLAN-4-LOCAL2REMOTE_SOCKET_OVERFLOW". ', 'alertNote': 'In VXLAN routing setups, the counter value of "Number of Pkts dropped by DMA socket" from the CLI "show vxlan counter software" output may incorrectly show large values. Also, this may result in a syslog "VXLAN-4-LOCAL2REMOTE_SOCKET_OVERFLOW".  The issue is self-correcting, no further action is necessary. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.4', '4.33.2'], 'bites': 9, 'lastBiteTime': 1778542825, 'exportedTime': 1739145600, 'releaseNote': 'In VXLAN routing setups, the counter value of "Number of Pkts dropped by DMA socket" from the CLI "show vxlan counter software" output may incorrectly show large values. Als