: 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1732030653, 'exportedTime': 1748822400, 'releaseNote': 'AP does not honour Additional VLANs for monitoring added from CV-CUE UI while operating in sensor mode.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'WifiAPs'}]]}, {'bugId': 1024261, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If an LLDP neighbor port ID is a byte sequence, a gNMI Get/Subscribe to the OpenConfig path "/lldp/interfaces/interface/neighbors/neighbor/state/port-id" results in the error "grpc: error while marshaling: string field contains invalid UTF-8".', 'alertNote': 'If an LLDP neighbor port ID is a byte sequence, a gNMI Get/Subscribe to the OpenConfig path "/lldp/interfaces/interface/neighbors/neighbor/state/port-id" results in the error "grpc: error while marshaling: string field contains invalid UTF-8".', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.7', '4.32.5', '4.33.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1768269413, 'exportedTime': 1740096000, 'releaseNote': 'If an LLDP neighbor port ID is a byte sequence, a gNMI Get/Subscribe to the OpenConfig path "/lldp/interfaces/interface/neighbors/neighbor/state/port-id" results in the error "grpc: error while marshaling: string field contains invalid UTF-8".', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'gNMIEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1024359, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When the -cvgnmi flag is enabled and the version of CloudVision that the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) is streaming to does not support gNMI streaming, the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may unexpectedly restart.', 'alertNote': 'When the -cvgnmi flag is enabled and the version of CloudVision that the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) is streaming to does not support gNMI streaming, the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may unexpectedly restart.\nThe workaround is to remove the -cvgnmi flag.', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.35.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.35.1', 'TerminAttr-v1.36.1', 'TerminAttr-v1.37.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1744752772, 'exportedTime': 1786492800, 'releaseNote': 'When the -cvgnmi flag is enabled and the version of CloudVision that the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) is streaming to does not support gNMI streaming, the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may unexpectedly restart.\nThe workaround is to remove the -cvgnmi flag.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'TerminAttrCvgnmi'}]]}, {'bugId': 1024377, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Mpls route can get unprogrammed when transitioning to a new adjacency until it is resolved.', 'alertNote': 'Mpls route can get unprogrammed when transitioning to a new adjacency until it is resolved.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.6', '4.33.3', '4.34.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1752911909, 'exportedTime': 1759017600, 'releaseNote': 'Mpls route can get unprogrammed when transitioning to a new adjacency until it is resolved.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1025806, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A VRF named /NULL/ may not function correctly. In ribd and multi-agent routing protocol model, the VRF may restart repeatedly. To work around this issue, use a different VRF name.', 'alertNote': 'A VRF named "NULL" may not function correctly. When using the ribd routing protocol model, the Rib agent for that VRF will restart repeatedly, preventing the VRF from becoming active. When using the multi-agnet routing protocol model, the agent for any IGP (Ospf, Ospf3, Isis, and Rip) configured for that VRF may restart repeatedly.\n\nTo work around this issue, use a different VRF name.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.30.9', '4.31.6', '4.32.5', '4.33.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1729835843, 'exportedTime': 1738108800, 'releaseNote': 'A VRF named "NULL" may not function correctly. When using the ribd routing protocol model, the Rib agent for that VRF will restart repeatedly, preventing the VRF from becoming active. When using the multi-agnet routing protocol model, the agent for any IGP (Ospf, Ospf3, Isis, and Rip) configured for that VRF may restart repeatedly.\n\nTo work around this issue, use a different VRF name.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1026094, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On devices running EVPN multicast OISM, when a PIM External Gateway ( PEG) device is configured as RP, receivers in the external network that join the EVPN network via the PEG-nonDR RP may experience traffic loss. ', 'alertNote': 'When "fips logging" is enabled under "management security" mode the SuperServer agent will restart repeatedly and not function. This will mean many system services such as SSH, eAPI, and NTP will not update in response to configuration changes.  A workaround is to disable the "fips logging" option as it does not provide additional functionality on affected systems.\n ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.4', '4.33.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1752913095, 'exportedTime': 1745798400, 'releaseNote': 'When "fips logging" is enabled under "management security" mode the SuperServer agent will restart repeatedly and not function. This will mean many system services such as SSH, eAPI, and NTP will not update in response to configuration changes.  A workaround is to disable the "fips logging" option as it does not provide additional functionality on affected systems.\n '}, {'bugId': 1029184, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When BGP receives routes with nexthop points to its own peering address, those routes are discarded, because such nexthop is invalid per RFC4271 Section 5.1.3. However a new Via Id is consumed for the invalid nexthop. ', 'alertNote': 'BGP next hops are tracked using Via IDs.  Likewise, programmed BGP next hop lists for ECMP best paths are tracked using Via Set IDs.  Prolonged, excessive creation and deletion of BGP next hops or of BGP next hop lists may cause Via IDs or Via Set IDs to wrap which can cause Via and/or Via Set information to be overwritten which can lead to BGP routing entries in the IP FIB which are not consistent with the state in the BGP RIB.\nThese problems have been observed in the presence of continuous route churn at a very high rate for a prolonged time.  Via ID wrapping has also been observed when BGP receives routes with a next hop that is its peering address.  Those routes are discarded as invalid per RFC4271 Section 5.1.3, but a Via ID is consumed each time.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.9', '4.32.7', '4.33.4', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 8, 'lastBiteTime': 1782766580, 'exportedTime': 1753833600, 'releaseNote': 'BGP next hops are tracked using Via IDs.  Likewise, programmed BGP next hop lists for ECMP best paths are tracked using Via Set IDs.  Prolonged, excessive creation and deletion of BGP next hops or of BGP next hop lists may cause Via IDs or Via Set IDs to wrap which can cause Via and/or Via Set information to be overwritten which can lead to BGP routing entries in the IP FIB which are not consistent with the state in the BGP RIB.\nThese problems have been observed in the presence of continuous route churn at a very high rate for a prolonged time.  Via ID wrapping has also been observed when BGP receives routes with a next hop that is its peering address.  Those routes are discarded as invalid per RFC4271 Section 5.1.3, but a Via ID is consumed each time.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1029581, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agents (TerminAttr, OpenConfig, or Octa) may fail to stream logs if more than one Streaming Agent is run concurrently on a single device.', 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agents (TerminAttr, OpenConfig, or Octa) 