.\n\nWorkaround is to remove the file /mnt/flash/asu-persistent-store.json and issue a subsequent reload.'}, {'bugId': 1070942, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'ESP trailer in IPsec packet is padded with zeros by the sender. Such packets may get dropped by the receiving tunnel endpoint.', 'alertNote': 'ESP trailer in IPsec packet is padded with zeros by the sender. Such packets may get dropped by the receiving tunnel endpoint.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.3', '4.34.1'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1773044367, 'exportedTime': 1750982400, 'releaseNote': 'ESP trailer in IPsec packet is padded with zeros by the sender. Such packets may get dropped by the receiving tunnel endpoint.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ipsecEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Jericho2M'}]]}, {'bugId': 1073674, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': '7280SR3 devices using the AMD Embedded R-Series RX-421ND may not run customer-provided executables using the RDRAND instruction on the CPU. A script can be run to work around the problem by disabling the CPUs support for the instruction', 'alertNote': "7280SR3 devices using the AMD Embedded R-Series RX-421ND may not run customer-provided executables using the RDRAND instruction on the CPU. A script can be run to work around the problem by disabling the CPU's support for the instruction ", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.8', '4.32.6', '4.33.3', '4.34.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1738036265, 'exportedTime': 1745539200, 'releaseNote': "7280SR3 devices using the AMD Embedded R-Series RX-421ND may not run customer-provided executables using the RDRAND instruction on the CPU. A script can be run to work around the problem by disabling the CPU's support for the instruction ", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7280SR3'}]]}, {'bugId': 1076200, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary'