e SEU. Restarting these agents may impact traffic\n', 'alertNote': 'SEUs affecting some hardware MDB hash tables may not be corrected.\n\nDepending on the affected hardware hash table, restarting one or more of the following feature agents may resolve the SEU:  SandAcl, SandBcmSec, SandMact, and SandOam. Note that restarting some of these agents may be traffic impacting.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.1FX-wbb', '4.33.1.2', '4.33.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1746576000, 'releaseNote': 'SEUs affecting some hardware MDB hash tables may not be corrected.\n\nDepending on the affected hardware hash table, restarting one or more of the following feature agents may resolve the SEU:  SandAcl, SandBcmSec, SandMact, and SandOam. Note that restarting some of these agents may be traffic impacting.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7280R3A'}]]}, {'bugId': 1081806, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In EVPN MPLS multihome AA, if an IPv6 device changes address, all active multihome peers repeatedly send NS packets for the old IPv6 address. This causes switching between proxy and non-proxy MAC-IP routes, which may result in incorrectly sent traffic', 'alertNote': 'In an EVPN MPLS multihome active-active setup, if an IPv6 device changes its address, all active multihome peers will repeatedly send Neighbor Solicitation (NS) packets for the old IPv6 address. This causes them to repeatedly switch between advertising proxy and non-proxy MAC-IP routes. As a result, traffic may be incorrectly sent to these peers, even if a new device with a different MAC has taken the IP address on a different PE.\n\nWorkaround: Add a static drop MAC on all but one of the multihoming devices until all problematic ND entries are removed if "redistribute static" is not configured. If "redistribute static" is configured, workaround is shut the VLAN on all multihoming devices until all problematic ND entries are removed.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.10', '4.33.8', '4.34.5', '4.35.2'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1753468371, 'exportedTime': 1778716800, 'releaseNote': 'In an EVPN MPLS multihome active-active setup, if an IPv6 device changes its address, all active multihome peers will repeatedly send Neighbor Solicitation (NS) packets for the old IPv6 address. This causes them to repeatedly switch between advertising proxy and non-proxy MAC-IP routes. As a result, traffic may be incorrectly sent to these peers, even if a new device with a different MAC has taken the IP address on a different PE.\n\nWorkaround: Add a static drop MAC on all but one of the multihoming devices until all problematic ND entries are removed if "redistribute static" is not configured. If "redistribute static" is configured, workaround is shut the VLAN on all multihoming devices until all problematic ND entries are removed.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpn-multihoming-enabled'}, {'tag': 'Ipv6Interface'}, {'tag': 'MPLSEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1082596, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On the 7170B baremetal profile, when there are more than 500 ECMP groups, the BfnL3 agent may unexpectedly restart.', 'alertNote': 'On the 7170B baremetal profile, when there are more than 500 ECMP groups, the BfnL3 agent may unexpectedly restart.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.31.7'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.6', '4.35.3'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1771560851, 'exportedTime': 1781654400, 'releaseNote': 'On the 7170B baremetal profile, when there are more than 500 ECMP groups, the BfnL3 agent may unexpectedly restart.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7170B-64C'}]]}, {'bugId': 1084459, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) stopped sending _counts messages for some Smash paths. This may result in missing or stale telemetry data in CloudVision dashboards.