ionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.1FX-GDC', '4.35.nofixyet', '4.36.nofixyet', '4.37.nofixyet'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1760177522, 'exportedTime': 1786492800, 'releaseNote': "When a host's ARP entry is learned on two MH A-A PEs and the host changes MAC address and sends an ARP packet with the same IP and the new MAC, the PE receiving the ARP packet may delete its local ARP entry and replace it with a remote ARP entry with the old MAC instead of updating the ARP entry with the new MAC. This will cause traffic destined to the IP to continue to be sent to the old MAC\n\nWorkaround is to add an RCF rule to not advertise EVPN type 2 routes for hosts whose MACs are expected to change or have the host resend the ARP packet upon changing MACs.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpn-multihoming-enabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1117760, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Performing a config replace may cause routing to be disabled in some VRFs. A workaround is to perform another config replace operation. If that does not resolve the issue, then the switch needs to be rebooted.', 'alertNote': 'Performing a config replace may cause routing to be disabled in some VRFs. A workaround is to perform another config replace operation. If that does not resolve the issue, then the switch needs to be rebooted.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.8', '4.32.6', '4.33.4', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1753261041, 'exportedTime': 1750464000, 'releaseNote': 'Performing a config replace may cause routing to be disabled in some VRFs. A workaround is to perform another config replace operation. If that does not resolve the issue, then the switch needs to be rebooted.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1118105, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In an EVPN VXLAN deployment, configuring a VLAN-VNI mapping without creating corresponding VL