ibrated when "Announce message with timestamp earlier than the previous timestamp" packet drops occur.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'PTPEnabledInterface'}]]}, {'bugId': 1154188, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When the PhyDs280 agent is restarted, including in a reboot scenario, some ports may exhibit PCS errors or link flaps.', 'alertNote': 'Any interface may experience PCS errors or link flaps.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.25.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.9', '4.32.7', '4.33.5', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1732658862, 'exportedTime': 1754092800, 'releaseNote': 'Any interface may experience PCS errors or link flaps.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7130LBR-48S6QD'}]]}, {'bugId': 1154255, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Removing a passive copper cable and replacing it with a 400GBASE-FR4 transceiver while the XcvrAgent is in the process of starting will cause XcvrAgent to restart repeatedly. ', 'alertNote': 'Removing a passive copper cable and replacing it with a 400GBASE-FR4 transceiver while the XcvrAgent is in the process of starting will cause XcvrAgent to restart repeatedly.\n\nRemoving the newly inserted transceiver will allow XcvrAgent to restart successfully.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.31.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.9', '4.32.7', '4.33.4', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1789963329, 'exportedTime': 1750723200, 'releaseNote': 'Removing a passive copper cable and replacing it with a 400GBASE-FR4 transceiver while the XcvrAgent is in the process of starting will cause XcvrAgent to restart repeatedly.\n\nRemoving the newly inserted transceiver will allow XcvrAgent to restart successfully.'}, {'bugId': 1156288, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Dot1x agent might silently drop RADIUS dynamic-authorization messages when more than one RADIUS servers are configured using hostname. The workaround is to remove the hostname based configuration and re- configure the RADIUS servers using IP addresses. ', 'alertNote': 'Dot1x agent might silently drop RADIUS dynamic-authorization messages when more than one RADIUS servers are configured using hostname.\nThe workaround is to remove the hostname based configuration and re-configure the RADIUS servers using IP addresses.\n\nFor example if the configuration in issue state is like below -\n(config)# radius-server host dummy-hostname1 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# radius-server host dummy-hostname2 vrf dummy-vrf\n\nThe workaround to recover would be to first remove the existing configuration and then reconfigure using IP address\n(config)# no radius-server host dummy-hostname1 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# no radius-server host dummy-hostname2 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# radius-server host ipaddr1 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# radius-server host ipaddr2 vrf dummy-vrf', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1769653125, 'exportedTime': 1786492800, 'releaseNote': 'Dot1x agent might silently drop RADIUS dynamic-authorization messages when more than one RADIUS servers are configured using hostname.\nThe workaround is to remove the hostname based configuration and re-configure the RADIUS servers using IP addresses.\n\nFor example if the configuration in issue state is like below -\n(config)# radius-server host dummy-hostname1 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# radius-server host dummy-hostname2 vrf dummy-vrf\n\nThe workaround to recover would be to first remove the existing configuration and then reconfigure using IP address\n(config)# no radius-server host dummy-hostname1 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# no radius-server host dummy-hostname2 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# radius-server host ipaddr1 vrf dummy-vrf\n(config)# radius-server host ipaddr2 vrf dummy-vrf', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1156661, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The `show boot` command can fail when trying to read CPU Model Specific Registers.', 'alertNote': 'The "show boot" command can fail when trying to read CPU Model Specific Registers.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.2'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1770342459, 'exportedTime': 1793404800, 'releaseNote': 'The "show boot" command can fail when trying to read CPU Model Specific Registers.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'cEOS'}]]}, {'bugId': 1159262, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'L2 subinterfaces and access ports on non-DF of single-active Ethernet Segment go error-disabled.To recover,reconfigure the Ethernet Segment,switch to all-active by removing"redundancy single-active" then remove the Ethernet Segment to avoid error-disable', 'alertNote': 'L2-Subinterfaces and Access Ports belonging to a single-active Ethernet Segment are put in an error-disabled state on the non-DF.  These interfaces will remain in the error-disabled state if the Ethernet Segment configuration is removed from these interfaces.\n\nAs a workaround, the Ethernet Segment can be re-configured under the problematic interface, and re-configured to all-active by removing the "redundancy single-active" configuration.  The Ethernet Segment can then be removed from the interface without leaving it in an error-disabled state.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.6', '4.33.4', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1745845310, 'exportedTime': 1754352000, 'releaseNote': 'L2-Subinterfaces and Access Ports belonging to a single-active Ethernet Segment are put in an error-disabled state on the non-DF.  These interfaces will remain in the error-disabled state if the Ethernet Segment configuration is removed from these interfaces.\n\nAs a workaround, the Ethernet Segment can be re-configured under the problematic interface, and re-configured to all-active by removing the "redundancy single-active" configuration.  The Ethernet Segment can then be removed from the interface without leaving it in an error-disabled state.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1161768, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The switch may reload unexpectedly.', 'alertNote': 'The switch may reload unexpectedly.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.1FX-7060X.3', '4.34.nofixyet', '4.35.0FX-7060X6.3', '4.35.2'], 'bites': 24, 'lastBiteTime': 1788481022, 'exportedTime': 1756944000, 'releaseNote': 'The switch may reload unexpectedly.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7060X6-64PE'}]]}, {'bugId': 1164839, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Triggering SSU from later than EOS-4.34.0F fails when at least one system linecard has been shutdown, causing a full reboot.', 'alertNote': 'Triggering SSU from later than EOS-4.34.0F fails when at least one system linecard has been shutdown, causing a full reboot.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.34.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.3', '4.35.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1759276800, 'releaseNote': 'Triggering SSU from later than EOS-4.34.0F fails when at least one system linecard has been shutdown, causing a full reboot.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Trident3X4'}]]}, {'bugId': 1165537, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Image optimizations used on certain platforms are not correctly signed. This may result in errors when loading the image on a switch using the "install source" or "boot system" commands and upon reloading the switch with the "reload" command.', 'alertNote': 'Image optimizations used on certain platforms are not correctly signed. This may result in errors when loading the image on a switch using the "install source" or "boot system" commands and upon reloading the switch with the "reload" command. If secure