ng BGP routes get redistributed correctly.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'BGPAggregateAddress'}]]}, {'bugId': 1195435, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The EVPN gateway linking VXLAN and DPS networks may drop traffic to specific next hops. Check this via show adaptive-virtual-topology next-hop tunnel encapsulation. If the type is wrong or missing, un-configure then re-apply topology role x gateway vxlan.', 'alertNote': 'The EVPN gateway that interconnects VXLAN and dynamic path selection (DPS) networks may drop traffic heading to certain next hops. This issue can be identified by “show adaptive-virtual-topology next-hop tunnel encapsulation” when the next hop’s encapsulation type is incorrect or the next hop is not shown in the output.\n\nThe workaround is to un-configure the “topology role x gateway vxlan” and then re-apply this configuration. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.7', '4.33.5', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1749623736, 'exportedTime': 1774915200, 'releaseNote': 'The EVPN gateway that interconnects VXLAN and dynamic path selection (DPS) networks may drop traffic heading to certain next hops. This issue can be identified by “show adaptive-virtual-topology next-hop tunnel encapsulation” when the next hop’s encapsulation type is incorrect or the next hop is not shown in the output.\n\nThe workaround is to un-configure the “topology role x gateway vxlan” and then re-apply this configuration. '}, {'bugId': 1195909, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When Port 5 operating with 10M/100M speed, we might not able to establish the link if peer side don`t support autoneg. The workaround is trunning autoneg on peer link or change speed to 1G', 'alertNote': "When Port 5 operating with 10M/100M speed, we might not able to establish the link if peer side don't support autoneg. The workaround is trunning autoneg on peer link or change speed