e following error message "Tx Malicious Driver Detection events detected" is observed when the SSH session fails in the dmesg output on the device (viewed from the bash shell). \n\nThe workaround is to disable hardware crypto or send traffic via non-NAC ports.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CloudEOS'}, {'tag': 'ipsecEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'AWE-5000'}, {'tag': 'ipsecEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1200228, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A restart of the Strata agent when configured port channel(s) are present may cause traffic drops if subsequently these port channels are removed and/or interfaces are removed from port channels.', 'alertNote': 'A restart of the Strata agent when configured port channel(s) are present may cause traffic drops if subsequently these ports channels are removed and/or interfaces are removed from port channels.\nWorkaround:\n - restart StrataLag and StrataL2Combo agent\n\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.34.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.5', '4.35.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1773705600, 'releaseNote': 'A restart of the Strata agent when configured port channel(s) are present may cause traffic drops if subsequently these ports channels are removed and/or interfaces are removed from port channels.\nWorkaround:\n - restart StrataLag and StrataL2Combo agent\n\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7060X6'}, {'tag': 'Tomahawk5-T'}]]}, {'bugId': 1202073, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A Single Event Upset (SEU) on the L2_USER_ENTRY table may not be corrected. This may cause traffic to be misforwarded. A workaround is to reset the forwarding chip.', 'alertNote': 'A Single Event Upset (SEU) on the L2_USER_ENTRY table may not be corrected. This may cause traffic to be misforwarded.\nA workaround is to reset the forwarding chip.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.10', '4.33.7', '4.34.5', '4.35.2'], 'bites': 