id routes.', 'alertNote': 'In EVPN Deployments that make use of `neighbor default next-hop-self received-evpn-routes route-type ip-prefix`, if we receive inbound EVPN ip-prefix route without a RouteTarget extended community attached, it may result in continuous BGP crash and will affect routing and forwarding.\n\nAs a workaround, an inbound route-map may be configured to drop EVPN paths without a valid Route Target', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.9', '4.32.7', '4.33.5', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1758758400, 'releaseNote': 'In EVPN Deployments that make use of `neighbor default next-hop-self received-evpn-routes route-type ip-prefix`, if we receive inbound EVPN ip-prefix route without a RouteTarget extended community attached, it may result in continuous BGP crash and will affect routing and forwarding.\n\nAs a workaround, an inbound route-map may be configured to drop EVPN paths without a valid Route Target', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1210130, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When transceiver OpenConfig logical channel indices are configured, subsequent gNMI gets of certain paths do not return any values until the values within the transceiver are modified. Refer to Software Bug portal for exact paths and workaround', 'alertNote': 'When transceiver OpenConfig logical channel indices are configured, subsequent gNMI gets of certain paths do not return any values until the values within the transceiver are modified. Note that some of these attributes rarely, if ever, change, so the effect will be long lasting. Following paths affected by this behavior:\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/ethernet/state/fec-uncorrectable-blocks\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/ethernet/state/pre-fec-ber\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/fec-uncorrectable-blocks\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/pre-fec-ber\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/esnr\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/q-value\n\nThe workaround is to restart the L1OpenConfig agent.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.34.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.3', '4.35.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1782428674, 'exportedTime': 1793318400, 'releaseNote': 'When transceiver OpenConfig logical channel indices are configured, subsequent gNMI gets of certain paths do not return any values until the values within the transceiver are modified. Note that some of these attributes rarely, if ever, change, so the effect will be long lasting. Following paths affected by this behavior:\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/ethernet/state/fec-uncorrectable-blocks\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/ethernet/state/pre-fec-ber\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/fec-uncorrectable-blocks\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/pre-fec-ber\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/esnr\n/terminal-device/logical-channels/channel[index=*]/otn/state/q-value\n\nThe workaround is to restart the L1OpenConfig agent.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'gNMIEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1210795, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When a BGP peer is using the "neighbor <address | peer-group> out-delay <seconds>" configuration, a route may remain in queued state and fail to be advertised to the peer. ', 'alertNote': 'When a BGP peer is using the "neighbor <address | peer-group> out-delay <seconds>" configuration, a route may remain in queued state and fail to be advertised to the peer.\nThis issue does not apply to BGP peers using the "neighbor <address | peer-group> out-delay <seconds> changes [withdrawals]" configuration.\nWithdrawing all the paths for the queued route and subsequently re-learning the ro