rted. Following the restart, previous congestion data will be lost.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'lanzEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Sand'}]]}, {'bugId': 1225445, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Scheduling variation in interface counter updates and time stamping of these updates may increase with the scale of the MAC table.', 'alertNote': 'Scheduling variation in interface counter updates and time stamping of these updates may increase with the scale of the MAC table. ', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.6', '4.34.4', '4.35.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1744367250, 'exportedTime': 1774396800, 'releaseNote': 'Scheduling variation in interface counter updates and time stamping of these updates may increase with the scale of the MAC table. ', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 1225739, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A StrataL3 restart can leave EVPN Multi-Home MAC entries stale in hardware if they transitioned from an aged to a remote-learned state prior to the restart. To resolve this, restart the StrataL2 agent.', 'alertNote': 'After a StrataL3 restart, EVPN Multi-Home MAC entries may become stale and remain programmed in hardware with outdated values. This can occur when a MAC entry, after going through an aging interval with no traffic, receives traffic again and transitions to a remote-learned state. If StrataL3 is restarted any time after this transition, the stale entry may persist. \nRestarting the StrataL2 agent clears the stale entries and resolves the issue.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.31.10', '4.32.8', '4.33.6', '4.34.4', '4.35.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1774396800, 'releaseNote': 'After a StrataL3 restart, EVPN Multi-Home MAC entries may become stale and remain programmed in hardware with outdated values. This can occur when a MAC entry, after going through an aging interval with no traffic, receives traffic again and transitions to a remote-learned state. If StrataL3 is restarted any time after this transition, the stale entry may persist. \nRestarting the StrataL2 agent clears the stale entries and resolves the issue.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpn-multihoming-enabled'}, {'tag': 'Trident3X1'}]]}, {'bugId': 1229723, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may drop data and log “DATA_LOSS_ERROR” when CloudVision returns a retryable error code.', 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may drop data and log “DATA_LOSS_ERROR” when CloudVision returns a retryable error code.', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v0.1'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.31.14', 'TerminAttr-v1.34.8', 'TerminAttr-v1.37.6', 'TerminAttr-v1.40.3', 'TerminAttr-v1.41.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1784160000, 'releaseNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may drop data and log “DATA_LOSS_ERROR” when CloudVision returns a retryable error code.'}, {'bugId': 1232339, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In Tap Aggregation mode, packets received with an all zero destination MAC address will be dropped (dropVoqInPortNotVlanMember), instead of forwarded.', 'alertNote': 'In Tap Aggregation mode, packets received with an all zero destination MAC address will be dropped (dropVoqInPortNotVlanMember), instead of forwarded.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1789636234, 'exportedTime': 1786406400, 'releaseNote': 'In Tap Aggregation mode, packets received with an all zero destination MAC address will be dropped (dropVoqInPortNotVlanMember), instead of forwarded.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}, {'tag': 'tapaggEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1232494, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Committing a config session with `configure session FOO commit timer` may cause session to be cleaned up if the system already has the max number of completed sessions and there are enough committed sessions after the last time config session was exited.', 'alertNote': 'Committing a config session FOO with the "configure session FOO commit timer" command may cause the session to be cleaned up if 1) the system already has the maximum number of completed sessions and 2) there are enough committed sessions after the last time config session FOO was exited from.\n\nWhen this happens, "show configuration session" will show "Session with pending commit timer: FOO" but FOO does not appear in the session list. Many config session operations may fail due to "another session FOO is pending commit timer".\n\nTo work around this issue, use "commit timer" inside the config session. \n\nConfiguring “service configuration session max completed <N>” with a higher N (default 1) will make this bug less likely to trigger.\n\nTo recover from the error state, do the following from enable mode:\n\nIn 4.33.0 and earlier releases:\n\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/status\' ].commitTimerSessionName=\'\' " | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/status\'].commitTimerExpireTime" = Tac.endOfTime | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\n\nIn 4.33.1 and later releases:\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/state\' ].commitTimerSessionName=\'\' " | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/status\'].commitTimerExpireTime" = Tac.endOfTime | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.8', '4.33.5', '4.34.1FX-R4.2', '4.34.1FX-R4.3', '4.34.3', '4.35.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1785487549, 'exportedTime': 1767657600, 'releaseNote': 'Committing a config session FOO with the "configure session FOO commit timer" command may cause the session to be cleaned up if 1) the system already has the maximum number of completed sessions and 2) there are enough committed sessions after the last time config session FOO was exited from.\n\nWhen this happens, "show configuration session" will show "Session with pending commit timer: FOO" but FOO does not appear in the session list. Many config session operations may fail due to "another session FOO is pending commit timer".\n\nTo work around this issue, use "commit timer" inside the config session. \n\nConfiguring “service configuration session max completed <N>” with a higher N (default 1) will make this bug less likely to trigger.\n\nTo recover from the error state, do the following from enable mode:\n\nIn 4.33.0 and earlier releases:\n\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/status\' ].commitTimerSessionName=\'\' " | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/status\'].commitTimerExpireTime" = Tac.endOfTime | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\n\nIn 4.33.1 and later releases:\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/state\' ].commitTimerSessionName=\'\' " | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\nbash echo "_.entity[ \'ar/Sysdb/cli/session/status\'].commitTimerExpireTime" = Tac.endOfTime | python3 -m Acons Sysdb\n'}, {'bugId': 1233033, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In case dockerfile used to create the image does not have the COMMAND instruction, then variations of the show commands "show container-manager containers" can lead to an internal error. The only workaround is deploying image with the COMMAND instruction.', 'alertNote': 'In case the dockerfile used to create the image doesn\'t have the COMMAND instruction, then variations of the show commands "show container-manager containers ..." can lead to an internal error. The only workaround for this would be to deploy an image with the COMMAND instruction. (https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#cmd)', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.8', '4.33.5', '4.34.3', '4.35.0'], 'bites': 