ns\n3) login again and reconfigure the server group\n4) immediately type "quit" or "logout" or "exit" without running any other commands\n5) re-enable TACACS+ accounting if needed\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.23.9', '4.24.6', '4.25.4', '4.26.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.6', '4.35.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1753996238, 'exportedTime': 1774656000, 'releaseNote': 'When both TACACS+ authentication and command authorization are enabled, adding new members or reordering existing members in a server group may continue to use an old server for the next hour even for new login sessions. Note for existing login sessions they are expected to continue to use the old server.\n\nThe workaround is to either wait for an hour, or perform the following steps to let the new membership take effect immediately for new login sessions:\n1) disable TACACS+ accounting if it\'s enabled\n2) kill all existing login sessions\n3) login again and reconfigure the server group\n4) immediately type "quit" or "logout" or "exit" without running any other commands\n5) re-enable TACACS+ accounting if needed\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'TACACSenabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1249432, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may stop streaming due to a header overflow error.', 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may stop streaming due to a header overflow error. The workaround is to restart TerminAttr.', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.40.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.40.3', 'TerminAttr-v1.41.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1770750663, 'exportedTime': 1786492800, 'releaseNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may stop streaming due to a header overflow error. The workaround is to restart TerminAttr.'}, {'bugId': 1249522, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A Single Event Upset (SEU) on the L3_DEFIP_ALPM_LEVEL2_ECC table may not be corrected. This m