tyAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If /mnt/flash/.managed-config/L1OpenConfig.json file is present on the standby supervisor, the ConfigAgent on the standby can continuously restart unexpectedly.', 'alertNote': 'If /mnt/flash/.managed-config/L1OpenConfig.json file is present on the standby supervisor, the ConfigAgent on the standby can continuously restart unexpectedly.\nAs a workaround, delete the  /mnt/flash/.managed-config/L1OpenConfig.json file on the standby supervisor.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.1FX-wbb', '4.34.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.2FX-wbb.3', '4.34.2FX-wbb.4', '4.34.5', '4.35.0FX-wbb', '4.35.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1763501301, 'exportedTime': 1780358400, 'releaseNote': 'If /mnt/flash/.managed-config/L1OpenConfig.json file is present on the standby supervisor, the ConfigAgent on the standby can continuously restart unexpectedly.\nAs a workaround, delete the  /mnt/flash/.managed-config/L1OpenConfig.json file on the standby supervisor.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'modular'}]]}, {'bugId': 1338974, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When the Bgp agent is going through a hitful restart, e.g. after a cold reboot, all configured aggregates will not be generated if none of the BGP peering sessions comes up.', 'alertNote': "When the Bgp agent is going through a hitful restart, e.g. after a cold reboot, all configured aggregates will not be generated if none of the BGP peering sessions comes up.\n\nTo work around the issue, either remove all BGP peers in the VRF or make sure there is at least one established peer after the restart. Alternatively, in releases with a fix for this issue, configure 'bgp aggregate-route wait-for-convergence disabled' under the router bgp config mode to change this behavior.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.5', '4.35.3', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1764028219, 'exportedTime': 1785801600, 'releaseNote': 