 restart unexpectedly and continously after it has processed\nat least one VLAN configured with address locking and that VLAN has at least\none member port that is not configured for IP Locking for the same address\nfamily.\n\nAs a workaround, run "address-family ipv4" and "address-family ipv6" for every\nEthernet port that is a member of a VLAN configured with IPv4 or IPv6 address\nlocking respectively and then remove address locking configuration from all the\nVLANs', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.10', '4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.3', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1772679799, 'exportedTime': 1778716800, 'releaseNote': 'IpLocking agent may restart unexpectedly and continously after it has processed\nat least one VLAN configured with address locking and that VLAN has at least\none member port that is not configured for IP Locking for the same address\nfamily.\n\nAs a workaround, run "address-family ipv4" and "address-family ipv6" for every\nEthernet port that is a member of a VLAN configured with IPv4 or IPv6 address\nlocking respectively and then remove address locking configuration from all the\nVLANs', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'IPv4AddrLockingApplied'}], [{'tag': 'IPv6AddrLockingApplied'}]]}, {'bugId': 1391318, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Non-root users cannot login to the switch if the root filesystem is out of space. To recover, login as root if possible, or power cycle the switch.', 'alertNote': 'Non-root users cannot login to the switch if the root filesystem is out of space. To recover, login as root if possible, or power cycle the switch.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.5', '4.35.3', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1787951508, 'exportedTime': 1782777600, 'releaseNote': 'Non-root users cannot login to the switch if the root filesystem is out of space. To recover, login as root if possible, or power cycle the switch.'}, {'bugId': 1391707, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Isis agent might restart when `show tech-support extended isis` command is executed.', 'alertNote': "Isis agent might restart when 'show tech-support extended isis' command is executed.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.35.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.4', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1792828419, 'exportedTime': 1779840000, 'releaseNote': "Isis agent might restart when 'show tech-support extended isis' command is executed.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'isisEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1392364, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "If 'ip hardware fib optimize prefix-length 32' (or VRF equivalent) is configured and SandL3Unicast restarts during route changes, stale optimized /32 routes may persist in the hardware forwarding table, potentially disrupting forwarding to those prefixes.", 'alertNote': 'When FIB optimization for /32 or /24 prefix lengths is enabled via the "ip\nhardware fib optimize" command, a SandL3Unicast restart during route changes\ncan leave stale routes in the hardware forwarding table, potentially disrupting\ntraffic to those prefixes.\n\nThe recommended recovery procedure is to perform a hitful restart of the\nSandL3Unicast, using the following sequence of steps:\nbash touch /mnt/flash/disable_hitless_restart\nagent SandL3Unicast terminate\nwait-for-warmup SandL3Unicast\nbash rm /mnt/flash/disable_hitless_restart\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.36.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1788134400, 'releaseNote': 'When FIB optimization for /32 or /24 prefix lengths is enabled via the "ip\nhardware fib optimize" command, a SandL3Unicast restart during route changes\ncan leave stale routes in the hardware forwarding table, potentially disrupting\ntraffic to those prefixes.\n\nThe recommended recovery procedure is to perform a hitful restart of the\nSandL3Unicast, using the following sequence of steps:\nbash touch /mnt/flash/disable_hitless_restart\nagent SandL3Unicast terminate\nwait-for-warmup SandL3Unicast\nbash rm /mnt/flash/disable_hitless_restart\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'internetProfile'}, {'tag': 'Jericho2'}]]}, {'bugId': 1393536, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A short AC input power loss glitch can cause the system to enter a stuck power state where it must be manually power cycled.', 'alertNote': 'A short  AC input power loss glitch can cause the system to enter a stuck power state where it must be manually power cycled.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.6', '4.36.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1784195579, 'exportedTime': 1788134400, 'releaseNote': 'A short  AC input power loss glitch can cause the system to enter a stuck power state where it must be manually power cycled.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': '7289R3A-SC'}], [{'tag': '7289R3AK-SC'}], [{'tag': '7289R3AM-SC'}]]}, {'bugId': 1394610, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In a VXLAN deployment, if the MAC address used to reach a remote VTEP becomes unreachable, the StrataL3Unicast agent can restart unexpectedly, causing a brief disruption to traffic.', 'alertNote': 'In a VXLAN deployment, if the MAC address used to reach a remote VTEP becomes unreachable, the StrataL3Unicast agent can restart unexpectedly, causing a brief disruption to traffic.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.34.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.7', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1785801600, 'releaseNote': 'In a VXLAN deployment, if the MAC address used to reach a remote VTEP becomes unreachable, the StrataL3Unicast agent can restart unexpectedly, causing a brief disruption to traffic.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7050X4'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}], [{'tag': '7358'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1396360, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Addressless forwarding on an interface may not work after the interface is moved to a different VRF. The workaround is to disable and re-enable `ip routing ipv6 interface`.', 'alertNote': 'Addressless forwarding on an interface may not work after the interface is moved to a different VRF. The workaround is to disable and re-enable "ip routing ipv6 interface".', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.9', '4.34.5', '4.35.4', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1768890345, 'exportedTime': 1785456000, 'releaseNote': 'Addressless forwarding on an interface may not work after the interface is moved to a different VRF. The workaround is to disable and re-enable "ip routing ipv6 interface".', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ipv6RoutingEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'ipv6Routing-NonDefaultVrf'}]]}, {'bugId': 1396926, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'During periods of next hop group churn combined with routing table changes, the forwarding agent can restart unexpectedly.', 'alertNote': 'During periods of next hop group churn combined with routing table changes, the forwarding agent can restart unexpectedly.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.8', '4.34.2.2', '4.34.6', '4.35.4', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1768636833, 'exportedTime': 1785801600, 'releaseNote': 'During periods of next hop group churn combined with routing table changes, the forwarding agent can restart unexpectedly.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'NexthopGroupConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1397835, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'A DCI gateway configured in an MLAG pair, and using the multi-VTEP MLAG feature, will only advertise its shared VTEP IP in an IMET route, not its unique VTEP IP. ', 'alertNote': 'A DCI gateway configured in an MLAG pair, and using the multi-VTEP MLAG feature, will only advertise its shared VTEP IP in an IMET route, not its unique VTEP IP.  This will cause any other VTEPs in the topology to be unable to properly classify the domain of the unique VTEP IPs of the DCI gateways, as domain classification is only done using IMET routes.  This will further prevent the proper flow of L2 bridging traffic between DCI domains, as without proper domain classification of unique VTEP IPs, DCI split horizon rules will block any inter-domain traffic destined to the unique VTEP IPs.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.6', '4.35.3', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1769113944, 'exportedTime': 1780099200, 'releaseNote': 'A DCI gateway configured in an MLAG pair, and using the multi-VTEP MLAG feature, will only advertise its shared VTEP IP in an IMET route, not its unique VTEP IP.  This will cause any other VTEPs in the topology to be unable to properly classify the domain of the unique VTEP IPs of the DCI gateways, as domain classification is only done using IMET routes.  This will further prevent the proper flow of L2 bridging traffic between DCI domains, as without proper domain classification of unique VTEP IPs, DCI split horizon rules will block any inter-domain traffic destined to the unique VTEP IPs.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'MultiVtepMlag'}]]}, {'bugId': 1400607, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When PoE `reboot action maintain` is configured and a CPU lockup happens, the system may become stuck and will not automatically recover. Removing and restoring input power is required for the system to operate correctly.', 'alertNote': 'When PoE `reboot action maintain` is configured and a CPU lockup happens, the system may become stuck and will not automatically recover. Removing and restoring input power is required for the system to operate correctly.\n\nWorkaround is to remove the `reboot action maintain` configuration from the