Note': 'The forwarding agent may unexpectedly restart due to an index overflow. This will lead to the forwarding agent hitless restart with no interface flaps and a minimal traffic disruption.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 16, 'lastBiteTime': 1793352084, 'exportedTime': 1783555200, 'releaseNote': 'The forwarding agent may unexpectedly restart due to an index overflow. This will lead to the forwarding agent hitless restart with no interface flaps and a minimal traffic disruption.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Strata'}]]}, {'bugId': 1400733, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'On card initialisation, a card may stay powered down and will remain down until a power-cycle is initiated Workaround is to remove and re- insert the card or run `platform module LinecardX power-cycle`', 'alertNote': 'On card initialisation, a card may stay powered down and will remain down until a power-cycle is initiated\n\nWorkaround is to remove and re-insert the card or run "platform module LinecardX power-cycle"', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.11', '4.34.9', '4.35.7', '4.36.nofixyet', '4.37.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1793491200, 'releaseNote': 'On card initialisation, a card may stay powered down and will remain down until a power-cycle is initiated\n\nWorkaround is to remove and re-insert the card or run "platform module LinecardX power-cycle"', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CCS-750'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7800R3'}], [{'tag': '7388'}], [{'tag': '7368'}], [{'tag': '7358'}]]}, {'bugId': 1400746, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If an agent restarts and then a switchover occurs shortly afterward, an affected linecard may become powered off indefinitely. Workaround is to remove and re-insert the card.', 'alertNote': 'If an agent restarts and then a switchover occurs shortly afterward, an affected linecard may become powered off indefinitely.\n\nWorkaround is to remove and re-insert the card.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.11', '4.33.9', '4.34.7', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1782864000, 'releaseNote': 'If an agent restarts and then a switchover occurs shortly afterward, an affected linecard may become powered off indefinitely.\n\nWorkaround is to remove and re-insert the card.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CCS-750'}]]}, {'bugId': 1402722, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': ' In Tap Aggregation mode, Traffic Policies with Identity Tagging or MAC Replacement actions may not apply correctly after a reload or mode toggle, especially with many match rules. The issue is self-correcting — no manual intervention needed.', 'alertNote': 'In Tap Aggregation mode, a Traffic Policy with Identity Tagging actions or MAC Replacement actions may not apply these actions correctly following a switch reload, or if the Tap Aggregation mode is toggled. The problem can be more pronounced when the Traffic Policy has a large number of matches.\n\nThe switch will apply the correct actions eventually; no corrective action is required.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.36.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1755007310, 'exportedTime': 1788134400, 'releaseNote': 'In Tap Aggregation mode, a Traffic Policy with Identity Tagging actions or MAC Replacement actions may not apply these actions correctly following a switch reload, or if the Tap Aggregation mode is toggled. The problem can be more pronounced when the Traffic Policy has a large number of matches.\n\nThe switch will apply the correct actions eventually; no corrective action is required.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}, {'tag': 'tapaggEnabled'}, {'tag': 'TrafficPolicyInput'}]]}, {'bugId': 1403969, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'After a 2-bit ECC error is corrected on a TCAM bank, subsequent new 2-bit ECC errors on the same bank will not be detected and corrected.', 'alertNote': 'After a 2-bit ECC error is corrected on a TCAM bank, subsequent new 2-bit ECC errors on the same bank will not be detected and corrected.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.35.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1775520000, 'releaseNote': 'After a 2-bit ECC error is corrected on a TCAM bank, subsequent new 2-bit ECC errors on the same bank will not be detected and corrected.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen5'}]]}, {'bugId': 1405924, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If a 10G/25G speed is configured on a /1 interface while its /2-4 interfaces are shutdown, the adjacent QSFP100 port may stop receiving and transmitting traffic on any L1 configuration on the /1 interface, even if the link remains up on both ports. ', 'alertNote': "If a 10G or 25G speed is configured on a /1 interface while its subordinate /2-4 interfaces are shutdown, the adjacent QSFP100 port may stop receiving and transmitting traffic on any L1 configuration on the /1 interface, even if the link remains up on both ports.\n\nChange the subordinate port's speed to a different value and then change it back to the original setting. Alternatively, remove and re-insert the transceiver in the subordinate port.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.8', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1776808239, 'exportedTime': 1785456000, 'releaseNote': "If a 10G or 25G speed is configured on a /1 interface while its subordinate /2-4 interfaces are shutdown, the adjacent QSFP100 port may stop receiving and transmitting traffic on any L1 configuration on the /1 interface, even if the link remains up on both ports.\n\nChange the subordinate port's speed to a different value and then change it back to the original setting. Alternatively, remove and re-insert the transceiver in the subordinate port.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 1406483, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'OpenConfig subscriptions with subpaths may consume more CPU than their top-level paths. For example, a subscription for the `/components` path may consume less CPU than many specific paths under `/components`.', 'alertNote': 'OpenConfig subscriptions with subpaths may consume more CPU than their top-level paths.\nFor example, a subscription for the "/components" path may consume less CPU than many specific paths under "/components".', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.6', '4.35.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1768557729, 'exportedTime': 1791417600, 'releaseNote': 'OpenConfig subscriptions with subpaths may consume more CPU than their top-level paths.\nFor example, a subscription for the "/components" path may consume less CPU than many specific paths under "/components".', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'gNMIEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1411494, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Issuing a CLI command that contains the `slot X/Y` token within a short time after LinecardX has been inserted, then the command might produce an `Invalid input` error message in all subsequent commands.Refer to bug portal for fix.', 'alertNote': 'Issuing a CLI command that contains the "slot X/Y" token within a short time after LinecardX has been inserted, then the command might produce an "Invalid input" error message in all subsequent commands. Such affected commands are "show transceiver status [slot X/Y] firmware update" and "show transceiver status [slot X/Y] firmware version".\n\nIssuing show command without specifying the "slot" token will correctly display the information for all transceiver slots. For example: "show transceiver status firmware version".\nRestarting ConfigAgent using "agent ConfigAgent terminate" will allow all affected commands to function correctly again.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.6', '4.36.3', '4.37.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1780916522, 'exportedTime': 1793145600, 'releaseNote': 'Issuing a CLI command that contains the "slot X/Y" token within a short time after LinecardX has been inserted, then the command might produce an "Invalid input" error message in all subsequent commands. Such affected commands are "show transceiver status [slot X/Y] firmware update" and "show transceiver status [slot X/Y] firmware version".\n\nIssuing show command without specifying the "slot" token will correctly display the information for all transceiver slots. For example: "show transceiver status firmware version".\nRestarting ConfigAgent using "agent ConfigAgent terminate" will allow all affected commands to function correctly again.'}, {'bugId': 1413619, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'After a prior user-initiated chip reset via CLI command, issuing a config-replace will trigger another chip reset potentially resulting in transient packet loss.', 'alertNote': 'After a prior user-initiated chip reset via CLI command, issuing a config-replace will trigger another chip reset potentially resulting in transient packet loss.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.11', '4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1768042171, 'exportedTime': 1784764800, 'releaseNote': 'After a prior user-initiated chip reset via CLI command, issuing a config-replace will trigger another chip reset potentially resulting in transient packet loss.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}, {'tag': 'SandGen3'}, {'tag': 'SandGen4'}]]}, {'bugId': 1414455, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Changing the peer group for a peer in a non-default VRF may cause the peer to flap when the peer group is being used for the first time within the VRF', 'alertNote': "Changing the peer group for a peer in a non-default VRF may cause the peer to flap when the peer group is being used for the first time within the VRF.\nWorkarounds\n- Don't use a new peer group, use the existing peer group used by the peer.\n- Define a dummy peer in the non-default VRF which uses the new peer group first. Then update the in-use peer.\n- Define the new peer group as an ancestor of existing peer group and put the new settings only in the new peer group. This only applies if the affected attributes aren't already being set in the existing peer group.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.9', '4.34.7', '4.35.5', '4.36.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1769782485, 'exportedTime': 1785974400, 'releaseNote': "Changing the peer group for a peer in a non-default VRF may cause the peer to flap when the peer group is being used for the first time within the VRF.\nWorkarounds\n- Don't use a new peer group, use the existing peer group used by the peer.\n- Define a dummy peer in the non-default VRF which uses the new peer group first. Then update the in-use peer.\n- Define the new peer group as an ancestor of existing peer group and put the new settings only in the new peer group. This only applies if the affected attributes aren't already being set in the existing peer group.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'BGPPeerGroups'}, {'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1415140, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'In EVPN-VXLAN IRB setups using EVPN Multihoming (MH), the VLAN interfaces configured with `ipv6 address virtual` could go into duplicate address failure state. The workaround is to configure `no autostate` or `ipv6 nd dad disabled` for the VLAN interface.', 'alertNote': 'In EVPN-VXLAN IRB setups using  EVPN Multihoming (MH), the VLAN interfaces configured with "ipv6 address virtual" could go into duplicate address failure state.  \nThe workaround is to configure "no autostate" or "ipv6 nd dad disabled" for the VLAN interface.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.8', '4.34.7', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1781106877, 'exportedTime': 1779753600, 'releaseNote': 'In EVPN-VXLAN IRB setups using  EVPN Multihoming (MH), the VLAN interfaces configured with "ipv6 address virtual" could go into duplicate address failure state.  \nThe workaround is to configure "no autostate" or "ipv6 nd dad disabled" for the VLAN interface.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpn-multihoming-enabled'}, {'tag': 'Ipv6Interface'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1418413, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'StrataL3Unicast crash may be seen during VXLAN overlay and underlay route updates.', 'alertNote': 'StrataL3Unicast crash may be seen during VXLAN overlay and underlay route updates.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.30.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.11', '4.33.8', '4.34.2'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1773821435, 'exportedTime': 1775606400, 'releaseNote': 'StrataL3Unicast crash may be seen during VXLAN overlay and underlay route updates.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7050X4'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7358'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1418434, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When changing VXLAN configuration from EVPN to static flood VTEPs, remote MAC addresses may not be learned from data plane packets over VXLAN tunnels. Workaround: Flap the VXLAN interface.', 'alertNote': 'When changing VXLAN configuration from EVPN to static flood VTEPs, remote MAC addresses may not be learned from data plane packets over VXLAN tunnels.\nWorkaround: Flap the VXLAN interface.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.7', '4.36.3', '4.37.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1793491200, 'releaseNote': 'When changing VXLAN configuration from EVPN to static flood VTEPs, remote MAC addresses may not be learned from data plane packets over VXLAN tunnels.\nWorkaround: Flap the VXLAN interface.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'evpnVxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1420898, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If the storage model is one of `VTDU31PI008G-ARI`, `VTDU31PC008G-ARI` or `Virtium_TuffDrive`, `show system health storage` will show `Health Status` as `FAILED`. Refer to software bug portal for alternate commands', 'alertNote': 'If the storage model is one of "VTDU31PI008G-ARI", "VTDU31PC008G-ARI" or "Virtium_TuffDrive", "show system health storage" will show "Health Status" as "FAILED". \n\nUse the following command to find the health status:\nbash sudo smartctl -HA -d scsi --offlineauto=on /dev/sda', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.27.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.9', '4.34.8', '4.35.6', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1775003798, 'exportedTime': 1793318400, 'releaseNote': 'If the storage model is one of "VTDU31PI008G-ARI", "VTDU31PC008G-ARI" or "Virtium_TuffDrive", "show system health storage" will show "Health Status" as "FAILED". \n\nUse the following command to find the health status:\nbash sudo smartctl -HA -d scsi --offlineauto=on /dev/sda', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7250QX-64'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7260QX-64'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7516-SUP2'}], [{'tag': 'MontaraCpu'}]]}, {'bugId': 1423951, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Removing a shared, VFP-installed ACL from an Ethernet/LAG with multiple ACL types (IPv4, IPv6, MAC) may cause traffic drops on other interfaces using that same ACL', 'alertNote': 'When an Ethernet or LAG interface has multiple ACL types (IPv4, IPv6, MAC) applied to it, and at least one of these ACLs is installed in VFP with it having other interfaces attached to it, then removing that ACL from the interface (e.g., shutting the interface or detaching the VFP ACL) may cause traffic drop on other interfaces associated with the same ACL.\n\nOn encountering the issue you can follow the steps of restoring the original configuration by either,\n1. un-shutting the interface or,\n2. re-attaching the ACL to the interface or,\n3. recreating the ACL.\n\nTo workaround this issue, run the configuration command "hardware access-list update default-result permit", this will permit all traffic during ACL updates. Alternatively, disable VFP before configuring ACLs using "platform trident tcam port-acl vfp disabled" to prevent the issue (this reduces the ACL scale on the switch).', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.6', '4.34.4', '4.35.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.9', '4.34.7', '4.35.5', '4.36.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1771020069, 'exportedTime': 1786579200, 'releaseNote': 'When an Ethernet or LAG interface has multiple ACL types (IPv4, IPv6, MAC) applied to it, and at least one of these ACLs is installed in VFP with it having other interfaces attached to it, then removing that ACL from the interface (e.g., shutting the interface or detaching the VFP ACL) may cause traffic drop on other interfaces associated with the same ACL.\n\nOn encountering the issue you can follow the steps of restoring the original configuration by either,\n1. un-shutting the interface or,\n2. re-attaching the ACL to the interface or,\n3. recreating the ACL.\n\nTo workaround this issue, run the configuration command "hardware access-list update default-result permit", this will permit all traffic during ACL updates. Alternatively, disable VFP before configuring ACLs using "platform trident tcam port-acl vfp disabled" to prevent the issue (this reduces the ACL scale on the switch).', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'IPv4ACLApplied'}, {'tag': 'Strata'}], [{'tag': 'Ipv6ACLApplied'}, {'tag': 'Strata'}]]}, {'bugId': 1424096, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When `connector interface patch bgp vpws standby errdisable` on an EVPN Multihoming Interface, port-channel may continuously transition from errdisable to active state. Workaround is to remove LACP config from associated EVPN ethernet-segment interfaces.', 'alertNote': 'When "connector interface patch bgp vpws standby errdisable" on an EVPN Multihoming Interface, the port channel may continuously transition from errdisable to active state.\nWorkaround is to remove LACP configuration from associated EVPN ethernet-segment interfaces.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.35.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.36.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1785974400, 'releaseNote': 'When "connector interface patch bgp vpws standby errdisable" on an EVPN Multihoming Interface, the port channel may continuously transition from errdisable to active state.\nWorkaround is to remove LACP configuration from associated EVPN ethernet-segment interfaces.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'EvpnVpwsEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1424656, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "When an interface traffic-policy with a 'redirect next-hop NEXTHOPS vrf VRF' action is applied to interfaces in multiple VRFs, unapplying the policy from all interfaces in one VRF may cause the action to not take effect for interfaces in other VRFs.", 'alertNote': 'When an interface traffic-policy with a "redirect next-hop NEXTHOPS vrf VRF" action is applied to interfaces in multiple VRFs, unapplying the policy from all interfaces in one VRF may cause the action to not take effect for interfaces in other VRFs.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.35.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1788134400, 'releaseNote': 'When an interface traffic-policy with a "redirect next-hop NEXTHOPS vrf VRF" action is applied to interfaces in multiple VRFs, unapplying the policy from all interfaces in one VRF may cause the action to not take effect for interfaces in other VRFs.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen5'}, {'tag': 'TrafficPolicyInput'}, {'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1424667, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When a traffic-policy or PBR policy with a redirect next-hop action is applied to interfaces in multiple VRFs, traffic on these interfaces may be incorrectly redirected', 'alertNote': 'When a traffic-policy or PBR policy with a "redirect next-hop" action is applied to interfaces in multiple VRFs, traffic on these interfaces may be incorrectly redirected.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.35.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1787027250, 'exportedTime': 1793664000, 'releaseNote': 'When a traffic-policy or PBR policy with a "redirect next-hop" action is applied to interfaces in multiple VRFs, traffic on these interfaces may be incorrectly redirected.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'PBRconfigured'}, {'tag': 'SandGen5'}]]}, {'bugId': 1425334, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may send historical log lines with a current timestamp.', 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may send historical log lines with a current timestamp.', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.28.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.45.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1784160000, 'releaseNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may send historical log lines with a current timestamp.'}, {'bugId': 1425396, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When reconfiguring an interface`s VRF and IP address in a config session, `show session-config diffs` may show a duplicate line of IP address without indentation. This is only a cosmetic issue.', 'alertNote': 'When reconfiguring an interface\'s VRF and IP address in a config session, "show session-config diffs" may show a duplicate line of IP address without indentation. This is only a cosmetic issue.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.34.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.6', '4.35.4', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1771391348, 'exportedTime': 1775779200, 'releaseNote': 'When reconfiguring an interface\'s VRF and IP address in a config session, "show session-config diffs" may show a duplicate line of IP address without indentation. This is only a cosmetic issue.'}, {'bugId': 1426370, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If SSO is triggered while a hardware ( e.g. Linecard, XCVR module, etc. ) insertion or removal is still being processed by EOS then the switchover may fail causing the supervisor to reboot.', 'alertNote': 'If SSO is triggered while a hardware ( e.g. Linecard, XCVR module, etc. ) insertion or removal is still being processed by EOS then the switchover may fail causing the supervisor to reboot.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.29.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.10', '4.34.8', '4.35.6', '4.36.2'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1788134400, 'releaseNote': 'If SSO is triggered while a hardware ( e.g. Linecard, XCVR module, etc. ) insertion or removal is still being processed by EOS then the switchover may fail causing the supervisor to reboot.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'CCS-755-CH'}, {'tag': 'ssoEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'CCS-758-CH'}, {'tag': 'ssoEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7808-CH'}, {'tag': 'ssoEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7816-CH'}, {'tag': 'ssoEnabled'}], [{'tag': 'DCS-7816L-CH'}, {'tag': 'ssoEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1429343, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Using a 4-octet local-as with a 2-octet global ASN on a peer lacking 4-octet capability crashes the BGP agent when advertising local aggregate routes. Attribute encoding conflicts trigger daemon memory faults, causing unexpected restarts and outages.', 'alertNote': 'If BGP is configured with a 2-octet ASN, and the "neighbor <address> local-as <ASN>" command is used to configure a 4-octet local ASN for a BGP peer that has not explicitly negotiated the Four-octet ASN capability, the Bgp agent may restart unexpectedly when attempting to advertise a locally originated aggregate route to that peer.\n\nTo work around this issue, configure the remote BGP peer to explicitly advertise the Four-octet ASN capability, or configure a 2-octet local-as ASN when peering with the remote peer, or avoid advertising locally originated aggregate routes to the peer.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.24.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.11', '4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.4', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1771593242, 'exportedTime': 1784764800, 'releaseNote': 'If BGP is configured with a 2-octet ASN, and the "neighbor <address> local-as <ASN>" command is used to configure a 4-octet local ASN for a BGP peer that has not explicitly negotiated the Four-octet ASN capability, the Bgp agent may restart unexpectedly when attempting to advertise a locally originated aggregate route to that peer.\n\nTo work around this issue, configure the remote BGP peer to explicitly advertise the Four-octet ASN capability, or configure a 2-octet local-as ASN when peering with the remote peer, or avoid advertising locally originated aggregate routes to the peer.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ArBgp'}, {'tag': 'bgpEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1429610, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'ConfigAgent may end up in a bad state when it can no longer query user name or user ID (getpwnam and getpwuid). Restarting ConfigAgent recovers the error state.', 'alertNote': 'ConfigAgent may end up in a bad state when it can no longer query user name or user ID (getpwnam and getpwuid). Restarting ConfigAgent recovers the error state.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 4, 'lastBiteTime': 1790801536, 'exportedTime': 1793318400, 'releaseNote': 'ConfigAgent may end up in a bad state when it can no longer query user name or user ID (getpwnam and getpwuid). Restarting ConfigAgent recovers the error state.'}, {'bugId': 1430413, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'An affected linecard may fail to power on if an FPGA has a corrupted image. When this happens the following system logs may be seen: %HARDWARE-3-CARD_LOST_POWER and %HARDWARE-3-CARD_UNSTABLE_SHUTDOWN.', 'alertNote': 'An affected linecard may fail to power on if an FPGA has a corrupted image. When this happens the following system logs may be seen: %HARDWARE-3-CARD_LOST_POWER and %HARDWARE-3-CARD_UNSTABLE_SHUTDOWN.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.35.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.3', '4.36.nofixyet', '4.37.nofixyet'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1782864000, 'releaseNote': 'An affected linecard may fail to power on if an FPGA has a corrupted image. When this happens the following system logs may be seen: %HARDWARE-3-CARD_LOST_POWER and %HARDWARE-3-CARD_UNSTABLE_SHUTDOWN.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7800R3ALCs'}]]}, {'bugId': 1432541, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If the VRRP master learns the VRRP virtual MAC from a remote VTEP, the MLAG backup switch can incorrectly program the VRRP virtual MAC as learned via the VXLAN tunnel instead of via the MLAG peer link, causing intermittent packet loss.', 'alertNote': 'In a VXLAN MLAG deployment with VRRP, if the VRRP master learns the VRRP virtual MAC from a remote VTEP, the MLAG backup switch can incorrectly program the VRRP virtual MAC as learned via the VXLAN tunnel instead of via the MLAG peer link, causing intermittent packet loss.\n\nPerform a VRRP failover and failback to restore correct MAC programming.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.9', '4.34.8', '4.35.6', '4.36.2'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1769735423, 'exportedTime': 1786579200, 'releaseNote': 'In a VXLAN MLAG deployment with VRRP, if the VRRP master learns the VRRP virtual MAC from a remote VTEP, the MLAG backup switch can incorrectly program the VRRP virtual MAC as learned via the VXLAN tunnel instead of via the MLAG peer link, causing intermittent packet loss.\n\nPerform a VRRP failover and failback to restore correct MAC programming.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}, {'tag': 'Strata'}, {'tag': 'VRRPEnabled'}, {'tag': 'vxlanEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1433825, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If BMP Loc-Rib monitoring is enabled by configuring `export-policy bgp rib bestpaths` under `monitoring station` mode, BMP agent could unexpectedly restart during periods of BGP churn when multiple paths on the same route were updated simultaneously.', 'alertNote': 'If BMP Loc-Rib monitoring is enabled by configuring "export-policy bgp rib bestpaths" under "monitoring station" mode, BMP agent could unexpectedly restart during periods of BGP churn when multiple paths on the same route were updated simultaneously.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.31.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1778526025, 'exportedTime': 1784764800, 'releaseNote': 'If BMP Loc-Rib monitoring is enabled by configuring "export-policy bgp rib bestpaths" under "monitoring station" mode, BMP agent could unexpectedly restart during periods of BGP churn when multiple paths on the same route were updated simultaneously.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'BMPenabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1434358, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "Atomic gNMI notifications may be sent with the 'atomic' flag not set. This can happen when a gNMI client exerts backpressure on the gNMI server and multiple updates to a single atomic object happen before the backlog is relieved.", 'alertNote': "Atomic gNMI notifications may be sent with the 'atomic' flag not set. This can happen when a gNMI client exerts backpressure on the gNMI server and multiple updates to a single atomic object happen before the backlog is relieved.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.34.0', '4.34.2FX-wbb'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.2FX-wbb.4', '4.35.4', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1772097000, 'exportedTime': 1788134400, 'releaseNote': "Atomic gNMI notifications may be sent with the 'atomic' flag not set. This can happen when a gNMI client exerts backpressure on the gNMI server and multiple updates to a single atomic object happen before the backlog is relieved.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'gNMIEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1445043, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'After prolonged VRF and route churn, the L3 forwarding agent may become stuck consuming high CPU.', 'alertNote': 'After prolonged VRF and route churn, the L3 forwarding agent may become stuck consuming high CPU.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.28.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.11', '4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.3', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1765594755, 'exportedTime': 1778457600, 'releaseNote': 'After prolonged VRF and route churn, the L3 forwarding agent may become stuck consuming high CPU.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'DCS-7170-64C'}, {'tag': 'vrfConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1447045, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If `write memory` command is executed during system bootup before the platform agent has fully initialized, the `ip hardware fib optimize` and `ipv6 hardware fib optimize` configurations can be silently omitted from startup-config and permanently lost.', 'alertNote': 'If "write memory" command is executed during system bootup before the platform agent has fully initialized, the "ip hardware fib optimize" and "ipv6 hardware fib optimize" configurations can be silently omitted from startup-config and permanently lost.\n\nWorkaround: Re-apply the lost configuration manually and execute "write memory" command again after the system has fully booted.\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.11', '4.33.8', '4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1771942246, 'exportedTime': 1780099200, 'releaseNote': 'If "write memory" command is executed during system bootup before the platform agent has fully initialized, the "ip hardware fib optimize" and "ipv6 hardware fib optimize" configurations can be silently omitted from startup-config and permanently lost.\n\nWorkaround: Re-apply the lost configuration manually and execute "write memory" command again after the system has fully booted.\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'SandGen4'}], [{'tag': 'SandGen3'}]]}, {'bugId': 1448569, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If only one MLAG peer is upgraded to a release that supports STP priority in MLAG config-sanity, while the other remains on an older release, the MLAG agent restarts.Note: also recommended to run the same EOS version for both peers.', 'alertNote': 'When only one peer is upgraded from old releases to newer releases that support STP priority in MLAG config-sanity, and the other is kept in the old version for a longer time, then MLAG agent restarts itself. \n\nWorkaround: Upgrading the peers one by one within a shorter interval. \nNote: It is also recommended to run the same EOS version for both peers.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.32.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.9', '4.34.7', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 5, 'lastBiteTime': 1793244030, 'exportedTime': 1782777600, 'releaseNote': 'When only one peer is upgraded from old releases to newer releases that support STP priority in MLAG config-sanity, and the other is kept in the old version for a longer time, then MLAG agent restarts itself. \n\nWorkaround: Upgrading the peers one by one within a shorter interval. \nNote: It is also recommended to run the same EOS version for both peers.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'mlagEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1448721, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'The Dot1x agent may unexpectedly send multiple EAP Identity-Requests which may cause the device to stop its EAPoL functionalities.', 'alertNote': 'The Dot1x agent may unexpectedly send multiple EAP Identity-Requests which may cause the device to stop its EAPoL functionalities.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.22.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.33.9', '4.34.6', '4.35.5', '4.36.1'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1774024061, 'exportedTime': 1782864000, 'releaseNote': 'The Dot1x agent may unexpectedly send multiple EAP Identity-Requests which may cause the device to stop its EAPoL functionalities.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'dot1xConfigured'}]]}, {'bugId': 1448766, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Under some very rare upgrade or system reload scenarios the SandCounter agent may restart repeatedly and unexpectedly.', 'alertNote': 'Under some very rare upgrade or system reload scenarios the SandCounter agent may restart repeatedly and unexpectedly.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.30.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.34.7', '4.35.5', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1774040384, 'exportedTime': 1784332800, 'releaseNote': 'Under some very rare upgrade or system reload scenarios the SandCounter agent may restart repeatedly and unexpectedly.', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Sand'}]]}, {'bugId': 1450552, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may remove the NTP configuration from the running config and incorrectly set the device time when the device time falls outside of the validity period for the CloudVision certificate stored on the device.', 'alertNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may remove the NTP configuration from the running config and incorrectly set the device time when the device time falls outside of the validity period for the CloudVision certificate stored on the device.   \n\nThe workaround is to add -monitor_cluster=false to the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) configuration.', 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.39.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.40.15', 'TerminAttr-v1.43.11', 'TerminAttr-v1.46.0'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1784845795, 'exportedTime': 1792454400, 'releaseNote': 'Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) may remove the NTP configuration from the running config and incorrectly set the device time when the device time falls outside of the validity period for the CloudVision certificate stored on the device.   \n\nThe workaround is to add -monitor_cluster=false to the Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) configuration.'}, {'bugId': 1450613, 'severity': 'sev3', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When flash: is in read-only state due to filesystem error, the reload CLI gives internal error. A workaround is to run `bash reboot` instead.', 'alertNote': 'When flash: is in read-only state due to filesystem error, the reload CLI gives internal error. A workaround is to run "bash reboot" instead.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.1'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.7', '4.36.3', '4.37.nofixyet'], 'bites': 2, 'lastBiteTime': 1786228185, 'exportedTime': 1792108800, 'releaseNote': 'When flash: is in read-only state due to filesystem error, the reload CLI gives internal error. A workaround is to run "bash reboot" instead.'}, {'bugId': 1452469, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'If auto-negotiation fails on RJ45 ports, ZeroTouch may try forced 10/100M speeds. This can trigger peer parallel detection, causing a duplex mismatch, lower bandwidth, and provisioning timeouts', 'alertNote': "On RJ45 ports (both Ethernet and Management), ZeroTouch may periodically try non-negotiated 10M or 100M speed configurations, if the ports are unable to successfully bring up the link using auto-negotiation. This may trigger parallel detect on the peer, which would force the link up in a duplex mismatched state at a lower speed and may result in bandwidth/timeout issues while provisioning.\n\nOne workaround is to force the peer's advertisements to 1G only. This will prevent provisioning attempts while linked up at the non-negotiated speeds and will force ZeroTouch to cycle back to auto-negotiation more quickly. Another workaround is to modify the bootstrap script to configure the bootstrap interface to the desired configuration while the provisioning is ongoing.", 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.36.1'], 'bites': 1, 'lastBiteTime': 1777064610, 'exportedTime': 1785196800, 'releaseNote': "On RJ45 ports (both Ethernet and Management), ZeroTouch may periodically try non-negotiated 10M or 100M speed configurations, if the ports are unable to successfully bring up the link using auto-negotiation. This may trigger parallel detect on the peer, which would force the link up in a duplex mismatched state at a lower speed and may result in bandwidth/timeout issues while provisioning.\n\nOne workaround is to force the peer's advertisements to 1G only. This will prevent provisioning attempts while linked up at the non-negotiated speeds and will force ZeroTouch to cycle back to auto-negotiation more quickly. Another workaround is to modify the bootstrap script to configure the bootstrap interface to the desired configuration while the provisioning is ongoing.", 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'ZTPEnabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1454311, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': "Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) with fips enabled can start silently with FIPS mode OFF, or crash when the EOS version doesn't meet the requirement.", 'alertNote': "Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) with fips enabled can start silently with FIPS mode OFF, or crash when the EOS version doesn't meet the requirement.", 'product': 'terminattr', 'versionIntroduced': ['TerminAttr-v1.42.0'], 'versionFixed': ['TerminAttr-v1.43.2', 'TerminAttr-v1.44.1', 'TerminAttr-v1.45.0'], 'bites': 0, 'lastBiteTime': 0, 'exportedTime': 1784160000, 'releaseNote': "Streaming Agent (TerminAttr) with fips enabled can start silently with FIPS mode OFF, or crash when the EOS version doesn't meet the requirement."}, {'bugId': 1455531, 'severity': 'sev2', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'DSCP markings for control plane packets may not work after reload. Packets for RADIUS, TACACS, SNMP, SSH, sFlow, NTP, DNS, Syslog and Traceroute will be affected.', 'alertNote': 'DSCP markings for control plane packets may not work after reload. Packets for RADIUS, TACACS, SNMP, SSH, sFlow, NTP, DNS, Syslog and Traceroute will be affected. \nThe workaround is to manually configure the jump rule after reload using bash command "sudo iptables -t mangle -A EOS_OUTPUT -j EOS_ARISTA_DSCP_AGENT"\n', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['1.0.0'], 'versionFixed': ['4.35.6', '4.36.0'], 'bites': 3, 'lastBiteTime': 1783040578, 'exportedTime': 1788134400, 'releaseNote': 'DSCP markings for control plane packets may not work after reload. Packets for RADIUS, TACACS, SNMP, SSH, sFlow, NTP, DNS, Syslog and Traceroute will be affected. \nThe workaround is to manually configure the jump rule after reload using bash command "sudo iptables -t mangle -A EOS_OUTPUT -j EOS_ARISTA_DSCP_AGENT"\n', 'conjunction': [[{'tag': 'Radius'}, {'tag': 'SflowEnabled'}, {'tag': 'SNMPenabled'}, {'tag': 'TACACSenabled'}]]}, {'bugId': 1469300, 'severity': 'sev1', 'securityAdvisoryURL': '', 'cve': '', 'alertSummary': 'When software multicast forwarding is set to `sfe`, initial multicast traffic may be dropped. Subsequent multicast traffic may be forwarded by the hardware if the route exists.', 'alertNote': 'When software multicast forwarding is set to "sfe", initial multicast traffic may be dropped. Subsequent multicast traffic may be forwarded by the hardware if the route exists.', 'product': 'eos', 'versionIntroduced': ['4.33.2'], 'versionFixed': ['4.32.1